{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CX1VfS2DWFRJE2mnB7hqXx","type":"tool_result","content":"310\t- `assets?: AssetReader`: How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`.\n311\t\n312\t### class LoadingScreen\n313\t\n314\tMinimal pixel-styled loading indicator: a blocky segmented bar and a status word,\n315\tplain DOM (it shows before the renderer exists). Reuses a `.pixel-loading` element\n316\talready in the container (index.html ships one so it appears before any JS runs).\n317\t\n318\t- `new LoadingScreen(container: HTMLElement, segments = 12)`\n319\t- `readonly root: HTMLElement`\n320\t- `set(progress: number, label?: string): void`: `progress` 0..1; `label` is shown in capitals.\n321\t- `done(): void`\n322\t\n323\t### loadSettings()\n324\t\n325\t```ts\n326\tfunction loadSettings(key: string): PlayerSettings\n327\t```\n328\t\n329\tThe settings saved under `key` ({} when there are none, or storage is blocked or holds junk).\n330\t\n331\t### normalizeSettings()\n332\t\n333\t```ts\n334\tfunction normalizeSettings(raw: unknown): PlayerSettings\n335\t```\n336\t\n337\tKeep only fields with a valid value: what storage or a caller handed over may be anything.\n338\t\n339\t### optionsFromUrl()\n340\t\n341\t```ts\n342\tfunction optionsFromUrl(search = location.search): Partial<EngineOptions>\n343\t```\n344\t\n345\tRead engine options from the URL:\n346\t  ?mode=raw  ?res=320  ?debug=1|0\n347\t  ?aspect=fixed|adaptive  ?fps=30 (0 = uncapped)  ?quality=low|medium|high|auto\n348\t  ?camera=iso|topdown|side|third|first|free|fixed  ?zoom=1.5\n349\t  ?cam=<JSON CameraConfig>   (e.g. the config printed by the free camera)\n350\t  ?filters=crt,lcd  or  ?look=handheld (a LOOK_PRESETS name, e.g. pixel_heroes)\n351\t\n352\t### PIXEL_SIZES\n353\t\n354\t```ts\n355\tconst PIXEL_SIZES: readonly [\"fine\", \"chunky\"]\n356\t```\n357\t\n358\t### interface PlayerSettings\n359\t\n360\tThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n361\t(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\n362\tchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\n363\tthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n364\t\n365\t- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n366\t- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n367\t- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n368\t- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n369\t- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n370\t- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n371\t\n372\t### QUALITY\n373\t\n374\t```ts\n375\tconst QUALITY: Readonly<Record<QualityLevel, QualitySettings>>\n376\t```\n377\t\n378\tAt the iso preset's default zoom the shadow box spans ~30 world units, i.e. ~600 art\n379\tpixels: 512² is about one shadow texel per art pixel, 1024² is finer than the art can show.\n380\t\n381\t### QUALITY_LEVELS\n382\t\n383\t```ts\n384\tconst QUALITY_LEVELS: readonly QualityLevel[]\n385\t```\n386\t\n387\t### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n388\t\n389\t```ts\n390\tconst QUALITY_OPTIONS: readonly QualityOption[]\n391\t```\n392\t\n393\t### type QualityLevel\n394\t\n395\t```ts\n396\ttype QualityLevel = 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'\n397\t```\n398\t\n399\tRender quality presets. Pure data + decisions (no DOM, no three.js): unit-tested.\n400\t\n401\tThe pixel pipeline is cheap by design (the scene and every art-pixel filter render at\n402\tthe art resolution), so quality trades the shadow map size and the number of dynamic\n403\tpoint lights (`ctx.lights`, render/lights.ts). `auto` picks `low` on\n404\tphones/tablets and `medium` elsewhere, then lowers it once if the first seconds of play\n405\trun well below the frame-rate target.\n406\t\n407\t### type QualityOption\n408\t\n409\t```ts\n410\ttype QualityOption = QualityLevel | 'auto'\n411\t```\n412\t\n413\t### interface QualitySettings\n414\t\n415\t- `readonly shadowMapSize: number`: Directional-light shadow map size (texels per side).\n416\t- `readonly lights: number`: Real point lights in the dynamic light pool (`ctx.lights`); constant per level.\n417\t\n418\t### rebindDebugKeys()\n419\t\n420\t```ts\n421\tfunction rebindDebugKeys(keys: DebugKeyMap, changes: DebugKeyChanges): DebugKeyMap\n422\t```\n423\t\n424\tRebind the hotkeys that are on and leave the ones that are off off: what a game with its own\n425\tuse for a key does at runtime (`engine.debugKeys = rebindDebugKeys(engine.debugKeys, {\n426\tresolution: 'F7' })`), so a shipped game, which has no hotkeys, gets none back.\n427\t\n428\t### interface Resolution\n429\t\n430\tPure layout math for pixel-perfect presentation. No DOM, no three.js: unit-tested.\n431\t\n432\tThe canvas backing store is sized to `art × scale` device pixels with an integer\n433\t`scale`, and the scene renders at exactly the art resolution (pixelSize = scale). Every\n434\tart pixel therefore covers an integer block of device pixels, and the canvas is centered\n435\tinside the viewport. Fixed/adaptive framing letterboxes; fill framing crops only the\n436\texcess device pixels at the edges of the last art pixel.\n437\t\n438\tThree aspect modes:\n439\t- `fixed`: the art resolution is exactly `internal` (16:9); other screen shapes letterbox.\n440\t- `adaptive`: the art *height* stays `internal.height` and the art width follows the\n441\t  screen's aspect…\n442\t\n443\t- `readonly width: number`\n444\t- `readonly height: number`\n445\t\n446\t### RESOLUTIONS\n447\t\n448\t```ts\n449\tconst RESOLUTIONS: { readonly default: { readonly width: 480; readonly height: 270; }; readonly compare: { readonly width: 320; readonly height: 180; }; }\n450\t```\n451\t\n452\t### resolveDebugKeys()\n453\t\n454\t```ts\n455\tfunction resolveDebugKeys(option?: DebugKeysOption): DebugKeyMap\n456\t```\n457\t\n458\tThe key map an option gives: none for `false` or nothing, the defaults for `true`, the defaults with an object's changes.\n459\t\n460\t### class Settings\n461\t\n462\t`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\n463\tsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\n464\tsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\n465\tsettings panel.\n466\t\n467\t- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n468\t- `readonly key: string | null`\n469\t- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n470\t- `get isOpen: boolean`\n471\t- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n472\t- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n473\t- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n474\t- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n475\t- `open(): void`\n476\t- `close(): void`\n477\t- `toggle(): void`\n478\t\n479\t### interface SettingsHost\n480\t\n481\tWhat the settings change in the engine (Engine implements it; tests pass a fake).\n482\t\n483\t- `readonly look: Look`\n484\t- `setLook(look: Look): void`\n485\t- `readonly renderer: { readonly mode: RenderMode; readonly baseResolution: Resolution; readonly lookVersion: number; setMode(mode: RenderMode): void; setResolution(resolution: Reso…`\n486\t- `maxFps: number`\n487\t- `readonly qualityOption: QualityOption`\n488\t- `useQuality(option: QualityOption): void`\n489\t- `readonly debugShown: boolean`\n490\t- `showDebug(on: boolean): void`\n491\t\n492\t### class SettingsPanel\n493\t\n494\tThe settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n495\t⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\n496\tsettings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\n497\tpressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n498\t\n499\t- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n500\t- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n501\t- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`\n502\t- `show(): void`: Show the panel with the engine's current values. The panel takes the focus, not a control: a game key pressed out of habit (D, Space) must not pick an option; Tab reaches the controls.\n503\t- `hide(): void`\n504\t- `sync(): void`: Put the engine's current values into the controls, and into the debug panel (the loop fills it only while the game runs).\n505\t- `dispose(): void`\n506\t\n507\t### storeSettings()\n508\t\n509\t```ts\n510\tfunction storeSettings(key: string, settings: PlayerSettings): void\n511\t```\n512\t\n513\t### urlSettings()\n514\t\n515\t```ts\n516\tfunction urlSettings(url: UrlFlags, options: UrlFlags = url): Set<keyof PlayerSettings>\n517\t```\n518\t\n519\tThe settings a page URL's review flags set (`?look=`, `?filters=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`,\n520\t`?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`): the fields `url` (optionsFromUrl) holds that the game's\n521\t`options` took (`withUrlOptions`). They win over the saved ones at start.\n522\t\n523\t### interface Viewport\n524\t\n525\tA page's viewport: its size in CSS pixels and the device pixel ratio (a recording keeps it: `Recording.view`).\n526\t\n527\t- `readonly width: number`\n528\t- `readonly height: number`\n529\t- `readonly dpr: number`\n530\t\n531\t### withUrlOptions()\n532\t\n533\t```ts\n534\tfunction withUrlOptions(options: EngineOptions, search = location.search): EngineOptions\n535\t```\n536\t\n537\tA game's own options with the review flags from the page URL (optionsFromUrl) on top:\n538\t`Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ container, camera: { preset: 'side', zoom: 1.2 } }))`.\n539\tThe camera is merged key by key (`?zoom=1.5` keeps the game's `side` preset), and\n540\t`?filters=` replaces the game's look (a look would win over filters otherwise).\n541\t\n542\t## 2. Camera\n543\t\n544\t### CAMERA_PRESETS\n545\t\n546\t```ts\n547\tconst CAMERA_PRESETS: readonly CameraPreset[]\n548\t```\n549\t\n550\t### interface CameraConfig\n551\t\n552\t- `preset?: CameraPreset`\n553\t- `zoom?: number`: Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`.\n554\t- `minZoom?: number`\n555\t- `maxZoom?: number`\n556\t- `viewHeight?: number`: Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1.\n557\t- `pitch?: number`: iso: degrees below horizon / around Y.\n558\t- `yaw?: number`\n559\t- `fov?: number`: Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees.\n560\t- `distance?: number`: third: orbit distance at zoom 1.\n561\t- `position?: [number, number, number]`: fixed: camera position and look-at target.\n562\t- `target?: [number, number, number]`\n563\t- `projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho'`: fixed/free: projection.\n564\t- `stiffness?: number`: Follow smoothing; higher is snappier.\n565\t\n566\t### type CameraPreset\n567\t\n568\t```ts\n569\ttype CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed'\n570\t```\n571\t\n572\tCamera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\n573\treviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\n574\tis an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\n575\t`fixed` config into your game.\n576\t\n577\t### class CameraRig\n578\t\n579\tBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n580\t\n581\t- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n582\t- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n583\t- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n584\t- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n585\t- `zoom: number`\n586\t- `readonly minZoom: number`\n587\t- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n588\t- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n589\t- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n590\t- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n591\t- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n592\t- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n593\t- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n594\t- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n595\t- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n596\t- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n597\t- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n598\t- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n599\t- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n600\t- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n601\t- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n602\t- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n603\t\n604\t### interface CameraRigState\n605\t\n606\tWhere a rig is and looks, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): the frame after a restore sees the camera the frame after the snapshot did.\n607\t\n608\t- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n609\t- `readonly focus: readonly number[]`\n610\t- `readonly zoom: number`\n611\t- `readonly aspect: number`\n612\t- `readonly position: readonly number[]`\n613\t- `readonly quaternion: readonly number[]`\n614\t- `readonly shaken: readonly number[]`\n615\t- `readonly own: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`: What a preset keeps of its own (an orbit's yaw, pitch and distance).\n616\t\n617\t### createCameraRig()\n618\t\n619\t```ts\n620\tfunction createCameraRig(config: CameraConfig = {}): CameraRig\n621\t```\n622\t\n623\t### class FirstPersonRig\n624\t\n625\tEyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n626\t\n627\t- `new FirstPersonRig(config: CameraConfig = {})`\n628\t- `readonly preset: \"first\"`\n629\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n630\t- `readonly zoomable: false`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n631\t- `readonly hidesTarget: true`: First person hides the player model.\n632\t- `yaw: number`\n633\t- `pitch: number`\n634\t- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3; }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n635\t- `describe(): { yaw: number; pitch: number; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n636\t\n637\t### class FreeRig\n638\t\n639\tAuthoring camera. While flying: WASD move, Q/E down/up, drag (or click to lock) to look,\n640\tShift = fast, wheel = field of view. Press Enter to fix it: the view freezes, the player\n641\tgets control, and `fixedConfig()` returns the config to hard-code (preset 'fixed').\n642\tEnter again unfixes.\n643\t\n644\t- `new FreeRig(preset: 'free' | 'fixed', config: CameraConfig = {})`\n645\t- `readonly preset: 'free' | 'fixed'`\n646\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera | OrthographicCamera`\n647\t- `fixed: boolean`\n648\t- `yaw: number`\n649\t- `pitch: number`\n650\t- `onFix: ((config: CameraConfig) => void) | null`\n651\t- `setFixed(fixed: boolean): void`: Freeze (or unfreeze) the view.\n652\t- `fixedConfig(): CameraConfig`\n653\t- `describe(): { fixed: boolean; config: CameraConfig; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n654\t\n655\t### class OrthoRig\n656\t\n657\tOrthographic presets: classic 3/4 isometric, straight top-down, straight side-on.\n658\t\n659\t- `new OrthoRig(preset: 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side', config: CameraConfig = {})`\n660\t- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera`\n661\t- `readonly preset: 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side'`\n662\t- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n663\t- `readonly baseViewHeight: number`\n664\t- `get viewHeight: number`\n665\t\n666\t### class ThirdPersonRig\n667\t\n668\tOver-the-shoulder orbit camera: mouse-drag or Q/E to orbit, wheel to zoom, avoids walls.\n669\t\n670\t- `new ThirdPersonRig(config: CameraConfig = {})`\n671\t- `readonly preset: \"third\"`\n672\t- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n673\t- `yaw: number`\n674\t- `pitch: number`\n675\t- `describe(): { yaw: number; pitch: number; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n676\t\n677\t## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n678\t\n679\t### AMOUNT"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"3ef74f4e-fff0-4d8f-a7b5-edda95eed4c4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:52.143Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/.research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"- `assets?: AssetReader`: How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`.\n\n### class LoadingScreen\n\nMinimal pixel-styled loading indicator: a blocky segmented bar and a status word,\nplain DOM (it shows before the renderer exists). Reuses a `.pixel-loading` element\nalready in the container (index.html ships one so it appears before any JS runs).\n\n- `new LoadingScreen(container: HTMLElement, segments = 12)`\n- `readonly root: HTMLElement`\n- `set(progress: number, label?: string): void`: `progress` 0..1; `label` is shown in capitals.\n- `done(): void`\n\n### loadSettings()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadSettings(key: string): PlayerSettings\n```\n\nThe settings saved under `key` ({} when there are none, or storage is blocked or holds junk).\n\n### normalizeSettings()\n\n```ts\nfunction normalizeSettings(raw: unknown): PlayerSettings\n```\n\nKeep only fields with a valid value: what storage or a caller handed over may be anything.\n\n### optionsFromUrl()\n\n```ts\nfunction optionsFromUrl(search = location.search): Partial<EngineOptions>\n```\n\nRead engine options from the URL:\n  ?mode=raw  ?res=320  ?debug=1|0\n  ?aspect=fixed|adaptive  ?fps=30 (0 = uncapped)  ?quality=low|medium|high|auto\n  ?camera=iso|topdown|side|third|first|free|fixed  ?zoom=1.5\n  ?cam=<JSON CameraConfig>   (e.g. the config printed by the free camera)\n  ?filters=crt,lcd  or  ?look=handheld (a LOOK_PRESETS name, e.g. pixel_heroes)\n\n### PIXEL_SIZES\n\n```ts\nconst PIXEL_SIZES: readonly [\"fine\", \"chunky\"]\n```\n\n### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n### QUALITY\n\n```ts\nconst QUALITY: Readonly<Record<QualityLevel, QualitySettings>>\n```\n\nAt the iso preset's default zoom the shadow box spans ~30 world units, i.e. ~600 art\npixels: 512² is about one shadow texel per art pixel, 1024² is finer than the art can show.\n\n### QUALITY_LEVELS\n\n```ts\nconst QUALITY_LEVELS: readonly QualityLevel[]\n```\n\n### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n\n```ts\nconst QUALITY_OPTIONS: readonly QualityOption[]\n```\n\n### type QualityLevel\n\n```ts\ntype QualityLevel = 'low' | 'medium' | 'high'\n```\n\nRender quality presets. Pure data + decisions (no DOM, no three.js): unit-tested.\n\nThe pixel pipeline is cheap by design (the scene and every art-pixel filter render at\nthe art resolution), so quality trades the shadow map size and the number of dynamic\npoint lights (`ctx.lights`, render/lights.ts). `auto` picks `low` on\nphones/tablets and `medium` elsewhere, then lowers it once if the first seconds of play\nrun well below the frame-rate target.\n\n### type QualityOption\n\n```ts\ntype QualityOption = QualityLevel | 'auto'\n```\n\n### interface QualitySettings\n\n- `readonly shadowMapSize: number`: Directional-light shadow map size (texels per side).\n- `readonly lights: number`: Real point lights in the dynamic light pool (`ctx.lights`); constant per level.\n\n### rebindDebugKeys()\n\n```ts\nfunction rebindDebugKeys(keys: DebugKeyMap, changes: DebugKeyChanges): DebugKeyMap\n```\n\nRebind the hotkeys that are on and leave the ones that are off off: what a game with its own\nuse for a key does at runtime (`engine.debugKeys = rebindDebugKeys(engine.debugKeys, {\nresolution: 'F7' })`), so a shipped game, which has no hotkeys, gets none back.\n\n### interface Resolution\n\nPure layout math for pixel-perfect presentation. No DOM, no three.js: unit-tested.\n\nThe canvas backing store is sized to `art × scale` device pixels with an integer\n`scale`, and the scene renders at exactly the art resolution (pixelSize = scale). Every\nart pixel therefore covers an integer block of device pixels, and the canvas is centered\ninside the viewport. Fixed/adaptive framing letterboxes; fill framing crops only the\nexcess device pixels at the edges of the last art pixel.\n\nThree aspect modes:\n- `fixed`: the art resolution is exactly `internal` (16:9); other screen shapes letterbox.\n- `adaptive`: the art *height* stays `internal.height` and the art width follows the\n  screen's aspect…\n\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n\n### RESOLUTIONS\n\n```ts\nconst RESOLUTIONS: { readonly default: { readonly width: 480; readonly height: 270; }; readonly compare: { readonly width: 320; readonly height: 180; }; }\n```\n\n### resolveDebugKeys()\n\n```ts\nfunction resolveDebugKeys(option?: DebugKeysOption): DebugKeyMap\n```\n\nThe key map an option gives: none for `false` or nothing, the defaults for `true`, the defaults with an object's changes.\n\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### interface SettingsHost\n\nWhat the settings change in the engine (Engine implements it; tests pass a fake).\n\n- `readonly look: Look`\n- `setLook(look: Look): void`\n- `readonly renderer: { readonly mode: RenderMode; readonly baseResolution: Resolution; readonly lookVersion: number; setMode(mode: RenderMode): void; setResolution(resolution: Reso…`\n- `maxFps: number`\n- `readonly qualityOption: QualityOption`\n- `useQuality(option: QualityOption): void`\n- `readonly debugShown: boolean`\n- `showDebug(on: boolean): void`\n\n### class SettingsPanel\n\nThe settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\n⚙ button that opens it: the player's picture, sound and engine options (`engine.settings`,\nsettings.ts; the AudioManager's volumes). The engine pauses the game while it is open. Keys\npressed in it never reach the game; Escape or Done closes it.\n\n- `new SettingsPanel(engine: Engine, container: HTMLElement, corner: TouchCorner | false)`\n- `readonly root: HTMLDivElement`\n- `readonly button: HTMLButtonElement | null`\n- `show(): void`: Show the panel with the engine's current values. The panel takes the focus, not a control: a game key pressed out of habit (D, Space) must not pick an option; Tab reaches the controls.\n- `hide(): void`\n- `sync(): void`: Put the engine's current values into the controls, and into the debug panel (the loop fills it only while the game runs).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### storeSettings()\n\n```ts\nfunction storeSettings(key: string, settings: PlayerSettings): void\n```\n\n### urlSettings()\n\n```ts\nfunction urlSettings(url: UrlFlags, options: UrlFlags = url): Set<keyof PlayerSettings>\n```\n\nThe settings a page URL's review flags set (`?look=`, `?filters=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`,\n`?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`): the fields `url` (optionsFromUrl) holds that the game's\n`options` took (`withUrlOptions`). They win over the saved ones at start.\n\n### interface Viewport\n\nA page's viewport: its size in CSS pixels and the device pixel ratio (a recording keeps it: `Recording.view`).\n\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n- `readonly dpr: number`\n\n### withUrlOptions()\n\n```ts\nfunction withUrlOptions(options: EngineOptions, search = location.search): EngineOptions\n```\n\nA game's own options with the review flags from the page URL (optionsFromUrl) on top:\n`Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ container, camera: { preset: 'side', zoom: 1.2 } }))`.\nThe camera is merged key by key (`?zoom=1.5` keeps the game's `side` preset), and\n`?filters=` replaces the game's look (a look would win over filters otherwise).\n\n## 2. Camera\n\n### CAMERA_PRESETS\n\n```ts\nconst CAMERA_PRESETS: readonly CameraPreset[]\n```\n\n### interface CameraConfig\n\n- `preset?: CameraPreset`\n- `zoom?: number`: Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`.\n- `minZoom?: number`\n- `maxZoom?: number`\n- `viewHeight?: number`: Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1.\n- `pitch?: number`: iso: degrees below horizon / around Y.\n- `yaw?: number`\n- `fov?: number`: Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees.\n- `distance?: number`: third: orbit distance at zoom 1.\n- `position?: [number, number, number]`: fixed: camera position and look-at target.\n- `target?: [number, number, number]`\n- `projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho'`: fixed/free: projection.\n- `stiffness?: number`: Follow smoothing; higher is snappier.\n\n### type CameraPreset\n\n```ts\ntype CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed'\n```\n\nCamera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\nreviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\nis an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\n`fixed` config into your game.\n\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### interface CameraRigState\n\nWhere a rig is and looks, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): the frame after a restore sees the camera the frame after the snapshot did.\n\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly focus: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly zoom: number`\n- `readonly aspect: number`\n- `readonly position: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly quaternion: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly shaken: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly own: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`: What a preset keeps of its own (an orbit's yaw, pitch and distance).\n\n### createCameraRig()\n\n```ts\nfunction createCameraRig(config: CameraConfig = {}): CameraRig\n```\n\n### class FirstPersonRig\n\nEyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\n\n- `new FirstPersonRig(config: CameraConfig = {})`\n- `readonly preset: \"first\"`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly zoomable: false`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: true`: First person hides the player model.\n- `yaw: number`\n- `pitch: number`\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3; }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `describe(): { yaw: number; pitch: number; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n\n### class FreeRig\n\nAuthoring camera. While flying: WASD move, Q/E down/up, drag (or click to lock) to look,\nShift = fast, wheel = field of view. Press Enter to fix it: the view freezes, the player\ngets control, and `fixedConfig()` returns the config to hard-code (preset 'fixed').\nEnter again unfixes.\n\n- `new FreeRig(preset: 'free' | 'fixed', config: CameraConfig = {})`\n- `readonly preset: 'free' | 'fixed'`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera | OrthographicCamera`\n- `fixed: boolean`\n- `yaw: number`\n- `pitch: number`\n- `onFix: ((config: CameraConfig) => void) | null`\n- `setFixed(fixed: boolean): void`: Freeze (or unfreeze) the view.\n- `fixedConfig(): CameraConfig`\n- `describe(): { fixed: boolean; config: CameraConfig; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n\n### class OrthoRig\n\nOrthographic presets: classic 3/4 isometric, straight top-down, straight side-on.\n\n- `new OrthoRig(preset: 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side', config: CameraConfig = {})`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera`\n- `readonly preset: 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side'`\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `readonly baseViewHeight: number`\n- `get viewHeight: number`\n\n### class ThirdPersonRig\n\nOver-the-shoulder orbit camera: mouse-drag or Q/E to orbit, wheel to zoom, avoids walls.\n\n- `new ThirdPersonRig(config: CameraConfig = {})`\n- `readonly preset: \"third\"`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `yaw: number`\n- `pitch: number`\n- `describe(): { yaw: number; pitch: number; }`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n\n## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n\n### AMOUNT","numLines":370,"startLine":310,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CX1VfS2DWFRJE2mnB7hqXx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
