{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdzUSnQ9xnjpjcxUUNDW83","type":"tool_result","content":"889:### LOOK_PRESETS\n1013:### PALETTES\n1192:### glowMaterial()\n1203:### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n1281:### interface LightRequestOptions\n1319:### PALETTE\n1368:### toonMaterial()\n1380:### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n1417:### class Breakables\n1834:### class Ragdoll\n3094:### interface ModelBuild\n3265:### packTextures()\n3273:### parsePack()\n3366:### setAssetReader()\n3927:### class BehaviorTree\n4027:### class BulletPool\n4114:### DECAL_SHAPES\n4127:### class Decals\n4152:### drawSheet()\n4203:### emitter()\n4323:### groundFog()\n4337:### hashString()\n4353:### class HeadlessView\n4486:### class NavGrid\n4606:### interface Recording\n4651:### class Rng\n4689:### class ScreenFx\n4780:### class SpriteBatch\n4881:### class Timeline\n4922:### class Trail\n5023:### class Tweens\n----\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\n\n## 5. Physics\n----\n### PALETTE\n\n```ts\nconst PALETTE: { readonly ink: 1711148; readonly plum: 6104925; readonly red: 11615827; readonly orange: 15695191; readonly sand: 16764277; readonly lime: 11006064; readonly green: 3716964; readonly teal: 2453881; ... 7 more ...; readonly night: 3357783; }\n```\n\nRestrained 16-color palette (Sweetie 16 by GrafxKid). Every color in a game should come\nfrom here: authentic pixel art reads as \"designed\" because the palette is small.\nKeep in sync with scripts/generate-assets.mjs.\n\n### type PaletteColor\n\n```ts\ntype PaletteColor = keyof typeof PALETTE\n```\n\n### pixelTexture()\n----\n7:    readonly ink: 1711148;\n8:    readonly plum: 6104925;\nink:1711148,plum:6104925,red:11615827,orange:15695191,sand:16764277,lime:11006064,green:3716964,teal:2453881,navy:2700911,blue:3890633,sky:4302582,cyan:7598071,white:16053492,mist:9744578,slate:5663878,night:3357783\nugrep: error: error at position 1307\nx80-\\xbf])*,(?:[^\\n\\x80-\\xbf][\\x80-\\xbf]*){200}\n                  exceeds complexity limits___/","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"51e8dc4e-0209-4402-8cd8-8cb738353137","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:45.335Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"889:### LOOK_PRESETS\n1013:### PALETTES\n1192:### glowMaterial()\n1203:### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n1281:### interface LightRequestOptions\n1319:### PALETTE\n1368:### toonMaterial()\n1380:### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n1417:### class Breakables\n1834:### class Ragdoll\n3094:### interface ModelBuild\n3265:### packTextures()\n3273:### parsePack()\n3366:### setAssetReader()\n3927:### class BehaviorTree\n4027:### class BulletPool\n4114:### DECAL_SHAPES\n4127:### class Decals\n4152:### drawSheet()\n4203:### emitter()\n4323:### groundFog()\n4337:### hashString()\n4353:### class HeadlessView\n4486:### class NavGrid\n4606:### interface Recording\n4651:### class Rng\n4689:### class ScreenFx\n4780:### class SpriteBatch\n4881:### class Timeline\n4922:### class Trail\n5023:### class Tweens\n----\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\n\n## 5. Physics\n----\n### PALETTE\n\n```ts\nconst PALETTE: { readonly ink: 1711148; readonly plum: 6104925; readonly red: 11615827; readonly orange: 15695191; readonly sand: 16764277; readonly lime: 11006064; readonly green: 3716964; readonly teal: 2453881; ... 7 more ...; readonly night: 3357783; }\n```\n\nRestrained 16-color palette (Sweetie 16 by GrafxKid). Every color in a game should come\nfrom here: authentic pixel art reads as \"designed\" because the palette is small.\nKeep in sync with scripts/generate-assets.mjs.\n\n### type PaletteColor\n\n```ts\ntype PaletteColor = keyof typeof PALETTE\n```\n\n### pixelTexture()\n----\n7:    readonly ink: 1711148;\n8:    readonly plum: 6104925;\nink:1711148,plum:6104925,red:11615827,orange:15695191,sand:16764277,lime:11006064,green:3716964,teal:2453881,navy:2700911,blue:3890633,sky:4302582,cyan:7598071,white:16053492,mist:9744578,slate:5663878,night:3357783\nugrep: error: error at position 1307\nx80-\\xbf])*,(?:[^\\n\\x80-\\xbf][\\x80-\\xbf]*){200}\n                  exceeds complexity limits___/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TdzUSnQ9xnjpjcxUUNDW83","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
