{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBypbgFX8LcHGzDnpzK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8yP7SQBJKNf4K5RSseFvx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work\ncat > .research/spike/fix_plan.py <<'PY'\nimport sys\np = sys.argv[1]\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    if n != 1:\n        print('NOT UNIQUE/FOUND', n, repr(old[:70]))\n        sys.exit(1)\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nrep(\"It lives in one constant, `TITLE` in `src/data/meta.js`, and appears only on the title screen, the session card, About, `<title>` and the engine's game `name`. Story text never mentions it, so the world below works with any title.\",\n    \"It lives in one constant, `TITLE` in `src/data/meta.js`, and appears only in the game's frame: title screen, attract overlay, session card, About, the no-WebGPU page, `<title>`, the engine's game `name` and the save key. Story text never mentions it, so the world below works with any title.\")\n\nrep(\"- `tools/test.mjs` greps `src/` for these names (section 14).\",\n    \"- `tools/test.mjs` greps `src/` for these names as whole words (section 16).\")\n\nrep(\"The result is about 5.3 MB plus your code. Don't minify: the import agent edits strings in this file later.\",\n    \"The result is about 5.3 MB plus your code, with nothing external. Don't minify your own code: the agent that imports the game adds its usage figures to the About screen later, so keep strings findable.\")\n\nrep(\"7. **(verified)** `Engine.headless` works in Node with `buildModel`, `compileClips`, mixers, ragdoll-free play, HUD calls and audio counts. `hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there.\",\n    \"7. **(verified)** `Engine.headless` works in Node with `buildModel`, `compileClips`, mixers, HUD calls and audio counts. `hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. (Ragdolls were only tried in the browser.)\")\n\nrep(\"works on the same body. Template in section 9.\", \"works on the same body. Template in section 8.\")\n\nrep(\"22. **(verified)** `camera: { preset: 'iso', viewHeight: 11.5, pitch: 42, yaw: 45 }` looks right at 1080p: a hero about 25 art pixels tall, with 40 monsters on screen and still readable.\",\n    \"22. **(verified)** `camera: { preset: 'iso', viewHeight: 11.5, pitch: 42, yaw: 45 }` looks right at 1080p: a hero about 25 art pixels tall, with 40 monsters on screen and still readable. A `viewHeight` of 13 still reads, which gives the room to zoom out for co-op.\")\n\nrep(\"It has: `0-9 A-Z . , : ; - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ ! ? < > # ' \\\" ' ' \\\" \\\" * @ ° · & | ~ ^ $` and the backtick. No em dash, no ×, no arrows.\",\n    \"It has digits, A to Z, straight and curly quotes, the backtick and `. , : ; - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ ! ? < > # * @ ° · & | ~ ^ $`. No em dash, no ×, no arrows.\")\n\nrep(\"30. **(verified)** Floor textures at full white are too loud against monsters (`flagstones` especially). Use `toonMaterial(PALETTE.mist, { map })` or `slate` to push floors back; `slate-tiles` and `ashlar` read well. Bright red `Decals` at 1 to 2 m look cartoonish: keep blood `plum` and under 1 m.\",\n    \"30. **(verified)** Floor textures at full white are too loud against monsters. `toonMaterial(PALETTE.mist, { map })` pushes them back and monsters read much better; `flagstones` tinted that way looked best, and `ashlar` is busy, so keep it for walls. Bright red `Decals` at 1 to 2 m look cartoonish; `plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"  aspect: 'fill', quality: 'high', touch: false,\n}));\n```\n\"\"\", \"\"\"  aspect: 'fill', quality: 'high', touch: false,\n}));\n```\n\nAdd `settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }` to that: your own Settings screen replaces the ⚙ everywhere except touch-only devices, where TASK.md asks for it. (Hiding it comes from the docs; I didn't run that option.)\n\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"`arc, circle, cone, ring, projectile, lob, chain, dash, leap, blink, zone, summon, turret, buff, debuff, pull, knock, stun, apply_status, consume_status, consume_graves, comet_rain, delay, repeat, spawn_decoy`\",\n    \"`arc, circle, cone, ring, projectile, lob, chain, dash, leap, blink, zone, obstacle, summon, turret, buff, debuff, pull, knock, stun, apply_status, consume_status, consume_graves, comet_rain, delay, repeat, spawn_decoy`\")\n\nrep(\"- **Pennywhistle:** buy (6 rotating items), sell, and Mystery Caskets (spend Bell Shards, pick a slot, get a random item).\",\n    \"- **Pennywhistle:** buy (6 rotating items), sell, and Mystery Caskets (spend Bell Shards, pick a slot, get a random item). Price target: a Reliquary item costs about 2 minutes of the gold you earn at its level.\")\n\nrep(\"After level 30, XP fills Devotion levels, shared across heroes. Each gives 1 point\",\n    \"After level 30, XP fills Devotion levels, shared across heroes, each costing `15000 + 1500 × n` XP. Each gives 1 point\")\n\nrep(\"| **Bloat Deacon** | Causeway, Ossuary | 2.0 | 0 | 2.0 | Swells 1 s, bursts in 4 m, leaves a poison pool | `Squash` blob |\",\n    \"| **Bloat Deacon** | Causeway, Ossuary | 2.0 | 2.5 (burst only) | 2.0 | Swells 1 s, bursts in 4 m, leaves a poison pool | `Squash` blob |\")\n\nrep(\"Generation: start at the entrance, attach templates at door sockets until the room count is met, end with the exit or boss room, seal unused sockets. Every biome has at least 8 templates plus its boss room. A test checks that `nav.path(entrance, exit)` exists for 200 seeds per zone.\",\n    \"Generation: start at the entrance, attach templates at door sockets until the room count is met, end with the exit or boss room, seal unused sockets. Every biome has at least 8 templates plus its boss room. A test checks that `nav.path(entrance, exit)` exists for 200 seeds per zone.\\n\\nDensity: each `S` marker spawns a pack of 4 to 9 and a room has 2 to 4 markers, so 20 to 40 monsters a room. Each `E` marker has a 1 in 3 chance of an elite pack. All of it scales with the density and elite sliders.\")\n\nrep(\"| **Ossuary of Saint Gloam** | 3 floors, 8 to 12 rooms each | `slate-tiles`, `ashlar`, `sarcophagus`,\",\n    \"| **Ossuary of Saint Gloam** | 3 floors, 8 to 12 rooms each | Floors `flagstones`, walls `ashlar`, `sarcophagus`,\")\nrep(\"| **The Cinder Cloister** | 12 rooms, part open sky | `flagstones`, `cinders`, `lava-crust`, `ruined-wall`,\",\n    \"| **The Cinder Cloister** | 12 rooms, part open sky | Floors `slate-tiles`, `cinders`, `lava-crust`, `ruined-wall`,\")\n\nrep(\"- **Rewards:** guaranteed legendary, Bell Shards, bonus XP, and a chance of a Grand Key.\",\n    \"- **Rewards:** guaranteed legendary, Bell Shards, bonus XP, and a 1 in 4 chance of a Grand Key.\")\n\nrep(\"- Own Settings screen covers what the engine's panel does (through `engine.settings.set`) plus the game's options, so it all works on a pad. The ⚙ stays for mouse and touch.\",\n    \"- Your own Settings screen covers what the engine's panel does (through `engine.settings.set`) plus the game's options, so it all works on a pad. The ⚙ shows only on touch-only devices.\")\n\nrep(\"10. **Settings.** Volumes (Master, Music, Sound, Voices), Glyphs (PlayStation or Xbox), Screen shake, Damage numbers, Zoom, Look (native plus a few presets), Pixel size, Quality, Fullscreen, Reset to defaults (music back to 10%).\",\n    \"10. **Settings.** Volumes (Master, Music, Sound, Voices), Glyphs (PlayStation or Xbox), Screen shake, Damage numbers, Zoom, Look (native plus a few presets), Pixel size, Quality, Fullscreen (catch the promise: browsers may refuse it, and an unhandled rejection fails the hub check), Reset to defaults (music back to 10%).\")\n\nrep(\"**Music is at 10% by default** (section 2 item 27), and a test asserts it.\",\n    \"**Music is at 10% by default** (section 2 item 27), and a test asserts it.\\n\\n**A pad may not unlock sound.** The engine unlocks audio on key, pointer and touch events, not on pad buttons. On the first pad press call `ctx.audio.unlock()`. If `audio.unlocked` stays false, show a small \\\"PRESS A KEY OR CLICK FOR SOUND\\\" on the title. There's no real pad here to prove what a browser does, so handle both.\")\n\nrep(\"Detect as in section 2 item 28. Show the attract mode with \\\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\\\" wrapped to `hud.width` (on a portrait phone that's about 22 characters a line, so break it onto three rows) and the engine's ⚙.\",\n    \"Detect as in section 2 item 28. Show the attract mode with \\\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\\\" wrapped to `hud.width` (a portrait phone fits about 22 characters a line) and the engine's ⚙.\")\n\nrep(\"so engine recordings and fingerprints cover a full playthrough. Use `loadGame` for nothing.\",\n    \"so engine recordings and fingerprints cover a full playthrough. Don't use `loadGame`.\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"docs/DESIGNERS.md       how to add a monster, skill, item, room, zone, quest, song\n```\n\"\"\", \"\"\"docs/DESIGNERS.md       how to add a monster, skill, item, room, zone, quest, song\n```\n\n**The day-to-day loop:** `node tools/build.mjs` (esbuild takes a second), then run the bundle over `file://`. ES modules can't load from `file://`, so `index.html` needs a server; `node check.mjs` brings its own on `127.0.0.1`, port 0. Install everything inside the dev folder.\n\"\"\")\n\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPY\npython3 .research/spike/fix_plan.py \"$PWD/PLAN.md\"\necho \"--- banned leftovers (TASK-specific names, title picks):\"; grep -n \"GameTitle\\|claude-opus\\|20261104\\|exit-interview\\|pixel-engine.zip\\|planner\" PLAN.md || echo none\necho \"--- section refs:\"; grep -n \"section [0-9]\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-110 | head -40\necho \"--- size:\"; wc -l -w PLAN.md","description":"Apply review corrections to the plan and check its references"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"