{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8yP7SQBJKNf4K5RSseFvx","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n--- banned leftovers (TASK-specific names, title picks):\nnone\n--- section refs:\n12:- **Build order is in section 15.** Follow it. The deliverable HTML must build and run from the first miles\n17:- **No stubs.** If you run out of budget, cut whole features in the order given in section 15, never halfwa\n70:- `tools/test.mjs` greps `src/` for these names as whole words (section 16).\n96:12. **(verified)** You can build any humanoid as a `ModelDef` of nested pivots named after `HERO_RIG`'s joi\n171:Lines fit two rows of about 52 characters. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24). Use\n209:**Side content:** the **Drowned Pantry** (optional small cellar off the Causeway, mini-boss the **Cellarer\n237:- **Moving while casting:** the Lamplighter's Spark Bolt and Sexton's Bone Toss play upper-body clips over\n381:**Main hands:** Bellwarden: hand-bell (`mace`), war-bell (`warhammer`), chain flail (`flail`). Lamplighter\n444:All bodies are authored models (section 8). Elite colouring and affix glows are data.\n524:- **Walls:** merged boxes, not thin wall models. **A wall cell whose floor neighbour lies on its +X or +Z \n566:A session is one 8-minute Knell Run for the seated players. Full details in section 12.\n572:**Base:** the engine's native look (`LOOK_PRESETS.none`: 3D low-poly toon rendered as pixel art, Sweetie 1\n608:- **Monsters:** table in section 6. Each has a palette variant for elites and glowing eyes (`glow: true`).\n612:- **HUD icons:** library ones (`whirlwind-icon`, `leap-icon`, `fireball-icon`, `summon-icon`, `curse-icon`\n614:- **Loot beams:** as in section 2 item 29. Items lie on the floor with a small label, always visible for R\n628:**Checks:** `validateClip` on every clip in tests; `analyzeClip` on `Shamble` and any new gait (section 2 \n638:- **Layout comes from `hud.width` and `hud.height`** (sec