{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X2be3fsUUnhk17hBpiLWrk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Game plan: a gothic action RPG for the TV, inspired by Diablo 3\n2\t\n3\t**Genre:** co-op action RPG (hack-and-slash loot game). **Camera:** fixed 3/4 isometric, orthographic.\n4\t**Players:** 1 to 4, on one screen or in AI Hub sessions. **Engine:** the Pixel Engine kit (0.46.0 when this was written).\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## 0. How to use this plan\n9\t\n10\t- TASK.md is the CEO's brief and wins over this plan. This plan decides everything TASK.md leaves open, so you can build without asking.\n11\t- Read in this order: this plan, then the kit's `GUIDE.md` and `ASSETS.md` whole, then the hub's `README.md` whole. Search `API.md` and `LIBRARY.md`; don't read them whole.\n12\t- **Build order is in section 15.** Follow it. The deliverable HTML must build and run from the first milestone on, and every milestone leaves the game playable.\n13\t- Lines marked **(verified)** were run on this computer against engine 0.46.0 in a throwaway build. Trust them. If your kit is newer, read its `CHANGELOG.md` first.\n14\t- Numbers are starting values. Anything about balance lives in one table (`src/data/tuning.js`) and shows up as a dev-mode slider.\n15\t- No more source research is needed. Section 1 says what to take from the source.\n16\t- All paths are relative to your dev folder. The deliverable's name and location, the exit interview file and the title rule all come from your TASK.md.\n17\t- Other agents share this computer. Follow TASK.md's sharing rules: stay out of the folders beside yours, keep every file inside your own folder, and stop only processes you started, by PID.\n18\t- **No stubs.** If you run out of budget, cut whole features in the order given in section 15, never halfway. A feature that isn't there is fine; a menu item that does nothing is not.\n19\t\n20\t### The title\n21\t\n22\tPick it as TASK.md says. Make it a pun that reads as its own name, not the source's name with a letter changed. It lives in one constant, `TITLE` in `src/data/meta.js`, and appears only in the game's frame: title screen, attract overlay, session card, About, the no-WebGPU page, `<title>`, the engine's game `name` and the save key. Story text never mentions it, so the world below works with any title.\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 1. The game\n27\t\n28\t### Pitch\n29\t\n30\tForty days ago the great bell that kept the dead asleep cracked. It still tolls every dusk, but now it says *get up*, and everything buried does. You got up too, except that you kept your wits. Pick a trade (swing a holy bell on a chain, hurl lanterns, or bury your problems with a shovel), smash hordes that burst apart, chase loot that rings like church bells, and climb the broken tower to silence the walled-up saint who has been screaming at you the whole way. Alone, on a couch, or online.\n31\t\n32\t### Pillars (when in doubt, these decide)\n33\t\n34\t1. **Every button press breaks something.** Hits have weight: flash, shake, knockback, ragdolls, shattered props. Hordes are the point.\n35\t2. **Loot you can hear.** Rarity is a colour, a beam and a sound. Legendary drops ring a bell. Good items change how skills work, not only the numbers.\n36\t3. **Builds are play styles.** Six slots, eight skills per class, three variations of each. Swapping is free and instant, so experimenting costs nothing.\n37\t4. **Gothic melodrama with a straight face and a black joke.** Villains proclaim. Townsfolk shrug. Nobody winks at the camera.\n38\t5. **A TV game.** Big, readable, one screen at a time, playable from a sofa with a pad. Mouse and keyboard feel native on the same screens.\n39\t6. **One more run.** After the story, a repeatable run mode with a meter, a boss and rising difficulty.\n40\t\n41\t### What we take from the source, and what we make ours\n42\t\n43\t| What the source does well | Our version |\n44\t|---|---|\n45\t| Hordes that explode, physical destruction | Ragdolls, shatter props, a kill-streak bonus called **Requiem** |\n46\t| Classes with their own resource | **Bellwarden** (Clangor), **Lamplighter** (Wick), **Sexton** (Tithe) |\n47\t| Skills with swappable modifiers | 8 skills per class, each with 3 **Tones** |\n48\t| Passive choices | 4 **Vows** per class, pick 2 |\n49\t| Life pickups that drop in combat | **Tallow**: wax drops that re-melt your life candle |\n50\t| Beams and sounds for great loot | Coloured beams, and a bell strike for every legendary |\n51\t| Elites with random powers | Elite packs with **Afflictions** |\n52\t| The loot creature you chase | **The Collection Plate**: a living offering dish on little legs, spilling coins as it runs |\n53\t| Risky chests | **Unquiet Coffins**: open one, survive 45 seconds, get paid |\n54\t| Temporary shrines | **Votive Shrines** |\n55\t| Repeatable random dungeon with a meter and a boss | **Knell Runs**; the timed version is the **Grand Knell** |\n56\t| Endless levelling | **Devotion** |\n57\t| Difficulty ladder | **Pilgrim, Zealot, Martyr, Penance I to V** |\n58\t| Crafting artisans | **Dame Brasse** the bellfounder, **Mother Ogive** at the Reliquary |\n59\t| Extracting item powers | The **Reliquary** holds three extracted powers |\n60\t| Waypoints, town portal | **Lychgates**, the **Passing Bell** |\n61\t| An AI companion | **Sister Pyx** |\n62\t| Couch and online co-op | Couch co-op on its own, shared-world sessions in AI Hub |\n63\t| A villain who taunts you while you play | **Malison**, in subtitled gibberish |\n64\t\n65\t### Stay original\n66\t\n67\tThis is a new game in the same genre, with its own world, cast, art, music and levels. TASK.md says so and it's a hard rule.\n68\t\n69\t- Never use the source's names or look: Sanctuary, Tristram, Caldeum, Westmarch, Horadrim, Nephalem, Cain, Leah, Adria, Tyrael, Imperius, Malthael, Azmodan, Belial, Kanai, Paragon, Torment, its class names and resource names, its famous lines, its melodies, or a HUD built around two orbs. No fallen star, no amnesiac angel.\n70\t- The source is credited by name only on the About screen and in the exit interview.\n71\t- `tools/test.mjs` greps `src/` for these names as whole words (section 16).\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## 2. Facts verified on this computer\n76\t\n77\tThese save you hours. All were run in a real build here.\n78\t\n79\t**Bundling**\n80\t1. **(verified)** One HTML file boots on `file://` with WebGPU. Bundle with `esbuild game.js --bundle --format=esm --target=es2022 --charset=utf8 --legal-comments=none`, put the result in one inline `<script type=\"module\">`. The engine has no `import.meta` and needs no fetch, so its built-in models and Rapier's wasm work from the file. The result is about 5.3 MB plus your code, with nothing external. Don't minify your own code: the agent that imports the game adds its usage figures to the About screen later, so keep strings findable.\n81\t2. Escape `</script` as `<\\/script` in the bundle. If you insert with `String.replace`, use a function replacer, or `$&` in the code corrupts the file.\n82\t3. **(verified)** Page order that the hub accepts: `<meta charset>`, then `session.js` byte for byte as the first script, then the `hub:*` metas, then `<title>`. Body: `<div id=\"app\"></div>` and the module script.\n83\t4. **(verified)** If you ever need a pack, set `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__['packs/x.json'] = 'data:application/json;base64,...'` in a classic script before the module, then `loadPack('packs/x.json')` works on `file://`. The built-in library is enough for this game, so prefer not to.\n84\t\n85\t**Browsers in tests**\n86\t5. **(verified) Use the kit's flags:** `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` (the list in `check.mjs`). The shorter list in the \"This computer\" notes lost the GPU device within seconds on this engine (`A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`). That error is the flags, not your game.\n87\t6. **(verified)** Software rendering is slow: about 20 fps for a small scene at 1280×720, 3 to 8 fps at 1080p with 40 rigged monsters. So tests advance time with `engine.step(n)` (120 frames took 6 ms in a small scene) and read pixels with `await engine.renderer.capture()` (about 180 ms). Never wait in real time when you can step.\n88\t7. **(verified)** `Engine.headless` works in Node with `buildModel`, `compileClips`, mixers, HUD calls and audio counts. `hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. (Ragdolls were only tried in the browser.) `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys KeyD*30` plays and replays to the same fingerprint. Every module must guard `window`, `document` and `navigator` with `typeof`.\n89\t\n90\t**The hub**\n91\t8. **(verified)** A full engine in the harness's iframes passes: 2 players; 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; the same with `scenario=host-leave`; 2 players with `scenario=server`; and a game-owned card. Copies were ready in 2 to 6.5 seconds.\n92\t9. **(verified)** For `AIHub.server` (a copy with no player) use `Engine.headless(game, {})` inside the iframe and drive it with a timer: ready in 0.6 s, no GPU, harness passes. Step by elapsed time, not a fixed count.\n93\t10. **(verified)** On the game's own card, answer Enter from a plain `window` `keydown` listener, not `wasPressed`. The harness allows 3 seconds and software-rendered frames are slow.\n94\t11. The hub's clocks (from `round.js`): hard limit is `hub:session-minutes` × 1.5, at most 15 minutes; 5 s grace after `time-up`; 3 s countdown; 20 s load grace; 20 s hidden-host limit.\n95\t\n96\t**Characters and animation**\n97\t12. **(verified)** You can build any humanoid as a `ModelDef` of nested pivots named after `HERO_RIG`'s joints, and `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, build.object)` animates it with all 78 hero clips, including `Slash1`, `Slash2`, `Slash3`, `Slam`, `LeapSlam`, `Spin`, `Cast`, `CastBig`, `CastWeapon`, `CastBigWeapon`, `BowDraw`, `BowRelease`, `Roll`, `Charge`, `Shout`, `HitReact`, `Death`, `Triumph`. `new Ragdoll(physics, root, HERO_RAGDOLL)` works on the same body. Template in section 8.\n98\t13. **(verified)** All 15 joints must exist or `compileClips` throws `rig joint \"ForearmR\" not found`. An empty pivot is fine, which keeps cheap monsters cheap (14 meshes against 21).\n99\t14. **(verified)** Compile clips once per body type (63 ms for 78 clips) and share them: `new THREE.AnimationMixer(instance).clipAction(clip)` moves a second instance. `buildModel` is cheap and shares geometry.\n100\t15. **(verified)** Custom clips: `{ name, frames, fast, keys: [[frame, { ArmR: [x, y, z], Pelvis: { p: [x, y, z] } }, 'outCubic'], ...] }` and `gaitClip(HERO_RIG, {...})` compile with `validateClip` clean.\n101\t16. **(verified)** `analyzeClip` throws on merged pivot bodies because its sole meshes are gone. Run it on the engine's own hero inside `Engine.headless`: `const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL)`, same rig, same results. It finds real problems such as `planted foot slides 0.80 m/s`; tune `speed` and `stance` until it's clean.\n102\t17. **(verified)** To attack while running, filter a compiled clip to upper-body tracks: `new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter(t => UPPER.has(t.name.split('.')[0])))` and play it over `Run`. Track names look like `Torso.quaternion`. It ran without error; check how it looks.\n103\t\n104\t**Pause, input, camera, HUD**\n105\t18. **(verified) Pause with `engine.timeScale = 0`.** `update` keeps running with `dt` 0, `fixedUpdate` stops, `wasPressed` still works, so menus work. `engine.paused = true` stops `update` too: never use it for menus. Menu animation counts rendered frames, since `dt` is 0.\n106\t19. `hitstop` and `timeScale` stall the whole simulation. Never use them on a session host. Use them solo and on the couch only.\n107\t20. **(verified)** Use `aspect: 'fill'`. The default letterboxes (at 1280×720 you get 960×540 in the middle). With `fill` the art size changes with the window: 427×240 at 720p, 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 512×288 at 1440p, about 136×276 on a portrait phone. Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height`, never from 480×270.\n108\t21. **(verified)** The `iso` camera with yaw 45 looks toward −X −Z: screen right is (+0.71, 0, −0.71), screen up is (−0.71, 0, −0.71). So a wall on a room's −X or −Z side shows its face to the camera, and a wall on the +X or +Z side blocks the view.\n109\t22. **(verified)** `camera: { preset: 'iso', viewHeight: 11.5, pitch: 42, yaw: 45 }` looks right at 1080p: a hero about 25 art pixels tall, with 40 monsters on screen and still readable. A `viewHeight` of 13 still reads, which gives the room to zoom out for co-op.\n110\t23. **(verified)** The rig zooms on the wheel after `update` runs. Read `ctx.input.wheel` yourself, then set `ctx.input.wheel = 0` to stop it. `setZoom` clamps to `minZoom` and `maxZoom`.\n111\t24. **(verified)** `hud.text` uppercases for you and draws `?` for any character it lacks. It has digits, A to Z, straight and curly quotes, the backtick and `. , : ; - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ ! ? < > # * @ ° · & | ~ ^ $`. No em dash, no ×, no arrows. Text is 6 art pixels per character (minus one) and 7 tall. `hudSprite` icons are about 12×12. A test lints all strings against this set.\n112\t25. **(verified)** The engine's `Input` merges every pad into one, which can't do couch co-op. Set `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = {}` and read `navigator.getGamepads()` yourself, per pad (guard with `typeof`). A stub via `addInitScript` reaches both. The kit's pad mapping is for the platformer and would press Space, KeyJ and so on.\n113\t26. Mouse buttons are keys (`MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`), and the canvas already blocks the context menu. The HUD canvas has `pointer-events: none`, so the pointer reaches the game through it.\n114\t\n115\t**Audio**\n116\t27. **(verified)** Engine defaults are master 0.8, sfx 1, music 0.6, saved under `pixel-engine:audio`, a key shared by every engine game on the same origin. So on first run (your own flag in storage) call `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)`. `audio.resetVolumes()`, which the engine's settings panel calls, puts it back to 0.6, so wrap that method on the instance to re-apply 0.1. That doesn't touch `pixel-engine.js`.\n117\t\n118\t**Touch and look**\n119\t28. **(verified)** Detect touch-only with `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` (true on Chromium's Pixel 7 profile, false on desktop). `touch: false` removes the joystick. The ⚙ button stays visible. WebKit here has no WebGPU, so test touch in Chromium.\n120\t29. **(verified) The mood:** `engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky); engine.sun.intensity = 0.55; engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy); engine.ambient.intensity = 0.9; scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);` plus library torches and a warm light following the hero gives a rich dark dungeon. A tall thin `glowMaterial` box plus a coloured point light on the floor makes a superb loot beam.\n121\t30. **(verified)** Floor textures at full white are too loud against monsters. `toonMaterial(PALETTE.mist, { map })` pushes them back and monsters read much better; `flagstones` tinted that way looked best, and `ashlar` is busy, so keep it for walls. Bright red `Decals` at 1 to 2 m look cartoonish; `plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\n122\t\n123\t**This engine start worked (verified):**\n124\t\n125\t```js\n126\tconst engine = await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({\n127\t  container: document.getElementById('app'),\n128\t  camera: { preset: 'iso', viewHeight: 11.5, pitch: 42, yaw: 45, minZoom: 0.6, maxZoom: 1.4 },\n129\t  aspect: 'fill', quality: 'high', touch: false,\n130\t}));\n131\t```\n132\t\n133\tAdd `settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }` to that **(verified: `false` removes the button)**. Your own Settings screen replaces the ⚙ everywhere except touch-only devices, where TASK.md asks for it.\n134\t\n135\t---\n136\t\n137\t## 3. World, story and tone\n138\t\n139\t### The world\n140\t\n141\t**Vespermoor** is a drowned moorland kingdom under one enormous tower, the **Belfry of Saint Malison**. In it hangs the Great Bell, **Old Clemency**. For a thousand years it tolled at dusk, and the toll told everything below: *stay down*. Forty days ago it cracked. It still tolls. It now says something else.\n142\t\n143\t- **The Risen:** the mindless dead, up and about.\n144\t- **The Unrung:** demons from Below, things no bell was ever rung for. They hate sound, and they've come up through the graves the dead left open.\n145\t- **The Late (formally the Tollborn):** you. You died during the cracked toll, or just after, and got up with your mind intact. Townsfolk find this awkward. They call you *the Late* and ask you to wipe your feet. Death doesn't stick to you, which is why you respawn.\n146\t- **Tollhaven:** the last parish with its lamps lit.\n147\t\n148\t**The truth:** Saint Malison, revered as the foundress who \"gave herself to the bell\", was walled up alive in the tower's foundation by the first bishops, singing. She has heard that bell every dusk for a thousand years. Bishop Ambrose, drowning in debts to a demon called the Bursar, cracked it for her. She wants one thing: to ring the Last Toll, **Eventide**, and wake everything ever buried. The only thing she still fears is the sound of Old Clemency rung true.\n149\t\n150\t### Cast\n151\t\n152\t| Who | Role | Voice and manner |\n153\t|---|---|---|\n154\t| **Crier Maudlin** | Quest giver, reads lore aloud. A severed head in a lantern on a post. Lost the body, kept the job. | High, reedy, unstoppable |\n155\t| **Dame Brasse** | Bellfounder: salvage, craft, reforge. Melts church bells into swords. Half deaf. | LOUD. Everything shouted |\n156\t| **Mother Ogive** | Keeper of the Reliquary: extract powers, sockets. Blind; knows relics by taste. | Soft, delighted, unsettling |\n157\t| **Pennywhistle** | Merchant in a plague-doctor beak. | Cheerful, nasal, modest markups considering the apocalypse |\n158\t| **Sister Pyx** | Companion. Armoured nun with a crossbow. | Deadpan |\n159\t| **Bishop Ambrose Thrice-Buried** | Kindly, pale, keeps a spade in the coffin. The traitor. | Warm, then not |\n160\t| **The Bursar** | Mid-game boss. A bloated demon accountant in a stolen cope. | Booming, delighted by interest |\n161\t| **Malison, the Unrung Saint** | Final boss. Huge entombed saint wrapped in bell ropes. | Vast, layered, furious |\n162\t| **The Narrator** | Opening and ending. | Deep and slow |\n163\t\n164\t### Tone\n165\t\n166\tThree registers, and write everything in one of them:\n167\t\n168\t1. **High gothic proclamation:** narration, lore books, Malison. Long vowels, doom, an ominous last line.\n169\t2. **Gallows humour:** townsfolk, item flavour, death messages. Dry, never modern. No slang, no winks.\n170\t3. **Boss taunts:** direct address, mid-fight, short.\n171\t\n172\tLines fit two rows of about 52 characters. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24). Use these as written and write the rest to match.\n173\t\n174\t**Narrator:** \"For a thousand years Old Clemency tolled at dusk, and the dead of Vespermoor stayed down.\" / \"Forty days ago the Great Bell cracked. It still tolls. It now says something else.\" / \"You were buried on the thirty-ninth day. It did not take.\"\n175\t\n176\t**Crier Maudlin:** \"Hear ye, hear ye! The dead are up, the roads are closed, and the fish is off. Also you. You are dead. Welcome back.\" / \"I lost the body at harvest and kept the job. No one told me to stop.\" / \"The parish asks that you wipe your feet. You have been in the ground.\"\n177\t\n178\t**Dame Brasse:** \"WHAT? SPEAK UP! I MELT BELLS FOR A LIVING!\" / \"THAT SWORD WAS A CHURCH BELL ON TUESDAY. HIT SOMETHING WITH IT AND IT STILL SAYS AMEN.\"\n179\t\n180\t**Mother Ogive:** \"Bring me the holy bones, child. I will know them by the taste.\" / \"A saint's knuckle. Very old. A little salty. She died angry.\"\n181\t\n182\t**Pennywhistle:** \"Everything is half price, dear friend. The other half is your soul, but we can discuss terms.\" / \"No refunds. No returns. No survivors, so far.\"\n183\t\n184\t**Sister Pyx:** \"I have killed four hundred things today and confessed to none of them.\" / \"Bless you. Duck.\" / \"You smell like a grave. It is an improvement on the last one.\"\n185\t\n186\t**Bishop Ambrose:** \"They have buried me three times, my child. One learns to keep a spade in the coffin.\"\n187\t\n188\t**The Bursar:** \"YOUR SOUL IS OVERDUE!\" / \"INTEREST COMPOUNDS, LITTLE CORPSE!\" / \"I HAVE YOU DOWN FOR ONE DEATH. I SEE IT WAS NOT COLLECTED.\" / \"FORECLOSURE!\"\n189\t\n190\t**Malison:** \"A THOUSAND YEARS I HAVE BEEN YOUR FOUNDATION STONE. NOW I SHALL BE YOUR CEILING.\" / \"THEY WALLED ME UP SINGING. DO YOU KNOW WHAT I LEARNED IN THE DARK? EVERY VERSE.\" / \"RUN, LITTLE RINGER. THE HOUR IS UNRUNG, AND IT IS YOURS.\" / \"LISTEN. THAT IS EVERY GRAVE YOU EVER WALKED ON, OPENING.\" / (on a hero's death) \"DOWN YOU GO. GIVE MY REGARDS TO THE WORMS.\"\n191\t\n192\t**Lore book:** \"THE THIRD NIGHT. THE GRAVES IN THE NEW YARD ARE EMPTY. THE GRAVES IN THE OLD YARD ARE EMPTY. I HAVE BEGUN DIGGING ONE FOR MYSELF, FOR THE COMPANY.\"\n193\t\n194\t**System lines:** Death: \"YOU HAVE DIED. AGAIN. IT IS BECOMING A HABIT.\" Level up: \"YOU FEEL MORE ALIVE. THIS IS NOT MEDICALLY POSSIBLE.\" Streak: \"37 KILL REQUIEM\".\n195\t\n196\t**Item flavour:** \"She rang it only once. It was enough.\" / \"The best one is still in him.\" / \"Smells of smoke and regret.\"\n197\t\n198\t### The story, in five quests\n199\t\n200\t| # | Quest | Where | What happens | Unlocks |\n201\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n202\t| 1 | **Wipe Your Feet** | St. Clement's Yard | Your coffin bursts. Tutorial fights. The Crier's voice carries over the wall. Reach Tollhaven. | Town, Pennywhistle, potion |\n203\t| 2 | **The Weeping Causeway** | The Causeway | Find Dame Brasse in a gibbet camp. Defend the wagon of bells on the way back. Sister Pyx joins. | Bellfounder, Lychgates, Pyx |\n204\t| 3 | **Saint Gloam's Bones** | Ossuary, 3 floors | Mother Ogive needs three relic bones. Under the third floor is the Counting House and **the Bursar**, who has a ledger with the Bishop's name in it. | Reliquary, sockets, first legendary guaranteed |\n205\t| 4 | **The Cinder Cloister** | Burning abbey | Rescue the last novices. Malison's voice taunts you openly now. Confront **Bishop Ambrose**, who is buried and bursts out three times. The Crier reads the truth about the saint. | Passing the Belfry gate |\n206\t| 5 | **Ring It or Die Trying** | The Cracked Belfry | Climb the tower. Fight **Malison** beneath the bell. Ring Old Clemency by hand. | Ending, credits, Penance, Knell Runs |\n207\t\n208\t**Ending:** the bell rings true, Malison comes apart, dawn hits the moor. Over the credits, far below, a much deeper bell answers. It's the hook for the rest of the game.\n209\t\n210\t**Side content:** the **Drowned Pantry** (optional small cellar off the Causeway, mini-boss the **Cellarer**, a \"return the overdue book\" joke quest for the Crier); 12 lore books (read aloud, kept in the Codex); **Writs** (section 7).\n211\t\n212\t### The first five minutes\n213\t\n214\t| Time | Beat |\n215\t|---|---|\n216\t| 0:00 | Title, New Hero, pick a class |\n217\t| 0:10 | Narrator over black, a cracked bell toll; 20 seconds, skippable |\n218\t| 0:30 | Night, rain, graveyard. A coffin bursts; hero plays `GetUp`. Prompt: move |\n219\t| 0:40 | Three Peatwalkers. Prompt: attack. They burst. Urns and a barrel shatter, gold rains |\n220\t| 1:30 | Tallow drops, the candle re-melts. A short-beam blue weapon drops. Toast: \"UPGRADE: [glyph] EQUIP\" |\n221\t| 2:30 | Level 2, second skill unlocked, prompt to assign |\n222\t| 3:00 | First telegraph: a red ring grows. Prompt: dodge |\n223\t| 4:00 | An Unquiet Coffin at the gate. 45 seconds of chaos, a chest of gold, level 3 |\n224\t| 5:00 | Tollhaven. \"Hear ye, hear ye!\" |\n225\t\n226\tPacing target: about 60 minutes to the credits for a first player. Tutorial 5, town 3, Causeway 12, Ossuary 15, town 2, Cloister 12, Belfry 8 with Malison, ending 2. A Knell Run takes 6 to 8 minutes.\n227\t\n228\t**New Hero** offers two starts: **The Beginning**, or **The Last Bell**, which is a level 20 hero with a legendary, the town fully open and Knell Runs available, so anyone can see the endgame right away.\n229\t\n230\t---\n231\t\n232\t## 4. Combat\n233\t\n234\t### Rules\n235\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"001bc5fb-6b89-4736-a02f-3efe4ff8ffdf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:03:00.576Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Game plan: a gothic action RPG for the TV, inspired by Diablo 3\n\n**Genre:** co-op action RPG (hack-and-slash loot game). **Camera:** fixed 3/4 isometric, orthographic.\n**Players:** 1 to 4, on one screen or in AI Hub sessions. **Engine:** the Pixel Engine kit (0.46.0 when this was written).\n\n---\n\n## 0. How to use this plan\n\n- TASK.md is the CEO's brief and wins over this plan. This plan decides everything TASK.md leaves open, so you can build without asking.\n- Read in this order: this plan, then the kit's `GUIDE.md` and `ASSETS.md` whole, then the hub's `README.md` whole. Search `API.md` and `LIBRARY.md`; don't read them whole.\n- **Build order is in section 15.** Follow it. The deliverable HTML must build and run from the first milestone on, and every milestone leaves the game playable.\n- Lines marked **(verified)** were run on this computer against engine 0.46.0 in a throwaway build. Trust them. If your kit is newer, read its `CHANGELOG.md` first.\n- Numbers are starting values. Anything about balance lives in one table (`src/data/tuning.js`) and shows up as a dev-mode slider.\n- No more source research is needed. Section 1 says what to take from the source.\n- All paths are relative to your dev folder. The deliverable's name and location, the exit interview file and the title rule all come from your TASK.md.\n- Other agents share this computer. Follow TASK.md's sharing rules: stay out of the folders beside yours, keep every file inside your own folder, and stop only processes you started, by PID.\n- **No stubs.** If you run out of budget, cut whole features in the order given in section 15, never halfway. A feature that isn't there is fine; a menu item that does nothing is not.\n\n### The title\n\nPick it as TASK.md says. Make it a pun that reads as its own name, not the source's name with a letter changed. It lives in one constant, `TITLE` in `src/data/meta.js`, and appears only in the game's frame: title screen, attract overlay, session card, About, the no-WebGPU page, `<title>`, the engine's game `name` and the save key. Story text never mentions it, so the world below works with any title.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game\n\n### Pitch\n\nForty days ago the great bell that kept the dead asleep cracked. It still tolls every dusk, but now it says *get up*, and everything buried does. You got up too, except that you kept your wits. Pick a trade (swing a holy bell on a chain, hurl lanterns, or bury your problems with a shovel), smash hordes that burst apart, chase loot that rings like church bells, and climb the broken tower to silence the walled-up saint who has been screaming at you the whole way. Alone, on a couch, or online.\n\n### Pillars (when in doubt, these decide)\n\n1. **Every button press breaks something.** Hits have weight: flash, shake, knockback, ragdolls, shattered props. Hordes are the point.\n2. **Loot you can hear.** Rarity is a colour, a beam and a sound. Legendary drops ring a bell. Good items change how skills work, not only the numbers.\n3. **Builds are play styles.** Six slots, eight skills per class, three variations of each. Swapping is free and instant, so experimenting costs nothing.\n4. **Gothic melodrama with a straight face and a black joke.** Villains proclaim. Townsfolk shrug. Nobody winks at the camera.\n5. **A TV game.** Big, readable, one screen at a time, playable from a sofa with a pad. Mouse and keyboard feel native on the same screens.\n6. **One more run.** After the story, a repeatable run mode with a meter, a boss and rising difficulty.\n\n### What we take from the source, and what we make ours\n\n| What the source does well | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| Hordes that explode, physical destruction | Ragdolls, shatter props, a kill-streak bonus called **Requiem** |\n| Classes with their own resource | **Bellwarden** (Clangor), **Lamplighter** (Wick), **Sexton** (Tithe) |\n| Skills with swappable modifiers | 8 skills per class, each with 3 **Tones** |\n| Passive choices | 4 **Vows** per class, pick 2 |\n| Life pickups that drop in combat | **Tallow**: wax drops that re-melt your life candle |\n| Beams and sounds for great loot | Coloured beams, and a bell strike for every legendary |\n| Elites with random powers | Elite packs with **Afflictions** |\n| The loot creature you chase | **The Collection Plate**: a living offering dish on little legs, spilling coins as it runs |\n| Risky chests | **Unquiet Coffins**: open one, survive 45 seconds, get paid |\n| Temporary shrines | **Votive Shrines** |\n| Repeatable random dungeon with a meter and a boss | **Knell Runs**; the timed version is the **Grand Knell** |\n| Endless levelling | **Devotion** |\n| Difficulty ladder | **Pilgrim, Zealot, Martyr, Penance I to V** |\n| Crafting artisans | **Dame Brasse** the bellfounder, **Mother Ogive** at the Reliquary |\n| Extracting item powers | The **Reliquary** holds three extracted powers |\n| Waypoints, town portal | **Lychgates**, the **Passing Bell** |\n| An AI companion | **Sister Pyx** |\n| Couch and online co-op | Couch co-op on its own, shared-world sessions in AI Hub |\n| A villain who taunts you while you play | **Malison**, in subtitled gibberish |\n\n### Stay original\n\nThis is a new game in the same genre, with its own world, cast, art, music and levels. TASK.md says so and it's a hard rule.\n\n- Never use the source's names or look: Sanctuary, Tristram, Caldeum, Westmarch, Horadrim, Nephalem, Cain, Leah, Adria, Tyrael, Imperius, Malthael, Azmodan, Belial, Kanai, Paragon, Torment, its class names and resource names, its famous lines, its melodies, or a HUD built around two orbs. No fallen star, no amnesiac angel.\n- The source is credited by name only on the About screen and in the exit interview.\n- `tools/test.mjs` greps `src/` for these names as whole words (section 16).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Facts verified on this computer\n\nThese save you hours. All were run in a real build here.\n\n**Bundling**\n1. **(verified)** One HTML file boots on `file://` with WebGPU. Bundle with `esbuild game.js --bundle --format=esm --target=es2022 --charset=utf8 --legal-comments=none`, put the result in one inline `<script type=\"module\">`. The engine has no `import.meta` and needs no fetch, so its built-in models and Rapier's wasm work from the file. The result is about 5.3 MB plus your code, with nothing external. Don't minify your own code: the agent that imports the game adds its usage figures to the About screen later, so keep strings findable.\n2. Escape `</script` as `<\\/script` in the bundle. If you insert with `String.replace`, use a function replacer, or `$&` in the code corrupts the file.\n3. **(verified)** Page order that the hub accepts: `<meta charset>`, then `session.js` byte for byte as the first script, then the `hub:*` metas, then `<title>`. Body: `<div id=\"app\"></div>` and the module script.\n4. **(verified)** If you ever need a pack, set `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__['packs/x.json'] = 'data:application/json;base64,...'` in a classic script before the module, then `loadPack('packs/x.json')` works on `file://`. The built-in library is enough for this game, so prefer not to.\n\n**Browsers in tests**\n5. **(verified) Use the kit's flags:** `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` (the list in `check.mjs`). The shorter list in the \"This computer\" notes lost the GPU device within seconds on this engine (`A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`). That error is the flags, not your game.\n6. **(verified)** Software rendering is slow: about 20 fps for a small scene at 1280×720, 3 to 8 fps at 1080p with 40 rigged monsters. So tests advance time with `engine.step(n)` (120 frames took 6 ms in a small scene) and read pixels with `await engine.renderer.capture()` (about 180 ms). Never wait in real time when you can step.\n7. **(verified)** `Engine.headless` works in Node with `buildModel`, `compileClips`, mixers, HUD calls and audio counts. `hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. (Ragdolls were only tried in the browser.) `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys KeyD*30` plays and replays to the same fingerprint. Every module must guard `window`, `document` and `navigator` with `typeof`.\n\n**The hub**\n8. **(verified)** A full engine in the harness's iframes passes: 2 players; 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; the same with `scenario=host-leave`; 2 players with `scenario=server`; and a game-owned card. Copies were ready in 2 to 6.5 seconds.\n9. **(verified)** For `AIHub.server` (a copy with no player) use `Engine.headless(game, {})` inside the iframe and drive it with a timer: ready in 0.6 s, no GPU, harness passes. Step by elapsed time, not a fixed count.\n10. **(verified)** On the game's own card, answer Enter from a plain `window` `keydown` listener, not `wasPressed`. The harness allows 3 seconds and software-rendered frames are slow.\n11. The hub's clocks (from `round.js`): hard limit is `hub:session-minutes` × 1.5, at most 15 minutes; 5 s grace after `time-up`; 3 s countdown; 20 s load grace; 20 s hidden-host limit.\n\n**Characters and animation**\n12. **(verified)** You can build any humanoid as a `ModelDef` of nested pivots named after `HERO_RIG`'s joints, and `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, build.object)` animates it with all 78 hero clips, including `Slash1`, `Slash2`, `Slash3`, `Slam`, `LeapSlam`, `Spin`, `Cast`, `CastBig`, `CastWeapon`, `CastBigWeapon`, `BowDraw`, `BowRelease`, `Roll`, `Charge`, `Shout`, `HitReact`, `Death`, `Triumph`. `new Ragdoll(physics, root, HERO_RAGDOLL)` works on the same body. Template in section 8.\n13. **(verified)** All 15 joints must exist or `compileClips` throws `rig joint \"ForearmR\" not found`. An empty pivot is fine, which keeps cheap monsters cheap (14 meshes against 21).\n14. **(verified)** Compile clips once per body type (63 ms for 78 clips) and share them: `new THREE.AnimationMixer(instance).clipAction(clip)` moves a second instance. `buildModel` is cheap and shares geometry.\n15. **(verified)** Custom clips: `{ name, frames, fast, keys: [[frame, { ArmR: [x, y, z], Pelvis: { p: [x, y, z] } }, 'outCubic'], ...] }` and `gaitClip(HERO_RIG, {...})` compile with `validateClip` clean.\n16. **(verified)** `analyzeClip` throws on merged pivot bodies because its sole meshes are gone. Run it on the engine's own hero inside `Engine.headless`: `const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL)`, same rig, same results. It finds real problems such as `planted foot slides 0.80 m/s`; tune `speed` and `stance` until it's clean.\n17. **(verified)** To attack while running, filter a compiled clip to upper-body tracks: `new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter(t => UPPER.has(t.name.split('.')[0])))` and play it over `Run`. Track names look like `Torso.quaternion`. It ran without error; check how it looks.\n\n**Pause, input, camera, HUD**\n18. **(verified) Pause with `engine.timeScale = 0`.** `update` keeps running with `dt` 0, `fixedUpdate` stops, `wasPressed` still works, so menus work. `engine.paused = true` stops `update` too: never use it for menus. Menu animation counts rendered frames, since `dt` is 0.\n19. `hitstop` and `timeScale` stall the whole simulation. Never use them on a session host. Use them solo and on the couch only.\n20. **(verified)** Use `aspect: 'fill'`. The default letterboxes (at 1280×720 you get 960×540 in the middle). With `fill` the art size changes with the window: 427×240 at 720p, 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 512×288 at 1440p, about 136×276 on a portrait phone. Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height`, never from 480×270.\n21. **(verified)** The `iso` camera with yaw 45 looks toward −X −Z: screen right is (+0.71, 0, −0.71), screen up is (−0.71, 0, −0.71). So a wall on a room's −X or −Z side shows its face to the camera, and a wall on the +X or +Z side blocks the view.\n22. **(verified)** `camera: { preset: 'iso', viewHeight: 11.5, pitch: 42, yaw: 45 }` looks right at 1080p: a hero about 25 art pixels tall, with 40 monsters on screen and still readable. A `viewHeight` of 13 still reads, which gives the room to zoom out for co-op.\n23. **(verified)** The rig zooms on the wheel after `update` runs. Read `ctx.input.wheel` yourself, then set `ctx.input.wheel = 0` to stop it. `setZoom` clamps to `minZoom` and `maxZoom`.\n24. **(verified)** `hud.text` uppercases for you and draws `?` for any character it lacks. It has digits, A to Z, straight and curly quotes, the backtick and `. , : ; - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ ! ? < > # * @ ° · & | ~ ^ $`. No em dash, no ×, no arrows. Text is 6 art pixels per character (minus one) and 7 tall. `hudSprite` icons are about 12×12. A test lints all strings against this set.\n25. **(verified)** The engine's `Input` merges every pad into one, which can't do couch co-op. Set `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = {}` and read `navigator.getGamepads()` yourself, per pad (guard with `typeof`). A stub via `addInitScript` reaches both. The kit's pad mapping is for the platformer and would press Space, KeyJ and so on.\n26. Mouse buttons are keys (`MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`), and the canvas already blocks the context menu. The HUD canvas has `pointer-events: none`, so the pointer reaches the game through it.\n\n**Audio**\n27. **(verified)** Engine defaults are master 0.8, sfx 1, music 0.6, saved under `pixel-engine:audio`, a key shared by every engine game on the same origin. So on first run (your own flag in storage) call `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)`. `audio.resetVolumes()`, which the engine's settings panel calls, puts it back to 0.6, so wrap that method on the instance to re-apply 0.1. That doesn't touch `pixel-engine.js`.\n\n**Touch and look**\n28. **(verified)** Detect touch-only with `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` (true on Chromium's Pixel 7 profile, false on desktop). `touch: false` removes the joystick. The ⚙ button stays visible. WebKit here has no WebGPU, so test touch in Chromium.\n29. **(verified) The mood:** `engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky); engine.sun.intensity = 0.55; engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy); engine.ambient.intensity = 0.9; scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);` plus library torches and a warm light following the hero gives a rich dark dungeon. A tall thin `glowMaterial` box plus a coloured point light on the floor makes a superb loot beam.\n30. **(verified)** Floor textures at full white are too loud against monsters. `toonMaterial(PALETTE.mist, { map })` pushes them back and monsters read much better; `flagstones` tinted that way looked best, and `ashlar` is busy, so keep it for walls. Bright red `Decals` at 1 to 2 m look cartoonish; `plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\n\n**This engine start worked (verified):**\n\n```js\nconst engine = await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({\n  container: document.getElementById('app'),\n  camera: { preset: 'iso', viewHeight: 11.5, pitch: 42, yaw: 45, minZoom: 0.6, maxZoom: 1.4 },\n  aspect: 'fill', quality: 'high', touch: false,\n}));\n```\n\nAdd `settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }` to that **(verified: `false` removes the button)**. Your own Settings screen replaces the ⚙ everywhere except touch-only devices, where TASK.md asks for it.\n\n---\n\n## 3. World, story and tone\n\n### The world\n\n**Vespermoor** is a drowned moorland kingdom under one enormous tower, the **Belfry of Saint Malison**. In it hangs the Great Bell, **Old Clemency**. For a thousand years it tolled at dusk, and the toll told everything below: *stay down*. Forty days ago it cracked. It still tolls. It now says something else.\n\n- **The Risen:** the mindless dead, up and about.\n- **The Unrung:** demons from Below, things no bell was ever rung for. They hate sound, and they've come up through the graves the dead left open.\n- **The Late (formally the Tollborn):** you. You died during the cracked toll, or just after, and got up with your mind intact. Townsfolk find this awkward. They call you *the Late* and ask you to wipe your feet. Death doesn't stick to you, which is why you respawn.\n- **Tollhaven:** the last parish with its lamps lit.\n\n**The truth:** Saint Malison, revered as the foundress who \"gave herself to the bell\", was walled up alive in the tower's foundation by the first bishops, singing. She has heard that bell every dusk for a thousand years. Bishop Ambrose, drowning in debts to a demon called the Bursar, cracked it for her. She wants one thing: to ring the Last Toll, **Eventide**, and wake everything ever buried. The only thing she still fears is the sound of Old Clemency rung true.\n\n### Cast\n\n| Who | Role | Voice and manner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Crier Maudlin** | Quest giver, reads lore aloud. A severed head in a lantern on a post. Lost the body, kept the job. | High, reedy, unstoppable |\n| **Dame Brasse** | Bellfounder: salvage, craft, reforge. Melts church bells into swords. Half deaf. | LOUD. Everything shouted |\n| **Mother Ogive** | Keeper of the Reliquary: extract powers, sockets. Blind; knows relics by taste. | Soft, delighted, unsettling |\n| **Pennywhistle** | Merchant in a plague-doctor beak. | Cheerful, nasal, modest markups considering the apocalypse |\n| **Sister Pyx** | Companion. Armoured nun with a crossbow. | Deadpan |\n| **Bishop Ambrose Thrice-Buried** | Kindly, pale, keeps a spade in the coffin. The traitor. | Warm, then not |\n| **The Bursar** | Mid-game boss. A bloated demon accountant in a stolen cope. | Booming, delighted by interest |\n| **Malison, the Unrung Saint** | Final boss. Huge entombed saint wrapped in bell ropes. | Vast, layered, furious |\n| **The Narrator** | Opening and ending. | Deep and slow |\n\n### Tone\n\nThree registers, and write everything in one of them:\n\n1. **High gothic proclamation:** narration, lore books, Malison. Long vowels, doom, an ominous last line.\n2. **Gallows humour:** townsfolk, item flavour, death messages. Dry, never modern. No slang, no winks.\n3. **Boss taunts:** direct address, mid-fight, short.\n\nLines fit two rows of about 52 characters. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24). Use these as written and write the rest to match.\n\n**Narrator:** \"For a thousand years Old Clemency tolled at dusk, and the dead of Vespermoor stayed down.\" / \"Forty days ago the Great Bell cracked. It still tolls. It now says something else.\" / \"You were buried on the thirty-ninth day. It did not take.\"\n\n**Crier Maudlin:** \"Hear ye, hear ye! The dead are up, the roads are closed, and the fish is off. Also you. You are dead. Welcome back.\" / \"I lost the body at harvest and kept the job. No one told me to stop.\" / \"The parish asks that you wipe your feet. You have been in the ground.\"\n\n**Dame Brasse:** \"WHAT? SPEAK UP! I MELT BELLS FOR A LIVING!\" / \"THAT SWORD WAS A CHURCH BELL ON TUESDAY. HIT SOMETHING WITH IT AND IT STILL SAYS AMEN.\"\n\n**Mother Ogive:** \"Bring me the holy bones, child. I will know them by the taste.\" / \"A saint's knuckle. Very old. A little salty. She died angry.\"\n\n**Pennywhistle:** \"Everything is half price, dear friend. The other half is your soul, but we can discuss terms.\" / \"No refunds. No returns. No survivors, so far.\"\n\n**Sister Pyx:** \"I have killed four hundred things today and confessed to none of them.\" / \"Bless you. Duck.\" / \"You smell like a grave. It is an improvement on the last one.\"\n\n**Bishop Ambrose:** \"They have buried me three times, my child. One learns to keep a spade in the coffin.\"\n\n**The Bursar:** \"YOUR SOUL IS OVERDUE!\" / \"INTEREST COMPOUNDS, LITTLE CORPSE!\" / \"I HAVE YOU DOWN FOR ONE DEATH. I SEE IT WAS NOT COLLECTED.\" / \"FORECLOSURE!\"\n\n**Malison:** \"A THOUSAND YEARS I HAVE BEEN YOUR FOUNDATION STONE. NOW I SHALL BE YOUR CEILING.\" / \"THEY WALLED ME UP SINGING. DO YOU KNOW WHAT I LEARNED IN THE DARK? EVERY VERSE.\" / \"RUN, LITTLE RINGER. THE HOUR IS UNRUNG, AND IT IS YOURS.\" / \"LISTEN. THAT IS EVERY GRAVE YOU EVER WALKED ON, OPENING.\" / (on a hero's death) \"DOWN YOU GO. GIVE MY REGARDS TO THE WORMS.\"\n\n**Lore book:** \"THE THIRD NIGHT. THE GRAVES IN THE NEW YARD ARE EMPTY. THE GRAVES IN THE OLD YARD ARE EMPTY. I HAVE BEGUN DIGGING ONE FOR MYSELF, FOR THE COMPANY.\"\n\n**System lines:** Death: \"YOU HAVE DIED. AGAIN. IT IS BECOMING A HABIT.\" Level up: \"YOU FEEL MORE ALIVE. THIS IS NOT MEDICALLY POSSIBLE.\" Streak: \"37 KILL REQUIEM\".\n\n**Item flavour:** \"She rang it only once. It was enough.\" / \"The best one is still in him.\" / \"Smells of smoke and regret.\"\n\n### The story, in five quests\n\n| # | Quest | Where | What happens | Unlocks |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Wipe Your Feet** | St. Clement's Yard | Your coffin bursts. Tutorial fights. The Crier's voice carries over the wall. Reach Tollhaven. | Town, Pennywhistle, potion |\n| 2 | **The Weeping Causeway** | The Causeway | Find Dame Brasse in a gibbet camp. Defend the wagon of bells on the way back. Sister Pyx joins. | Bellfounder, Lychgates, Pyx |\n| 3 | **Saint Gloam's Bones** | Ossuary, 3 floors | Mother Ogive needs three relic bones. Under the third floor is the Counting House and **the Bursar**, who has a ledger with the Bishop's name in it. | Reliquary, sockets, first legendary guaranteed |\n| 4 | **The Cinder Cloister** | Burning abbey | Rescue the last novices. Malison's voice taunts you openly now. Confront **Bishop Ambrose**, who is buried and bursts out three times. The Crier reads the truth about the saint. | Passing the Belfry gate |\n| 5 | **Ring It or Die Trying** | The Cracked Belfry | Climb the tower. Fight **Malison** beneath the bell. Ring Old Clemency by hand. | Ending, credits, Penance, Knell Runs |\n\n**Ending:** the bell rings true, Malison comes apart, dawn hits the moor. Over the credits, far below, a much deeper bell answers. It's the hook for the rest of the game.\n\n**Side content:** the **Drowned Pantry** (optional small cellar off the Causeway, mini-boss the **Cellarer**, a \"return the overdue book\" joke quest for the Crier); 12 lore books (read aloud, kept in the Codex); **Writs** (section 7).\n\n### The first five minutes\n\n| Time | Beat |\n|---|---|\n| 0:00 | Title, New Hero, pick a class |\n| 0:10 | Narrator over black, a cracked bell toll; 20 seconds, skippable |\n| 0:30 | Night, rain, graveyard. A coffin bursts; hero plays `GetUp`. Prompt: move |\n| 0:40 | Three Peatwalkers. Prompt: attack. They burst. Urns and a barrel shatter, gold rains |\n| 1:30 | Tallow drops, the candle re-melts. A short-beam blue weapon drops. Toast: \"UPGRADE: [glyph] EQUIP\" |\n| 2:30 | Level 2, second skill unlocked, prompt to assign |\n| 3:00 | First telegraph: a red ring grows. Prompt: dodge |\n| 4:00 | An Unquiet Coffin at the gate. 45 seconds of chaos, a chest of gold, level 3 |\n| 5:00 | Tollhaven. \"Hear ye, hear ye!\" |\n\nPacing target: about 60 minutes to the credits for a first player. Tutorial 5, town 3, Causeway 12, Ossuary 15, town 2, Cloister 12, Belfry 8 with Malison, ending 2. A Knell Run takes 6 to 8 minutes.\n\n**New Hero** offers two starts: **The Beginning**, or **The Last Bell**, which is a level 20 hero with a legendary, the town fully open and Knell Runs available, so anyone can see the endgame right away.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Combat\n\n### Rules\n","numLines":235,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1084}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X2be3fsUUnhk17hBpiLWrk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCBnpNPg4iN4h79p8WK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L1cJ7UhFi6W81LTa7S1hB2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","offset":844,"limit":240},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1881,"cache_read_input_tokens":447323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1881},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"a3488386-2ccd-45a2-b82e-7177b4fae30d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:03:01.668Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCBnYV7T2jnBJr179rx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01L1cJ7UhFi6W81LTa7S1hB2":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","offset":844,"limit":240}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L1cJ7UhFi6W81LTa7S1hB2","type":"tool_result","content":"844\t## 13. Attract, dev mode, About, touch\n845\t\n846\t### Attract mode\n847\t\n848\tAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or main menu**, start a looping AI-played tour. **Any input** (key, click, pointer move over 2 px, pad button or stick past deadzone) exits straight back to where it was. It never touches saves.\n849\t\n850\tIt runs a real world with real bots using `src/sim/bot.js`, cheating freely (invulnerable, level 25, full bars, good gear, no cooldown limits, reduced monster HP). A scripted tour of stops, about 2 minutes, joined with `engine.screen.cover('iris')` and `reveal`:\n851\t\n852\t1. Tollhaven, slow pan past each NPC, with a subtitle line.\n853\t2. Causeway: a Bellwarden in a horde, in the rain, a legendary beam drops.\n854\t3. Ossuary: a Sexton with Pallbearers against an elite pack, then the Bursar.\n855\t4. Cloister: a Lamplighter with Beacon and comets.\n856\t5. A Knell Run with all three bots in a party, meter filling, couch HUD showing.\n857\t6. Malison, phase 2, then phase 3 with the bell ringing.\n858\t7. Back to the title card, loop.\n859\t\n860\tShow a \"DEMO\" tag and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\", with the title on each transition. Music plays if audio is unlocked. On a touch-only device it runs too.\n861\t\n862\t### Dev mode\n863\t\n864\t**Pause menu → Dev Mode.** Not in sessions. Pad-navigable like everything else. All changes are live.\n865\t\n866\t**Tools:**\n867\t- *Cheats:* god mode, one-hit kills, no cooldowns, infinite resource, no collision, invisible to monsters.\n868\t- *Give:* level up, level to 30, gold, materials, any item by slot and rarity, any legendary, any set, all gems.\n869\t- *Spawn:* any monster, any elite with chosen Afflictions, any boss, Collection Plate, Unquiet Coffin, kill all.\n870\t- *Travel:* any zone and floor, any quest step, boss arena, start or fill the Knell.\n871\t- *World:* time scale, difficulty, reroll map seed, reveal map, next boss phase.\n872\t- *Party:* add or remove bot seats, bot plays this hero, play the attract tour.\n873\t- *Overlays:* nav grid, hit circles, AI state, spawn markers, flow field, FPS and `engine.state()`.\n874\t\n875\t**Live sliders** (from `src/data/tuning.js`; each with its default shown and a **Reset to defaults** button):\n876\t\n877\tMonster HP, Monster damage, Monster density, Elite frequency, Player damage, Player life, Player speed, Cooldown scale, Resource regen, XP rate, Gold rate, Legendary chance, Dodge cooldown, Tallow chance, Potion cooldown, Pick-up radius, Hit feel (flash, shake, stop), Camera view height.\n878\t\n879\tSim code reads these through `world.tuning`, never as copied constants.\n880\t\n881\t### About and Credits\n882\t\n883\tReachable from the main menu and pause. Pages on L1 and R1, text wrapped to the screen, paged with stick or wheel.\n884\t\n885\t- **Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** exactly what TASK.md lists. Fill them from your exit interview JSON: `tools/build.mjs` reads that file and generates `src/data/about.generated.js`, so the chat reply, the file and the screen can't disagree. Keep the Usage line as the exact words TASK.md asks for, as a plain string, because the import agent replaces it.\n886\t- **Credits:** the game, then the kit's `CREDITS.md` (the kit asks you to ship it): embed it at build time, paged.\n887\t\n888\t### Touch-only devices\n889\t\n890\tDetect as in section 2 item 28. Show the attract mode with \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" wrapped to `hud.width` (a portrait phone fits about 22 characters a line) and the engine's ⚙. No on-screen controls. A tap only returns to the message; idle restarts the tour. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, play normally.\n891\t\n892\t### No WebGPU\n893\t\n894\tCatch the `Engine.start` rejection. Show a static DOM page with the title and \"This game needs WebGPU: a recent Chrome or Edge, Safari 26, or Firefox on Windows\". In a session, call `AIHub.fail`.\n895\t\n896\t---\n897\t\n898\t## 14. Architecture\n899\t\n900\t### Folder layout\n901\t\n902\t```text\n903\tpixel-engine.js, check.mjs, GUIDE.md, API.md, ASSETS.md, LIBRARY.md, CREDITS.md   the kit, unedited\n904\tsession.js              the hub client, byte for byte\n905\tgame.js                 entry: exports createGame(opts); starts the engine only when document exists\n906\tindex.html              dev page\n907\tsrc/data/               meta tuning classes skills vows items affixes legendaries sets gems monsters\n908\t                        elites bosses zones rooms/* quests dialog lore songs sfx voices strings\n909\tsrc/sim/                world hero cast effects monsters elites bosses loot stats quests zonegen\n910\t                        knell round bot events intents serialize\n911\tsrc/view/               scene zonebuild actors models/* clips vfx lootview labels camera cutscene\n912\tsrc/ui/                 ui glyphs hud menus/* dialog devmode\n913\tsrc/input/              router pads kbm\n914\tsrc/net/                transport host client codec hubflow card\n915\tsrc/audio/              music sfx voice\n916\tsrc/save/               save\n917\tsrc/modes/              shell (title, menu, attract state machine), play\n918\ttools/                  build.mjs test.mjs shots.mjs report.mjs hub/(harness.html bridge.js round.js)\n919\ttests/                  sim/* headless/* browser/*\n920\tdocs/DESIGNERS.md       how to add a monster, skill, item, room, zone, quest, song\n921\t```\n922\t\n923\t**The day-to-day loop:** `node tools/build.mjs` (esbuild takes a second), then run the bundle over `file://`. ES modules can't load from `file://`, so `index.html` needs a server; `node check.mjs` brings its own on `127.0.0.1`, port 0. Install everything inside the dev folder.\n924\t\n925\t### The split that everything depends on\n926\t\n927\t- **`src/sim` is plain JavaScript:** no THREE, no DOM, no `ctx`, no `Math.random`, no `performance.now`. It takes the engine's `Rng` and `NavGrid` only (both pure). `stepWorld(world, intentsBySeat)` at 60 Hz. It can run alone in Node, headless, on a client's mirror API, and with bots.\n928\t- **One world, many seats from day one.** Solo is a party of one. There's no special case to retrofit for co-op.\n929\t- **Input becomes intent.** `Intent = { moveX, moveZ, aimX, aimZ, held, pressed }` from the keyboard and mouse, a pad, the network or a bot. The sim can't tell which.\n930\t- **The sim emits events, the view consumes them.** `world.events.push({ t: 'hit', id, amt, crit, x, z })`. The view turns events into effects. The host forwards the same events to clients. Effects never affect the sim.\n931\t- **The view reads a world interface:** heroes, monsters, drops, zones. On a host it's the sim, on a client a mirror. The view code is the same.\n932\t- **One `Game` object for the whole session.** Zones are swapped inside it by disposing a `zoneRoot` group (`disposeObject`), releasing lights and clearing particles, so engine recordings and fingerprints cover a full playthrough. Don't use `loadGame`.\n933\t\n934\t### Game hooks\n935\t\n936\t- `fixedUpdate`: gather intents, `stepWorld`, unless paused or waiting.\n937\t- `update`: consume events, pose actors, draw UI, set zoom, poll pads and `input.send` their state.\n938\t- `fingerprint`: a hash of sim state. `status`: zone, level, party, kills. `ready`: `window.__GAME__ = this`, guarded.\n939\t- `dt` can reach 0.1 s on slow machines; the sim only sees fixed steps.\n940\t\n941\t### Pathing and AI\n942\t\n943\t- `NavGrid` from the zone grid (1 m cells). One `NavGrid` instance per seat for `flowTo`, since each holds one flow field. Monsters read the field of their nearest hero, plus separation from a spatial hash with 1.5 m cells. Click-to-move uses `nav.path`.\n944\t- Monsters are per-archetype state machines (idle, aggro, approach, telegraph, strike, recover, flee), with data for numbers. `BehaviorTree` is available but not needed. Packs stay dormant until a hero is within 30 m. Aggro at 12 m with `lineOfSight`.\n945\t\n946\t### Randomness and saves\n947\t\n948\t- All sim randomness from `Rng` forks: `rng.fork('zone:' + id)`, `rng.fork('loot')`. Sessions seed from `info.seed`. A new game seed is chosen in the UI and passed through `ctx.input.send` so it replays.\n949\t- **Saves:** `localStorage` under a key built from `TITLE`, in `try/catch`, versioned JSON. Heroes (3 slots, each with gear, inventory, skills, quests, zone seed), guest heroes, stash, Devotion, unlocks, bests, settings. Autosave on zone change, quest step, vendor close, and every 60 s. Sessions never save. Saved game data reaches the sim through `ctx.input.send`.\n950\t\n951\t### Performance\n952\t\n953\tTASK.md makes the budget unlimited, so don't optimise: `quality: 'high'` (16 lights), as many monsters, particles and lights as a scene wants, 150+ on screen at peak. The only rule is sharing things that are free to share: `compileClips` per body type, `buildModel` for geometry, `glowMaterial` for flashes.\n954\t\n955\t### Designer tools\n956\t\n957\tSo the rest of the game can be built later: all content is plain tables in `src/data`, rooms are ASCII, models are `ModelDef`s (`node check.mjs --sheets`), songs are text patterns. Dev mode tests any of it at once. `docs/DESIGNERS.md` is a page of recipes.\n958\t\n959\t---\n960\t\n961\t## 15. Build order\n962\t\n963\tFinish each milestone before the next. The deliverable builds and runs after each one. Run the tier of tests that covers what you changed.\n964\t\n965\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n966\t|---|---|---|\n967\t| **M0** | **Setup.** Kit unpacked, `session.js` and hub files fetched, `npm i -D playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder, `tools/build.mjs`, `tools/test.mjs`, an empty game | The HTML boots on `file://` in Playwright with the right flags; `node check.mjs --headless game.js` passes; title picked |\n968\t| **M1** | **One good room.** Sim, intents, one Bellwarden with Clout and Great Toll, Peatwalkers, keyboard and mouse and pad, candle, action bar, numbers, ragdolls, shattering props, gold, Tallow | It's fun to hit things for a minute. A sim test kills 20 monsters with a bot. Replay matches |\n969\t| **M2** | **Zone pipeline.** ASCII rooms, generator, wall rule, textures, lights, Ossuary floor, `NavGrid` chase, telegraphs, dodge | Path test passes for 200 seeds. A 1080p shot reads |\n970\t| **M3** | **All three classes.** Effect ops, all 8 skills per class, Tones, Vows, resources, unlocks, Skills screen. Loopback net test (host and mirror in Node) | Bot uses every skill and Tone without error. Mirror test passes |\n971\t| **M4** | **Loot.** Items, affixes, rarities, beams, Gear screen, compare, equip, visible weapons and helms, legendaries, sets, Pennywhistle, Brasse, Ogive, gems, stash, save and load | Bot finds and equips upgrades. Save round-trips. Menu flow test by pad and by mouse |\n972\t| **M5** | **The campaign.** All zones, quests, dialogue, voices, town, Lychgates, Passing Bell, Requiem, shrines, coffins, Plate, elites, bosses, cutscenes, full music and SFX | Whole-game playthrough passes for all three classes |\n973\t| **M6** | **Multiplayer.** Couch seats and camera, Pyx. Hub flow, netcode, own card, the round | Harness passes in all 5 variants. A game test sees P2's hero move in P1's world. Pad stubs drive 4 seats |\n974\t| **M7** | **Endgame.** Knell Runs, Grand Knell, Penance, Devotion, Writs, The Last Bell start | Bot clears a Knell Run on each class |\n975\t| **M8** | **The shell.** Title, menu, hero select, settings, attract, dev mode, Codex, How to Play, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU | All shell tests pass. Every screen shot looks right at three sizes |\n976\t| **M9** | **Finish.** Balance with `tools/report.mjs` and sliders, a look at every shot, more lines, more juice, exit interview, final build | Definition of done |\n977\t\n978\t**Do M6 after M5 but keep the seams from M1:** the mirror test in M3 proves the split early.\n979\t\n980\t### If you must cut\n981\t\n982\tWhole features only, in this order, and remove every trace: Writs → Drowned Pantry → Gems → Devotion → Vows → Grand Knell → Sister Pyx → Reliquary extraction → Lore books (keep How to Play) → the round's level-up picks → the third class's last 2 skills.\n983\t\n984\t**Never cut:** three classes, Tones, loot rarities with beams, legendaries, town services, five quests, three bosses, Knell Runs, couch co-op, hub sessions, pad-first UI, glyph switching, attract, dev mode with sliders, About, voices, music at 10%, the playthrough test.\n985\t\n986\t---\n987\t\n988\t## 16. Testing\n989\t\n990\t`node tools/test.mjs` runs everything and prints **only failures and one count line**. `--sim`, `--headless`, `--browser`, `--hub` run one tier; rerun only the tier that covers what you changed. Use at most two browsers at once, sequentially. Serve from `127.0.0.1` on port 0 inside the test process, confirm the page's title is yours, and stop only what you started. \"Target closed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out: run fewer at once. Don't use subagents or workflows to review or judge.\n991\t\n992\t### Tier 1: sim (Node, no engine loop, seconds)\n993\t\n994\t- `stepWorld` is deterministic: same seed and intents, same hash, for 5 minutes of play.\n995\t- Damage, armour, XP curve, item generation stay inside ranges; items always valid. Each effect op works. Each legendary's hook fires. Each Affliction behaves.\n996\t- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone.\n997\t- **Net:** host plus mirrors over a simulated lossy transport (150 ms, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss) in Node: mirrors converge, commands arrive, budgets respected (message rate under 20 a second, `s` under 1,100 bytes, `e` under 12 KB).\n998\t- **Lint:** every string in `src/data` fits the HUD font; line lengths fit; no `Math.random` or `performance.now` in `src/sim`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, `placeholder`, `stub` or `coming soon` anywhere in `src`; none of the banned names from section 1; every `use`, texture, clip, sound and song referenced by data exists; `validateClip` clean on every clip; `renderSound` non-silent and peak ≤ 1 for every sound; `parseSong` on every song.\n999\t- `checkModel` has zero problems on every model.\n1000\t\n1001\t### Tier 2: the game in `Engine.headless` (Node, a minute or two)\n1002\t\n1003\t- `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys ...` with keys that really play. Replay matches.\n1004\t- **Whole-game playthrough, once per class, default tuning, Pilgrim:** the bot (`tests/headless/playthrough.mjs`) starts at the title, makes a hero through the real menus by keys, plays to the credits by intents and commands. Asserts: every zone visited; every quest done; all three bosses killed; every skill slot used; a legendary equipped; item salvaged, crafted, reforged, sold, bought, stashed, extracted, socketed; every Lychgate touched; a shrine and a coffin used; ending played; Knell Runs unlocked; then one full Knell Run. Fail on any softlock (no progress for 3 sim minutes).\n1005\t- **Balance report:** `tools/report.mjs` prints minutes per zone, deaths, level at each zone, boss durations, drops by rarity. Assert: campaign under 75 sim minutes; level 16 to 24 at the credits; the Bursar 60 to 180 s; Malison 120 to 300 s; 2+ legendaries.\n1006\t- **Screens:** every menu opens, navigates, closes, by keyboard codes. `ui.drawnText` has what it should. Dev mode: every tool and slider has an effect, and Reset restores.\n1007\t- **Attract:** idle 600 frames on the title: attract starts. Idle on the main menu: same. Any key exits. It loops twice with no errors, covering each stop. Saves untouched.\n1008\t- **Audio:** `audio.volume.music === 0.1` on first run, and after Reset. Every zone starts its song. Speaking a line increases counts and its syllables are the same each time.\n1009\t\n1010\t### Tier 3: browser (real WebGPU on SwiftShader)\n1011\t\n1012\tUse the flags in section 2 item 5. Open the bundle over `file://`, use `engine.step` and `capture`, and don't wait in real time.\n1013\t\n1014\t- **Boot:** no page, console, game or GPU errors. Picture isn't blank (`capture`). The bundle is one file: `session.js` byte-identical and first; metas present.\n1015\t- **Pad only** (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads` in standard mapping via `addInitScript`): press through title, hero select, play, skills, Hero screen, pause, dev mode, settings, quit. PlayStation glyphs shown (`ui` reports the glyph set). Xbox option switches them. A key press switches prompts to keycaps; a pad press switches back.\n1016\t- **Mouse and keyboard only:** hover moves focus (`page.mouse.move` over a menu item, `ui.focus` changes); click activates; click-to-move moves; click on a monster attacks; every key in section 10 works.\n1017\t- **Couch:** 4 stub pads join, each moves its own hero, camera holds them.\n1018\t- **Touch:** Chromium's Pixel 7 profile: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. Tap doesn't start a game. WebKit here has no WebGPU, so it can only confirm the no-WebGPU page.\n1019\t- **Sound, by what Web Audio produces:** the engine doesn't expose its output node, so wrap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in `addInitScript` to also feed anything connected to the destination into an `AnalyserNode`. After a key press unlocks audio: music alone gives a non-zero level; a sound effect raises it well above that; a spoken line produces sound; `end` in a session brings it to silence.\n1020\t- **Layout:** `ui.drawnText` rectangles stay inside the screen at 1280×720, 1920×1080, 2560×1440, with no overlaps on each screen.\n1021\t- **Screenshots** for your own eyes (`tools/shots.mjs`, at 1920×1080): title, attract, combat with 40+ monsters, each zone, each class casting, Gear, Skills, each vendor, Map, dialogue, each boss, Knell meter, couch HUD, dev mode, About, touch. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check: look at each one at least once before finishing.\n1022\t\n1023\t### Tier 4: hub\n1024\t\n1025\tCopy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` beside a copy of the deliverable and serve them on `127.0.0.1` port 0. Open and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`:\n1026\t\n1027\t1. `?game=GAME&players=2&auto=1`\n1028\t2. `?game=GAME&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n1029\t3. The same with `&scenario=host-leave`\n1030\t4. `?game=GAME&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n1031\t5. `?game=GAME&players=1&auto=1`\n1032\t\n1033\tThen a **game-level** check: two frames, drive P2 by synthetic keys inside its frame, and read `frame.contentWindow.__GAME__` to see P2's hero move in P1's world and P1's in P2's. Then outside a session: the page opened on its own still plays normally.\n1034\t\n1035\t---\n1036\t\n1037\t## 17. Coverage and definition of done\n1038\t\n1039\t### TASK.md to this plan\n1040\t\n1041\t| TASK.md asks for | Where |\n1042\t|---|---|\n1043\t| Inspired by the source, original | 1, 3 |\n1044\t| Genre, perspective | Top, 2 (item 22) |\n1045\t| Title | 0 (builder picks) |\n1046\t| Single-file package | 2 (items 1 to 4), 14 |\n1047\t| Engine kit, kept as shipped; new systems on top | 2, 14 |\n1048\t| Art direction, new assets | 8 |\n1049\t| Animation, new clips | 9 |\n1050\t| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | 11, 2 (item 27) |\n1051\t| Online and multiplayer, hub and on its own | 12 |\n1052\t| Dev folder, sharing rules, ports | 0, 14, 16 |\n1053\t| Unlimited performance budget | 14 |\n1054\t| Headless testing, whole-game playthrough, one command | 16 |\n1055\t| Stand-ins for what this computer lacks (pad, touch, listener, second player, TV) | 16 (tiers 3 and 4) |\n1056\t| Research is the builder's choice | 0 |\n1057\t| Feature-complete demo, all mechanics shown | 3 to 7 |\n1058\t| Infrastructure for later content | 14 (Designer tools) |\n1059\t| Dev mode, sliders, reset | 13 |\n1060\t| Attract mode | 13 |\n1061\t| Narrative tone | 3 |\n1062\t| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; prompts by last input; PS glyphs, Xbox option | 10 |\n1063\t| No dense screens | 10 |\n1064\t| Touch-only behaviour | 13 |\n1065\t| No TODOs or stubs | 0, 16 (lint) |\n1066\t| Source Information and feedback in chat and on About | 13, below |\n1067\t| Exit interview | Below |\n1068\t\n1069\t### Done means\n1070\t\n1071\t- [ ] Every \"never cut\" item in section 15 is in and works. Nothing visible does nothing.\n1072\t- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs` reports zero failures, including the playthrough for all three classes and all hub variants.\n1073\t- [ ] You looked at every screenshot. The scene reads, HUD is legible, nothing is black or clipped.\n1074\t- [ ] The deliverable HTML is where TASK.md says, one file, and runs on `file://` and from a server.\n1075\t- [ ] Exit interview JSON saved where TASK.md says, in its exact shape, and parses. Suggested `aiHub` fields (use your own title for `name`):\n1076\t  - tagline: `The bell is cracked. The dead are up. So are you.`\n1077\t  - description: `A gothic hack-and-slash for 1 to 4 players: smash hordes as a Bellwarden, Lamplighter or Sexton, hunt loot that rings like church bells, and silence a furious walled-up saint.`\n1078\t  - type: `Game`; genre: `RPG`; source: `Diablo 3`; series: `Diablo`; players: `1–4`\n1079\t  - controls: `Stick or WASD or click to move · Cross or click to attack · face buttons, R1, R2 or right click, 1-4 for skills · L2 or Space to dodge`\n1080\t  - tags: `3d`, `co-op`, `pixel art`, `fantasy`, `boss fights`, `top-down`\n1081\t- [ ] About shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, generated from that JSON, with real answers.\n1082\t- [ ] Your final chat reply carries the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n1083\t- [ ] Every process you started is stopped, and every file you made is inside your folder."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"b3bde4da-d044-49d5-9a2c-46b0b477599f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:03:01.674Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 13. Attract, dev mode, About, touch\n\n### Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or main menu**, start a looping AI-played tour. **Any input** (key, click, pointer move over 2 px, pad button or stick past deadzone) exits straight back to where it was. It never touches saves.\n\nIt runs a real world with real bots using `src/sim/bot.js`, cheating freely (invulnerable, level 25, full bars, good gear, no cooldown limits, reduced monster HP). A scripted tour of stops, about 2 minutes, joined with `engine.screen.cover('iris')` and `reveal`:\n\n1. Tollhaven, slow pan past each NPC, with a subtitle line.\n2. Causeway: a Bellwarden in a horde, in the rain, a legendary beam drops.\n3. Ossuary: a Sexton with Pallbearers against an elite pack, then the Bursar.\n4. Cloister: a Lamplighter with Beacon and comets.\n5. A Knell Run with all three bots in a party, meter filling, couch HUD showing.\n6. Malison, phase 2, then phase 3 with the bell ringing.\n7. Back to the title card, loop.\n\nShow a \"DEMO\" tag and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\", with the title on each transition. Music plays if audio is unlocked. On a touch-only device it runs too.\n\n### Dev mode\n\n**Pause menu → Dev Mode.** Not in sessions. Pad-navigable like everything else. All changes are live.\n\n**Tools:**\n- *Cheats:* god mode, one-hit kills, no cooldowns, infinite resource, no collision, invisible to monsters.\n- *Give:* level up, level to 30, gold, materials, any item by slot and rarity, any legendary, any set, all gems.\n- *Spawn:* any monster, any elite with chosen Afflictions, any boss, Collection Plate, Unquiet Coffin, kill all.\n- *Travel:* any zone and floor, any quest step, boss arena, start or fill the Knell.\n- *World:* time scale, difficulty, reroll map seed, reveal map, next boss phase.\n- *Party:* add or remove bot seats, bot plays this hero, play the attract tour.\n- *Overlays:* nav grid, hit circles, AI state, spawn markers, flow field, FPS and `engine.state()`.\n\n**Live sliders** (from `src/data/tuning.js`; each with its default shown and a **Reset to defaults** button):\n\nMonster HP, Monster damage, Monster density, Elite frequency, Player damage, Player life, Player speed, Cooldown scale, Resource regen, XP rate, Gold rate, Legendary chance, Dodge cooldown, Tallow chance, Potion cooldown, Pick-up radius, Hit feel (flash, shake, stop), Camera view height.\n\nSim code reads these through `world.tuning`, never as copied constants.\n\n### About and Credits\n\nReachable from the main menu and pause. Pages on L1 and R1, text wrapped to the screen, paged with stick or wheel.\n\n- **Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback:** exactly what TASK.md lists. Fill them from your exit interview JSON: `tools/build.mjs` reads that file and generates `src/data/about.generated.js`, so the chat reply, the file and the screen can't disagree. Keep the Usage line as the exact words TASK.md asks for, as a plain string, because the import agent replaces it.\n- **Credits:** the game, then the kit's `CREDITS.md` (the kit asks you to ship it): embed it at build time, paged.\n\n### Touch-only devices\n\nDetect as in section 2 item 28. Show the attract mode with \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" wrapped to `hud.width` (a portrait phone fits about 22 characters a line) and the engine's ⚙. No on-screen controls. A tap only returns to the message; idle restarts the tour. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, play normally.\n\n### No WebGPU\n\nCatch the `Engine.start` rejection. Show a static DOM page with the title and \"This game needs WebGPU: a recent Chrome or Edge, Safari 26, or Firefox on Windows\". In a session, call `AIHub.fail`.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Architecture\n\n### Folder layout\n\n```text\npixel-engine.js, check.mjs, GUIDE.md, API.md, ASSETS.md, LIBRARY.md, CREDITS.md   the kit, unedited\nsession.js              the hub client, byte for byte\ngame.js                 entry: exports createGame(opts); starts the engine only when document exists\nindex.html              dev page\nsrc/data/               meta tuning classes skills vows items affixes legendaries sets gems monsters\n                        elites bosses zones rooms/* quests dialog lore songs sfx voices strings\nsrc/sim/                world hero cast effects monsters elites bosses loot stats quests zonegen\n                        knell round bot events intents serialize\nsrc/view/               scene zonebuild actors models/* clips vfx lootview labels camera cutscene\nsrc/ui/                 ui glyphs hud menus/* dialog devmode\nsrc/input/              router pads kbm\nsrc/net/                transport host client codec hubflow card\nsrc/audio/              music sfx voice\nsrc/save/               save\nsrc/modes/              shell (title, menu, attract state machine), play\ntools/                  build.mjs test.mjs shots.mjs report.mjs hub/(harness.html bridge.js round.js)\ntests/                  sim/* headless/* browser/*\ndocs/DESIGNERS.md       how to add a monster, skill, item, room, zone, quest, song\n```\n\n**The day-to-day loop:** `node tools/build.mjs` (esbuild takes a second), then run the bundle over `file://`. ES modules can't load from `file://`, so `index.html` needs a server; `node check.mjs` brings its own on `127.0.0.1`, port 0. Install everything inside the dev folder.\n\n### The split that everything depends on\n\n- **`src/sim` is plain JavaScript:** no THREE, no DOM, no `ctx`, no `Math.random`, no `performance.now`. It takes the engine's `Rng` and `NavGrid` only (both pure). `stepWorld(world, intentsBySeat)` at 60 Hz. It can run alone in Node, headless, on a client's mirror API, and with bots.\n- **One world, many seats from day one.** Solo is a party of one. There's no special case to retrofit for co-op.\n- **Input becomes intent.** `Intent = { moveX, moveZ, aimX, aimZ, held, pressed }` from the keyboard and mouse, a pad, the network or a bot. The sim can't tell which.\n- **The sim emits events, the view consumes them.** `world.events.push({ t: 'hit', id, amt, crit, x, z })`. The view turns events into effects. The host forwards the same events to clients. Effects never affect the sim.\n- **The view reads a world interface:** heroes, monsters, drops, zones. On a host it's the sim, on a client a mirror. The view code is the same.\n- **One `Game` object for the whole session.** Zones are swapped inside it by disposing a `zoneRoot` group (`disposeObject`), releasing lights and clearing particles, so engine recordings and fingerprints cover a full playthrough. Don't use `loadGame`.\n\n### Game hooks\n\n- `fixedUpdate`: gather intents, `stepWorld`, unless paused or waiting.\n- `update`: consume events, pose actors, draw UI, set zoom, poll pads and `input.send` their state.\n- `fingerprint`: a hash of sim state. `status`: zone, level, party, kills. `ready`: `window.__GAME__ = this`, guarded.\n- `dt` can reach 0.1 s on slow machines; the sim only sees fixed steps.\n\n### Pathing and AI\n\n- `NavGrid` from the zone grid (1 m cells). One `NavGrid` instance per seat for `flowTo`, since each holds one flow field. Monsters read the field of their nearest hero, plus separation from a spatial hash with 1.5 m cells. Click-to-move uses `nav.path`.\n- Monsters are per-archetype state machines (idle, aggro, approach, telegraph, strike, recover, flee), with data for numbers. `BehaviorTree` is available but not needed. Packs stay dormant until a hero is within 30 m. Aggro at 12 m with `lineOfSight`.\n\n### Randomness and saves\n\n- All sim randomness from `Rng` forks: `rng.fork('zone:' + id)`, `rng.fork('loot')`. Sessions seed from `info.seed`. A new game seed is chosen in the UI and passed through `ctx.input.send` so it replays.\n- **Saves:** `localStorage` under a key built from `TITLE`, in `try/catch`, versioned JSON. Heroes (3 slots, each with gear, inventory, skills, quests, zone seed), guest heroes, stash, Devotion, unlocks, bests, settings. Autosave on zone change, quest step, vendor close, and every 60 s. Sessions never save. Saved game data reaches the sim through `ctx.input.send`.\n\n### Performance\n\nTASK.md makes the budget unlimited, so don't optimise: `quality: 'high'` (16 lights), as many monsters, particles and lights as a scene wants, 150+ on screen at peak. The only rule is sharing things that are free to share: `compileClips` per body type, `buildModel` for geometry, `glowMaterial` for flashes.\n\n### Designer tools\n\nSo the rest of the game can be built later: all content is plain tables in `src/data`, rooms are ASCII, models are `ModelDef`s (`node check.mjs --sheets`), songs are text patterns. Dev mode tests any of it at once. `docs/DESIGNERS.md` is a page of recipes.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Build order\n\nFinish each milestone before the next. The deliverable builds and runs after each one. Run the tier of tests that covers what you changed.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | **Setup.** Kit unpacked, `session.js` and hub files fetched, `npm i -D playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder, `tools/build.mjs`, `tools/test.mjs`, an empty game | The HTML boots on `file://` in Playwright with the right flags; `node check.mjs --headless game.js` passes; title picked |\n| **M1** | **One good room.** Sim, intents, one Bellwarden with Clout and Great Toll, Peatwalkers, keyboard and mouse and pad, candle, action bar, numbers, ragdolls, shattering props, gold, Tallow | It's fun to hit things for a minute. A sim test kills 20 monsters with a bot. Replay matches |\n| **M2** | **Zone pipeline.** ASCII rooms, generator, wall rule, textures, lights, Ossuary floor, `NavGrid` chase, telegraphs, dodge | Path test passes for 200 seeds. A 1080p shot reads |\n| **M3** | **All three classes.** Effect ops, all 8 skills per class, Tones, Vows, resources, unlocks, Skills screen. Loopback net test (host and mirror in Node) | Bot uses every skill and Tone without error. Mirror test passes |\n| **M4** | **Loot.** Items, affixes, rarities, beams, Gear screen, compare, equip, visible weapons and helms, legendaries, sets, Pennywhistle, Brasse, Ogive, gems, stash, save and load | Bot finds and equips upgrades. Save round-trips. Menu flow test by pad and by mouse |\n| **M5** | **The campaign.** All zones, quests, dialogue, voices, town, Lychgates, Passing Bell, Requiem, shrines, coffins, Plate, elites, bosses, cutscenes, full music and SFX | Whole-game playthrough passes for all three classes |\n| **M6** | **Multiplayer.** Couch seats and camera, Pyx. Hub flow, netcode, own card, the round | Harness passes in all 5 variants. A game test sees P2's hero move in P1's world. Pad stubs drive 4 seats |\n| **M7** | **Endgame.** Knell Runs, Grand Knell, Penance, Devotion, Writs, The Last Bell start | Bot clears a Knell Run on each class |\n| **M8** | **The shell.** Title, menu, hero select, settings, attract, dev mode, Codex, How to Play, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU | All shell tests pass. Every screen shot looks right at three sizes |\n| **M9** | **Finish.** Balance with `tools/report.mjs` and sliders, a look at every shot, more lines, more juice, exit interview, final build | Definition of done |\n\n**Do M6 after M5 but keep the seams from M1:** the mirror test in M3 proves the split early.\n\n### If you must cut\n\nWhole features only, in this order, and remove every trace: Writs → Drowned Pantry → Gems → Devotion → Vows → Grand Knell → Sister Pyx → Reliquary extraction → Lore books (keep How to Play) → the round's level-up picks → the third class's last 2 skills.\n\n**Never cut:** three classes, Tones, loot rarities with beams, legendaries, town services, five quests, three bosses, Knell Runs, couch co-op, hub sessions, pad-first UI, glyph switching, attract, dev mode with sliders, About, voices, music at 10%, the playthrough test.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing\n\n`node tools/test.mjs` runs everything and prints **only failures and one count line**. `--sim`, `--headless`, `--browser`, `--hub` run one tier; rerun only the tier that covers what you changed. Use at most two browsers at once, sequentially. Serve from `127.0.0.1` on port 0 inside the test process, confirm the page's title is yours, and stop only what you started. \"Target closed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out: run fewer at once. Don't use subagents or workflows to review or judge.\n\n### Tier 1: sim (Node, no engine loop, seconds)\n\n- `stepWorld` is deterministic: same seed and intents, same hash, for 5 minutes of play.\n- Damage, armour, XP curve, item generation stay inside ranges; items always valid. Each effect op works. Each legendary's hook fires. Each Affliction behaves.\n- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone.\n- **Net:** host plus mirrors over a simulated lossy transport (150 ms, 50 ms jitter, 5% loss) in Node: mirrors converge, commands arrive, budgets respected (message rate under 20 a second, `s` under 1,100 bytes, `e` under 12 KB).\n- **Lint:** every string in `src/data` fits the HUD font; line lengths fit; no `Math.random` or `performance.now` in `src/sim`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, `placeholder`, `stub` or `coming soon` anywhere in `src`; none of the banned names from section 1; every `use`, texture, clip, sound and song referenced by data exists; `validateClip` clean on every clip; `renderSound` non-silent and peak ≤ 1 for every sound; `parseSong` on every song.\n- `checkModel` has zero problems on every model.\n\n### Tier 2: the game in `Engine.headless` (Node, a minute or two)\n\n- `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys ...` with keys that really play. Replay matches.\n- **Whole-game playthrough, once per class, default tuning, Pilgrim:** the bot (`tests/headless/playthrough.mjs`) starts at the title, makes a hero through the real menus by keys, plays to the credits by intents and commands. Asserts: every zone visited; every quest done; all three bosses killed; every skill slot used; a legendary equipped; item salvaged, crafted, reforged, sold, bought, stashed, extracted, socketed; every Lychgate touched; a shrine and a coffin used; ending played; Knell Runs unlocked; then one full Knell Run. Fail on any softlock (no progress for 3 sim minutes).\n- **Balance report:** `tools/report.mjs` prints minutes per zone, deaths, level at each zone, boss durations, drops by rarity. Assert: campaign under 75 sim minutes; level 16 to 24 at the credits; the Bursar 60 to 180 s; Malison 120 to 300 s; 2+ legendaries.\n- **Screens:** every menu opens, navigates, closes, by keyboard codes. `ui.drawnText` has what it should. Dev mode: every tool and slider has an effect, and Reset restores.\n- **Attract:** idle 600 frames on the title: attract starts. Idle on the main menu: same. Any key exits. It loops twice with no errors, covering each stop. Saves untouched.\n- **Audio:** `audio.volume.music === 0.1` on first run, and after Reset. Every zone starts its song. Speaking a line increases counts and its syllables are the same each time.\n\n### Tier 3: browser (real WebGPU on SwiftShader)\n\nUse the flags in section 2 item 5. Open the bundle over `file://`, use `engine.step` and `capture`, and don't wait in real time.\n\n- **Boot:** no page, console, game or GPU errors. Picture isn't blank (`capture`). The bundle is one file: `session.js` byte-identical and first; metas present.\n- **Pad only** (stubbed `navigator.getGamepads` in standard mapping via `addInitScript`): press through title, hero select, play, skills, Hero screen, pause, dev mode, settings, quit. PlayStation glyphs shown (`ui` reports the glyph set). Xbox option switches them. A key press switches prompts to keycaps; a pad press switches back.\n- **Mouse and keyboard only:** hover moves focus (`page.mouse.move` over a menu item, `ui.focus` changes); click activates; click-to-move moves; click on a monster attacks; every key in section 10 works.\n- **Couch:** 4 stub pads join, each moves its own hero, camera holds them.\n- **Touch:** Chromium's Pixel 7 profile: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. Tap doesn't start a game. WebKit here has no WebGPU, so it can only confirm the no-WebGPU page.\n- **Sound, by what Web Audio produces:** the engine doesn't expose its output node, so wrap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in `addInitScript` to also feed anything connected to the destination into an `AnalyserNode`. After a key press unlocks audio: music alone gives a non-zero level; a sound effect raises it well above that; a spoken line produces sound; `end` in a session brings it to silence.\n- **Layout:** `ui.drawnText` rectangles stay inside the screen at 1280×720, 1920×1080, 2560×1440, with no overlaps on each screen.\n- **Screenshots** for your own eyes (`tools/shots.mjs`, at 1920×1080): title, attract, combat with 40+ monsters, each zone, each class casting, Gear, Skills, each vendor, Map, dialogue, each boss, Knell meter, couch HUD, dev mode, About, touch. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check: look at each one at least once before finishing.\n\n### Tier 4: hub\n\nCopy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` beside a copy of the deliverable and serve them on `127.0.0.1` port 0. Open and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`:\n\n1. `?game=GAME&players=2&auto=1`\n2. `?game=GAME&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n3. The same with `&scenario=host-leave`\n4. `?game=GAME&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n5. `?game=GAME&players=1&auto=1`\n\nThen a **game-level** check: two frames, drive P2 by synthetic keys inside its frame, and read `frame.contentWindow.__GAME__` to see P2's hero move in P1's world and P1's in P2's. Then outside a session: the page opened on its own still plays normally.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Coverage and definition of done\n\n### TASK.md to this plan\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Inspired by the source, original | 1, 3 |\n| Genre, perspective | Top, 2 (item 22) |\n| Title | 0 (builder picks) |\n| Single-file package | 2 (items 1 to 4), 14 |\n| Engine kit, kept as shipped; new systems on top | 2, 14 |\n| Art direction, new assets | 8 |\n| Animation, new clips | 9 |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | 11, 2 (item 27) |\n| Online and multiplayer, hub and on its own | 12 |\n| Dev folder, sharing rules, ports | 0, 14, 16 |\n| Unlimited performance budget | 14 |\n| Headless testing, whole-game playthrough, one command | 16 |\n| Stand-ins for what this computer lacks (pad, touch, listener, second player, TV) | 16 (tiers 3 and 4) |\n| Research is the builder's choice | 0 |\n| Feature-complete demo, all mechanics shown | 3 to 7 |\n| Infrastructure for later content | 14 (Designer tools) |\n| Dev mode, sliders, reset | 13 |\n| Attract mode | 13 |\n| Narrative tone | 3 |\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; prompts by last input; PS glyphs, Xbox option | 10 |\n| No dense screens | 10 |\n| Touch-only behaviour | 13 |\n| No TODOs or stubs | 0, 16 (lint) |\n| Source Information and feedback in chat and on About | 13, below |\n| Exit interview | Below |\n\n### Done means\n\n- [ ] Every \"never cut\" item in section 15 is in and works. Nothing visible does nothing.\n- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs` reports zero failures, including the playthrough for all three classes and all hub variants.\n- [ ] You looked at every screenshot. The scene reads, HUD is legible, nothing is black or clipped.\n- [ ] The deliverable HTML is where TASK.md says, one file, and runs on `file://` and from a server.\n- [ ] Exit interview JSON saved where TASK.md says, in its exact shape, and parses. Suggested `aiHub` fields (use your own title for `name`):\n  - tagline: `The bell is cracked. The dead are up. So are you.`\n  - description: `A gothic hack-and-slash for 1 to 4 players: smash hordes as a Bellwarden, Lamplighter or Sexton, hunt loot that rings like church bells, and silence a furious walled-up saint.`\n  - type: `Game`; genre: `RPG`; source: `Diablo 3`; series: `Diablo`; players: `1–4`\n  - controls: `Stick or WASD or click to move · Cross or click to attack · face buttons, R1, R2 or right click, 1-4 for skills · L2 or Space to dodge`\n  - tags: `3d`, `co-op`, `pixel art`, `fantasy`, `boss fights`, `top-down`\n- [ ] About shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, generated from that JSON, with real answers.\n- [ ] Your final chat reply carries the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n- [ ] Every process you started is stopped, and every file you made is inside your folder.","numLines":240,"startLine":844,"totalLines":1084}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L1cJ7UhFi6W81LTa7S1hB2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
