{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCJeENhNs91qBbRvHyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The audit turned up gaps in the plan: the Source Information fields, the 14 feedback questions, the exit interview shape, and some rules were never spelled out, and Devotion (level 30) may never appear in a story that ends near level 20. I'm reading the rest of the plan before fixing these together.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29611,"cache_read_input_tokens":449204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29611},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"03269207-b8bc-4bec-840e-d58182ce26da","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:06.075Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCJdxFatevivzzvghTd","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCJeENhNs91qBbRvHyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fz5i7hM5b35gQd7wMkpJ6y","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","offset":232,"limit":340},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29611,"cache_read_input_tokens":449204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29611},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"0e9a38ea-cd19-4f91-9d17-764fb3f663e3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:06.377Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCJdxFatevivzzvghTd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Fz5i7hM5b35gQd7wMkpJ6y":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","offset":232,"limit":340}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fz5i7hM5b35gQd7wMkpJ6y","type":"tool_result","content":"232\t## 4. Combat\n233\t\n234\t### Rules\n235\t\n236\t- **Simulation:** 60 Hz in `fixedUpdate`, on a flat world (y = 0). Hero speed 5 to 5.6 m/s, radius 0.4 m. Bodies push softly; a hero stuck for 0.3 s passes through small monsters.\n237\t- **Cast states:** wind-up, hit frame, recovery. Attack speed scales wind-up and recovery. Move input cancels the second half of recovery; dodge cancels anything. Hold a button to repeat.\n238\t- **Moving while casting:** the Lamplighter's Spark Bolt and Sexton's Bone Toss play upper-body clips over `Run` (section 2, item 17). Everything else roots the hero for its wind-up.\n239\t- **Dodge:** a 0.35 s `Roll`, 4.5 m, invulnerable throughout, 3 s cooldown (slider).\n240\t- **Potion:** infinite, heals 60%, 30 s cooldown.\n241\t- **Tallow:** kills drop it at 8% (elites always). Walking over it heals 20%.\n242\t- **Gold** flies to you inside the pick-up radius (3 m). **Items** are picked up by walking over them (inventory has 40 slots; when full, they stay on the ground with a message).\n243\t- **Telegraphs:** any attack worth more than 25% of a same-level hero's life shows a growing red ground ring or line for at least 0.6 s, with a warning sound. Dodging through it always works.\n244\t- **Requiem:** kills within 1 second of each other chain. At 10+ a banner shows the count and pays bonus XP (count × 2% of the kill XP total).\n245\t- **Death:** the candle goes out. Solo: 0.8 s of slow motion. Options: rise here (5 s wait, plus 5 s for each recent death, up to 30), last Lychgate, or town. No penalty beyond the walk. In co-op an ally revives you by holding interact for 2 s.\n246\t\n247\t### Feel recipe (apply to every hit)\n248\t\n249\tUse all of these and tune with the \"feel\" slider.\n250\t\n251\t- Target flashes: swap `mesh.material` to a shared `glowMaterial(PALETTE.white)` for 2 frames. Don't clone materials per monster.\n252\t- Knockback slide; `ctx.particles.burst` tinted by element; a pitched-up hit sound; a damage number that pops and drifts. Crits use scale 2 and `sand`.\n253\t- Big hits: `engine.shake.add(0.1 to 0.5)`, `engine.screen.shockwave(at, { radius })` on novas, `hitstop(0.04 to 0.08)` when solo or on the couch only.\n254\t- **Kills:** humanoids go into `Ragdoll` with velocity away from the hit, scaled by overkill. Keep up to 16 live ragdolls; older ones freeze and dissolve (`dissolve: true` on a per-body clone at death only). Others squash, burst and dissolve. `Decals`: small `plum` splats and `scorch`.\n255\t- **Props:** urns, barrels, crates, coffins, tombstones have HP. On break, hide the library model and do `breaks.break(breaks.add({ at, size, color, cuts }), hitAt, speed)` so chunks fly. They drop gold 40% and Tallow 5%.\n256\t- **Elements:** Sound (`sand`, `white`, expanding rings), Flame (`orange`, `red`, `sand`, a warm point light), Grave (`lime`, `plum`, smoke, a green point light). Lights use `lifetime` and priority 3; heroes 4, loot 2, torches 1.\n257\t\n258\t### Targeting\n259\t\n260\t- **Pad:** skills target softly. The best monster inside a 120° cone of facing and the skill's range gets a reticle ring. Right stick overrides aim and moves the ground reticle for ground-target skills. Melee gets a 0.6 m lunge assist.\n261\t- **Mouse:** hero faces the pointer. Left click on a monster walks into range and attacks; on an NPC or object, walks and uses it; on the ground, moves (hold to keep steering). Shift-click attacks in place. `camera.rayAt` gives the ground point (solve for y = 0); pick monsters by screen distance to their chest (14 art pixels), items by their label rectangle.\n262\t- **Keyboard:** WASD or arrows also move.\n263\t\n264\t### Classes\n265\t\n266\tEveryone has 6 slots. Slots open at levels 1, 1, 3, 6, 9, 12. Any skill can go in any slot. Swap freely out of combat (no cost, 1 s lockout on the changed slot). Each skill has an unlock level; its three Tones unlock at +2, +6 and +11 levels after it (capped at 30).\n267\t\n268\tPercentages are of weapon damage. \"Generator\" means it gives resource and costs nothing. Clips are engine clips unless marked *(new)*.\n269\t\n270\t#### The Bellwarden: melee bruiser\n271\t\n272\tA guardian of the bell-ringers' order who swings a consecrated hand-bell the size of an anvil on a chain. High life, armour +30%, speed 5.0.\n273\t\n274\t**Clangor** (0 to 100) builds on hits and drains after 4 s out of combat.\n275\t**Resonance:** every hit adds a stack to the monster (max 5, 6 s). *Toll* skills consume stacks for +25% damage each. Show stacks as small rings on the monster.\n276\t\n277\t| Skill (level) | Cost / cooldown | Clip | Effect | Tones |\n278\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n279\t| **Clout** (1) | Generator +10 | `Slash1`, `Slash2`, `Slash3` chain | 150%, 120° arc, 2.8 m | *Ringing:* chains 60% to 2 more. *Heavy:* slower, 230%, stun 0.4 s. *Pious:* heal 2% per target |\n280\t| **Chain Reap** (2) | Generator +6 per target | `Spin` once | 110% circle, 4 m | *Drag:* pulls 1.5 m. *Long Chain:* 5.5 m. *Rust:* bleed 40%/s for 3 s |\n281\t| **Great Toll** (4) | 30 Clangor, Toll | `BellOverhead` *(new)* | 300% ring, 6 m, knockback 3 m | *Twin Peal:* second ring after 0.5 s at 70%. *Cracked:* leaves shock patches 4 s. *Deaf:* 200%, stun 1 s |\n282\t| **Reverberate** (6) | 20 Clangor, Toll | `Shout` | 260% wave, cone, 9 m, passes through | *Echo:* bounces off walls once. *Narrow:* 60% narrower, 420%. *Hymn:* +3 Clangor per target |\n283\t| **Bellfall** (9) | 10 s | `LeapSlam` | Leap up to 12 m; 400%, 2 m, a bell falls with you | *Iron Bell:* leaves a taunting bell 5 s, 100%/s. *Swift:* 6 s, 250%. *Comet:* burning trail |\n284\t| **Clapper Charge** (12) | 8 s | `Charge` | Dash 10 m, 200%, shoves aside | *Battering:* stun at end. *Relentless:* kills refund 50% cooldown. *Wake:* sound trail 80%/s |\n285\t| **Hallowed Ground** (16) | 20 s | `CastBigWeapon` | 8 s ring, 7 m: allies take 30% less, heal 3%/s | *Vigil:* immune to stuns. *Ire:* +25% damage. *Procession:* follows you |\n286\t| **Last Peal** (20) | 45 s | `Spin` loop | 8 s spin: 180% per 0.25 s, 4.5 m, 20% slower, unstoppable | *Cyclone:* pulls. *Thunder:* ends with 800%. *Eternal:* kills add 0.3 s |\n287\t\n288\t**Vows (pick 2):** *Iron* (+20% armour). *Clamour* (+20 Clangor, no drain for 8 s). *Penance* (+15% damage under half life). *Silence* (kills give +15% speed for 3 s).\n289\t\n290\t#### The Lamplighter: ranged kiter\n291\t\n292\tLast of the guild that keeps night at bay. Long coat, wide hat, a lamp pole on the back. Medium life, speed 5.6.\n293\t\n294\t**Wick** (0 to 100) regenerates 14/s.\n295\t**Kindle:** Flame hits Burn (30%/s for 4 s). Burning enemies take +15% from your skills.\n296\t\n297\t| Skill (level) | Cost / cooldown | Clip | Effect | Tones |\n298\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n299\t| **Spark Bolt** (1) | Generator +4 | `CastWeapon` upper | 120% fast bolt, 18 m, Burns | *Split:* pierce 1, forks on kill. *Swift:* 1.4× speed, 90%. *Star:* arcs to 2 more |\n300\t| **Flare** (2) | 20 Wick | `Cast` | 220% cone, 8 m, monsters miss for 1.5 s | *Phosphor:* 50% wider. *Magnesium:* 340%, no blind. *Signal:* marks, allies +20% for 5 s |\n301\t| **Lantern Hurl** (4) | 30 Wick | `LanternLob` *(new)* | Lob up to 14 m: 240% in 3 m, burning pool 4 s at 60%/s | *Cluster:* 3 small. *Oil:* 8 s pool. *Blue Flame:* 40% slow |\n302\t| **Lamp Post** (6) | 12 s, max 3 | `Dig` *(new)* | Plants a lamp 15 s, fires 70% bolts twice a second | *Arc Lamp:* beams between lamps. *Bright:* heals allies in 4 m. *Bomb:* explodes 500% at the end |\n303\t| **Dusk Step** (9) | 6 s | `Roll` | Blink 8 m, ember decoy 2 s | *Double:* 2 charges. *Scorch:* 180% blast at origin. *Veil:* 2 s unseen, next hit +100% |\n304\t| **Snuff** (12) | 40 Wick | `CastBig` | All Burn within 14 m pays out at once: remaining burn × 3 | *Smother:* stun 1 s. *Relight:* re-Burns after 2 s. *Harvest:* +8 Wick per target |\n305\t| **Beacon** (16) | 25 s | `CastBigWeapon` | 10 s pillar, 7 m: allies +20% damage, +50% Wick regen; enemies inside burn 40%/s | *Walking:* follows you. *Warding:* stops projectiles. *Pyre:* ends with 600% blast |\n306\t| **Long Night's End** (20) | 50 s | `CastBig`, `Triumph` | 7 s: 3 comets a second, 220% in 2.5 m | *Meteor:* one comet, 1800%. *Drizzle:* 5 a second, weaker. *Dawn:* party heals 5%/s |\n307\t\n308\t**Vows:** *Long Wick* (+20 Wick). *Bright Eyes* (+10% crit against burning). *Keeper of Lamps* (+1 Lamp Post). *Last Light* (survive a fatal hit, once per 90 s).\n309\t\n310\t#### The Sexton: summoner and curse\n311\t\n312\tTends the graves and rings the passing bell. Stovepipe hat, black frock, spade. Raises what they bury, at union rates. Medium-high life, speed 5.2.\n313\t\n314\t**Tithe** (0 to 100) comes from generators and +3 for each nearby death.\n315\t**Graveyard Shift:** corpses remain as Graves for 12 s, and some skills consume them.\n316\t\n317\t| Skill (level) | Cost / cooldown | Clip | Effect | Tones |\n318\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n319\t| **Shovel Swat** (1) | Generator +8 | `ShovelSwat` *(new)* | 140%, arc, 2.6 m | *Spade Edge:* stun 0.3 s. *Flat Side:* slower, 180%, knockback. *Long Handle:* 3.6 m |\n320\t| **Bone Toss** (2) | Generator +5 | `Cast` upper | 110% lob, 14 m, 1.2 m burst | *Ribcage:* 3 shards. *Marrow:* poison 3 s. *Skull:* homing |\n321\t| **Raise Pallbearers** (4) | 30 Tithe, 3 s | `RaiseHands` *(new)* | Up to 4 skeleton minions, 60% each, until killed | *Coffin Crew:* 2 big ones that slam. *Quick Step:* faster. *Volatile:* explode on death |\n322\t| **Exhume** (6) | 20 Tithe | `CastBig` | Explodes up to 5 Graves within 12 m: 300% each, 3 m | *Chain:* blasts make Graves burst. *Feast:* heal 2% each. *Rise:* each leaves a 6 s skeleton |\n323\t| **Coffin Drop** (9) | 9 s | `CastWeapon` | Coffin crashes at target: 380%, 3 m, stun 1 s, stays 4 s as an obstacle | *Family Plot:* 3 coffins. *Occupied:* releases a skeleton. *Lead-Lined:* 700%, 16 s |\n324\t| **Last Rites** (12) | 30 Tithe | `Cast` | 8 s curse, 6 m: enemies take +25%; deaths inside give +6 Tithe | *Slow March:* 30% slow. *Wasting:* 60%/s. *Following:* follows the target |\n325\t| **Gravewalk** (16) | 7 s | `Roll` *(new sink)* | Sink and rise 9 m away: 150% burst, invulnerable 0.4 s | *Deep:* 2 charges. *Hands:* root 1.5 s at exit. *Whole Family:* minions come along |\n326\t| **Danse Macabre** (20) | 60 s | `Triumph` | 10 s: minions +50%, every Grave within 14 m rises, up to 12 extra skeletons | *Tarantella:* +speed. *Requiem:* all explode at the end. *Encore:* 40 s, lasts 6 s |\n327\t\n328\t**Vows:** *Union Rates* (+1 minion). *Plot Holder* (Graves last 20 s, +10% Grave damage). *Perpetual Care* (minions heal you 1% per hit). *Mourner's Due* (+2 Tithe per death).\n329\t\n330\t### Effect ops\n331\t\n332\tSkills are data, not code. `src/sim/effects.js` implements these ops and nothing else; skills and Tones only compose them:\n333\t\n334\t`arc, circle, cone, ring, projectile, lob, chain, dash, leap, blink, zone, obstacle, summon, turret, buff, debuff, pull, knock, stun, apply_status, consume_status, consume_graves, comet_rain, delay, repeat, spawn_decoy`\n335\t\n336\t```js\n337\tgreat_toll: { name: 'Great Toll', cost: 30, tags: ['toll', 'sound'], clip: 'BellOverhead', wind: 0.22, rec: 0.3,\n338\t  fx: [{ op: 'ring', radius: 6, dmg: 3.0, element: 'sound', knock: 3, consume: 'resonance', vfx: 'ring_bronze', sfx: 'bell_big', shake: 0.4 }],\n339\t  tones: { twin_peal: { name: 'Twin Peal', add: [{ op: 'delay', t: 0.5, then: { op: 'ring', radius: 6, dmg: 2.1 } }] } } }\n340\t```\n341\t\n342\t---\n343\t\n344\t## 5. Loot and progression\n345\t\n346\t### Formulas\n347\t\n348\t```text\n349\thit         = weaponDps × skill% × (1 + Power/100) × element bonus × (crit? 1.5 + critDmg) × tuning.playerDamage\n350\treduction   = armour / (armour + 50 × monsterLevel)\n351\tmonster HP  = 20 × 1.15^(L-1) × type × (1 + 0.6 × (players-1)) × difficulty × tuning.monsterHp\n352\tmonster hit = 6 × 1.12^(L-1) × type × difficulty × tuning.monsterDamage\n353\thero life   = 40 + 10 × level + 8 × Vitality\n354\tweaponDps   = 8 × 1.13^itemLevel × rarity × random(0.9, 1.1)\n355\txpToNext(L) = round(60 × L^1.75 + 40)\n356\tmonster XP  = (6 + 3 × L) × type\n357\t```\n358\t\n359\tStarting stats: Power 10, Vitality 10, plus 3 Power and 2 Vitality per level. Level cap 30, then Devotion. Monster level is the highest party level, floored by zone: Causeway 1, Ossuary 6, Cloister 11, Belfry 15. Numbers over 9,999 print as `12.4K`.\n360\t\n361\tTarget: level 18 to 22 at the credits. A trash monster dies in 1 to 2 hits at matching gear on Pilgrim.\n362\t\n363\t### Difficulty\n364\t\n365\t| Tier | Monster HP | Monster damage | XP, gold | Legendary chance | Available |\n366\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n367\t| Pilgrim | ×1 | ×1 | ×1 | ×1 | Start |\n368\t| Zealot | ×1.6 | ×1.3 | ×1.25 | ×1.2 | Start |\n369\t| Martyr | ×2.6 | ×1.7 | ×1.6 | ×1.5 | Start |\n370\t| Penance I | ×4.2 | ×2.2 | ×2 | ×2 | After the credits |\n371\t| Penance II | ×6.8 | ×2.9 | ×2.6 | ×2.6 | |\n372\t| Penance III | ×11 | ×3.8 | ×3.4 | ×3.4 | |\n373\t| Penance IV | ×18 | ×5 | ×4.5 | ×4.5 | |\n374\t| Penance V | ×29 | ×6.5 | ×6 | ×6 | |\n375\t\n376\tChange tier in town (Knell Font) or from hero select.\n377\t\n378\t### Items\n379\t\n380\t**Slots (10):** Head, Shoulders, Chest, Hands, Legs, Feet, Amulet, Ring, Main hand, Off hand.\n381\t\n382\t**Main hands:** Bellwarden: hand-bell (`mace`), war-bell (`warhammer`), chain flail (`flail`). Lamplighter: lamp staff (`staff`), hand crossbow (`crossbow`), torch wand (`wand`). Sexton: spade (`shovel`), `scythe`, grave sceptre (`sceptre`). **Off hands:** `kite-shield`, `round-shield`, lantern, censer. Weapons you hold are visible on the hero, and helm and shoulder tiers change the silhouette (section 8).\n383\t\n384\t| Rarity | Colour | Affixes | Multiplier | On the ground |\n385\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n386\t| Common | `white` | 0 | ×1 | Nothing |\n387\t| Blessed | `sky` | 1 to 2 | ×1.15 | Short beam (1.2 m) |\n388\t| Reliquary | `sand` | 3 to 4 | ×1.3 | Short beam, small light |\n389\t| Legendary | `orange` | 4 + a power | ×1.5 | 5 m beam, bell strike, floor light |\n390\t| Set | `lime` | 3 + set bonus | ×1.5 | 5 m beam, bell strike, floor light |\n391\t\n392\t**Affixes:** Power, Vitality, Armour %, Crit chance, Crit damage, Attack speed, Cooldown reduction, Cost reduction, Life per hit, Life regen, Move speed (feet only), Area damage, Sound %, Flame %, Grave %, Max resource, Gold find, Magic find, Pick-up radius, Thorns, Socket.\n393\t\n394\t**Names** come from tables, playfully: \"Mournful Cudgel of the Second Burial\", \"Soot-Blessed Hood\". Loot is personal: each player sees only their own drops and gold.\n395\t\n396\t**Drop chances** per kill: trash 12% any item; champion and rare packs always 1 to 3, with at least one Blessed. Legendary base 0.25% per trash, 6% per elite. Guaranteed legendary on first kill of the Bursar; a legendary plus a set piece on first kill of Malison. Target: 3 to 6 legendaries per campaign on Pilgrim.\n397\t\n398\t### Legendary powers\n399\t\n400\t| Item | Slot | Power |\n401\t|---|---|---|\n402\t| The Widow's Clapper | Main | Great Toll rings twice more at half strength |\n403\t| Anvil of Second Thoughts | Off | Clapper Charge drags enemies with you |\n404\t| The Deaf Verger's Cowl | Head | Immune to stuns; Resonance stacks to 8 |\n405\t| Hymnal Greaves | Legs | Chain Reap fires a homing note at each enemy hit |\n406\t| The Last Wick | Main | Spark Bolt splits into 3 when Wick is over 70 |\n407\t| Lantern of the Patient Moth | Off | Lantern Hurl pools drag enemies in |\n408\t| Snuffer's Mitts | Hands | Snuff refunds half its cost per 10 targets and resets Dusk Step |\n409\t| Cinderwalk Boots | Feet | Dusk Step leaves a burning line |\n410\t| Bishop's Second-Best Crook | Main | Pallbearers carry coffins and slam |\n411\t| Ledger of Unpaid Graves | Off | Exhume has no Grave limit, +1 Tithe per Grave |\n412\t| Spade of the First Digger | Hands | Every 5th Shovel Swat digs a Grave |\n413\t| Family Plot Deed | Chest | Coffin Drop drops 3 extra around the target |\n414\t| Plate-Lining | Amulet | Gold pickups heal 1%, and +1% damage per pickup up to 30% for 5 s |\n415\t| Ring of the Thrice-Buried | Ring | Survive a fatal hit at 30% life, once per 90 s |\n416\t| Malison's Knuckle | Ring | +25% against elites; hits on elites chain to their minions |\n417\t| Choirmaster's Baton | Off | Every 6th skill is free and deals +100% |\n418\t| Mourning Band | Ring | +5% damage per live minion or dead ally, up to 30% |\n419\t| Clemency's Shard | Amulet | Every 12 s a note rings around you: 300% in 6 m |\n420\t\n421\tImplement powers as small hook objects (`onCast`, `onHit`, `onKill`, `onPickup`, `modifySkill`). Each must visibly change play.\n422\t\n423\t### Sets (Head, Chest, Hands, Feet)\n424\t\n425\t- **Vestments of the Ringing Order (Bellwarden).** 2: Resonance stacks to 10. 4: Toll skills +300%, and each Toll takes 2 s off Bellfall.\n426\t- **Regalia of the Last Lamplighter (Lamplighter).** 2: Burn +30%. 4: Lamp Posts fire your Spark Bolt Tone at +400%.\n427\t- **Weeds of the Perpetual Mourner (Sexton).** 2: +2 Pallbearers. 4: Exhume +400%, and each Exhume heals minions.\n428\t\n429\t### Town services\n430\t\n431\t- **Pennywhistle:** buy (6 rotating items), sell, and Mystery Caskets (spend Bell Shards, pick a slot, get a random item). Price target: a Reliquary item costs about 2 minutes of the gold you earn at its level.\n432\t- **Dame Brasse:** *Salvage* items into Scrap (Common, Blessed), Dust (Reliquary), Bell Shards (Legendary, Set). *Craft:* pick slot and rarity, pay materials. *Reforge:* reroll one affix of an item, chosen by the player.\n433\t- **Mother Ogive:** *Extract* a legendary power (destroys the item). *The Reliquary* holds three extracted powers (one weapon, one armour, one jewellery), usable as if worn. *Socket* gems. *Merge* three gems into the next tier.\n434\t- **Gems (3 kinds, 3 tiers):** Ember Tear (weapon: damage %; armour: Power), Grave Salt (weapon: crit damage; armour: Vitality), Choir Amber (weapon: attack speed; armour: pick-up radius and gold).\n435\t- **The Collection Box:** a stash shared by all heroes, 3 tabs of 30.\n436\t\n437\t### Devotion\n438\t\n439\tAfter level 30, XP fills Devotion levels, shared across heroes, each costing `15000 + 1500 × n` XP. Each gives 1 point in one of four tracks: Core (Power, Vitality, Speed, Max resource), Offence (Attack speed, Crit, Crit damage, Cooldown), Defence (Life %, Armour, Regen, Reduction), Utility (Area, Cost, Life per hit, Gold). Shown as four big bars, not a table.\n440\t\n441\t---\n442\t\n443\t## 6. Monsters and bosses\n444\t\n445\tAll bodies are authored models (section 8). Elite colouring and affix glows are data.\n446\t\n447\t| Monster | Zones | HP× | Hit× | m/s | Behaviour | Body |\n448\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n449\t| **Peatwalker** | Causeway, Ossuary | 1.0 | 1.0 | 1.4 | Crowds; slow swing; bursts into mud | Humanoid, `Shamble` |\n450\t| **Gibbet Drop** | Causeway | 0.7 | 0.9 | 3.4 | Falls from gibbets, lunges | Humanoid |\n451\t| **Rattlebones** | Ossuary, Belfry | 0.8 | 1.0 | 3.2 | Fast sword; flies apart | Humanoid, empty pivots |\n452\t| **Choir Skull** | Ossuary | 0.5 | 1.1 | 2.4 | Floats 9 to 12 m away, slow \"sour note\" shots | Single mesh, hovers |\n453\t| **Pallid Bearer** | Ossuary, Cloister | 4.0 | 1.8 | 1.6 | Coffin slam (0.8 s telegraph), 2 Rattlebones on death | Big humanoid (scale 1.5) |\n454\t| **Tomb Crawler** | Ossuary | 0.4 | 0.6 | 5.0 | Swarms from breakable Nests | `LegStepper`, 6 legs |\n455\t| **Bloat Deacon** | Causeway, Ossuary | 2.0 | 2.5 (burst only) | 2.0 | Swells 1 s, bursts in 4 m, leaves a poison pool | `Squash` blob |\n456\t| **Cinderling** | Cloister, Belfry | 0.4 | 0.7 | 4.6 | Leaps in packs, fire patch on death | Small humanoid (scale 0.6) |\n457\t| **Tithe Collector** | Cloister | 1.6 | 1.2 | 2.8 | Hook pulls you from 10 m; steals gold, returned when killed | Humanoid + ledger |\n458\t| **Penitent** | Cloister, Belfry | 1.2 | 1.4 | 3.0 | Blinks in, 3-hit combo, blinks when struck | Humanoid, robed |\n459\t| **Clapperjaw** | Cloister, Belfry | 5.0 | 2.0 | 2.4 | Roar 0.9 s, charges 10 m at 7 m/s, stuns itself on walls | Big quadruped, `LegStepper` |\n460\t| **Ash Gargoyle** | Cloister, Belfry | 1.4 | 1.2 | 5.0 | Statue until close, then swoops in passes | Winged, low hover |\n461\t| **Shade Acolyte** | Cloister | 1.0 | 0.8 | 2.6 | Raises corpses every 5 s, keeps away; kill first | Humanoid |\n462\t| **The Collection Plate** | Anywhere, rare | 6.0 | 0 | 7.0 | Flees, spills gold, escapes after 12 s; jackpot if killed | Bowl on `LegStepper` |\n463\t| **Crawler Nest, Unrung Font** | Ossuary, Cloister | 8.0 | 0 | 0 | Static spawners, destructible | Prop |\n464\t\n465\t### Elites\n466\t\n467\t**Champion** packs (3 or 4, `sky` names, same Afflictions) and **Rare** packs (one `sand`-named leader with minions). Afflictions per elite: Pilgrim 1, Zealot 2, Martyr and above 3 or 4. Elites have ×4 HP, ×1.5 damage, ×8 XP. All effects are telegraphed and dodgeable.\n468\t\n469\t| Affliction | Effect |\n470\t|---|---|\n471\t| **Tolling** | Expanding shock rings from the pack, every 5 s |\n472\t| **Smouldering** | Burning trail; explodes on death after 1 s |\n473\t| **Shackled** | Chains root you for 1.5 s (telegraphed line) |\n474\t| **Entombing** | Raises walls of bone around you for 3 s |\n475\t| **Vigil Lamps** | Slow rotating beams around the pack |\n476\t| **Penitent Haste** | 40% faster, charges |\n477\t| **Undying** | Rises once at half life |\n478\t| **Plagued** | Poison pools under you |\n479\t\n480\t### Bosses\n481\t\n482\tEvery boss has a top-of-screen bar with phase ticks, a name, taunts with voice, an arena and an entrance. The target fight lengths below are at matching gear on Pilgrim.\n483\t\n484\t**The Bursar** (Ossuary, about 2 minutes). Slow, huge, ledger and abacus.\n485\t- *Audit:* marks a 5 m circle on each player, 2 s later the ledger slams.\n486\t- *Collections:* a sweep steals 10% of your gold as coins scattered on the floor. Picking them up heals you.\n487\t- *Adjustment:* summons Rattlebones \"clerks\".\n488\t- *Foreclosure* (under 30%): walls of coffins close in, shrinking the room until he dies. Melee is safest, ranged gets squeezed.\n489\t\n490\t**Bishop Ambrose Thrice-Buried** (Cloister, about 1 minute). Three short rounds. Each time he \"dies\", a coffin slams down, he's buried, and he bursts out elsewhere stronger: round 1 chains and censer, round 2 adds Penitents, round 3 a fire ring. \"ONE LEARNS TO KEEP A SPADE IN THE COFFIN.\"\n491\t\n492\t**Malison, the Unrung Saint** (Belfry top, 3 to 4 minutes). About 6 m tall, floating, wrapped in ropes, with Old Clemency hanging over a round arena.\n493\t- *Phase 1, Foundation:* rope lashes along telegraphed lines; expanding sound rings with a gap you must roll through; adds.\n494\t- *Phase 2, The Cracked Hour (60%):* floor sections crumble into pits (cells close with a telegraph). Every 15 s the bell tolls: stand behind a pillar or take huge damage (`nav.lineOfSight` from the bell's position). Pillars break after two tolls.\n495\t- *Phase 3, Eventide (25%):* the arena goes dark except the lights around heroes. She chases, slowly, and her touch is terrible. Three bell ropes hang at the rim. Interact with one (hold 2 s, she staggers each time): the bell rings true, she takes 12% and the screen shakes. Three rings end the fight, then the ending plays.\n496\t\n497\t**Knell Wardens** (Knell Runs, 90 s): *the Hollow Sexton* (Bellwarden-sized, raises graves), *the Grand Chorister* (Choir Skull swarm and rings), *Clapperjaw Prime* (charges and walls). Each is 2 phases and reuses existing bodies with new colours and scale.\n498\t\n499\t---\n500\t\n501\t## 7. Places and modes\n502\t\n503\t### Levels are data\n504\t\n505\tThe world is a flat grid with 1 m cells. `src/sim/zonegen.js` stitches ASCII room templates into a map from a seed, and the same code runs on every client:\n506\t\n507\t```text\n508\t###############      # wall       . floor      ~ water or pit (blocked, no wall)\n509\t#......L......#      D door socket   S trash spawn   E elite spawn\n510\t#..B.......B..#      C chest   B breakable   T trap   L light   A shrine\n511\tD......S......D      X entrance or exit   N named prop (from the template's list)\n512\t#...#.....#...#\n513\t#...#..E..#...#\n514\t#......C......#\n515\t#..T.......B..#\n516\t#######D#######\n517\t```\n518\t\n519\tGeneration: start at the entrance, attach templates at door sockets until the room count is met, end with the exit or boss room, seal unused sockets. Every biome has at least 8 templates plus its boss room. A test checks that `nav.path(entrance, exit)` exists for 200 seeds per zone.\n520\t\n521\tDensity: each `S` marker spawns a pack of 4 to 9 and a room has 2 to 4 markers, so 20 to 40 monsters a room. Each `E` marker has a 1 in 3 chance of an elite pack. All of it scales with the density and elite sliders.\n522\t\n523\t### Building a zone (view side)\n524\t\n525\t- **Walls:** merged boxes, not thin wall models. **A wall cell whose floor neighbour lies on its +X or +Z side is a back wall: 3 m tall. A wall on the +X or +Z edge of a room (floor neighbour on its −X or −Z side) is a front wall: a 0.6 m stub.** This is section 2 item 21, and it's what stops walls hiding the player. Tops are dark `ink` caps. Skip cells with no floor neighbour.\n526\t- **Dress the back walls** (`wall-torch`, `banner`, `wall-chains`, `column`) and floors (`bones`, `rubble`, `skull-pile`, `cobweb`). Tall props go near back walls; only low ones near front walls. Any tall prop that can come between camera and hero uses a per-prop `dissolve` material and fades when a hero is behind it.\n527\t- **Textures:** `toonMaterial(PALETTE.mist, { map: textureMap(id) })`, scale UVs to 8 texels a metre, never the map. Merge with `mergeStaticMeshes`.\n528\t- **Physics (cosmetic only):** one big floor box and merged wall boxes so ragdolls and chunks land and stop. Gameplay collision never uses Rapier.\n529\t- **Fog:** `groundFog` per biome.\n530\t\n531\t### Zones\n532\t\n533\t| Zone | Layout | Look | Monsters | Features |\n534\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n535\t| **St. Clement's Yard** | 3 authored rooms | Night, rain, `mud`, `tombstone`, `dead-tree` | Peatwalker | Tutorial, first Unquiet Coffin |\n536\t| **Tollhaven** | Authored, about 60×60 m, safe | Dusk, `cobbles`, `market-stall`, `well`, `lamp-post`, `fountain`, `statue` | None | All services, Knell Font, Writ board, Lychgate |\n537\t| **The Weeping Causeway** | Long outdoor corridor, about 200×60 m, branching | Rain (`Precipitation`), `WaterSurface` in blocked cells, `mud`, `swamp`, `willow`, `dead-tree`, `reeds`, gibbets, broken `cart` | Peatwalker, Gibbet Drop, Bloat Deacon | Wagon escort event, first Champion pack, Drowned Pantry entrance, 2 Lychgates |\n538\t| **Ossuary of Saint Gloam** | 3 floors, 8 to 12 rooms each | Floors `flagstones`, walls `ashlar`, `sarcophagus`, `coffin`, `cage`, `candles`, `altar`, `pit-grate`, `spikes`, `portcullis`, `lever` | Peatwalker, Rattlebones, Choir Skull, Pallid Bearer, Tomb Crawler, Bloat Deacon | Lever doors, floor traps, Nests, the Bursar's Counting House (coin piles, ledgers) |\n539\t| **The Cinder Cloister** | 12 rooms, part open sky | Floors `slate-tiles`, `cinders`, `lava-crust`, `ruined-wall`, `column`, `flame`, `brazier`, ember particles, falling beams | Cinderling, Tithe Collector, Penitent, Clapperjaw, Ash Gargoyle, Shade Acolyte | Defend the novices (timed event), Unrung Fonts, Ambrose in the chapter house |\n540\t| **The Cracked Belfry** | 3 short floors plus the arena | `basalt`, `rune-floor`, `rift-energy` void beyond pits, wind, the great bell | Rattlebones, Cinderling, Penitent, Clapperjaw, Gargoyle | Malison |\n541\t| **The Drowned Pantry** | 1 small floor (optional) | `shallow-water`, `barrel`, `keg`, `crate-stack` | Peatwalker, Bloat Deacon | The Cellarer mini-boss, overdue book |\n542\t\n543\t### World systems\n544\t\n545\t- **Lychgates:** roofed graveyard gates, one per floor or stretch, first touch unlocks. Travel from the Map screen when standing at one or in town.\n546\t- **Passing Bell:** hold to channel 1.5 s (a hit interrupts): a portal to town and back. Not in Knell Runs or sessions.\n547\t- **Votive Shrines:** rack of candles. One use, 30 s buff: *Ardour* (+50% damage), *Haste* (+30% speed), *Ward* (shield 30% life), *Plenty* (+100% gold).\n548\t- **Unquiet Coffin:** interact, then waves for 45 s from the ground; survive for a chest.\n549\t- **The Collection Plate:** 1 chance in 8 per zone load, 1 in 3 in Knell Runs.\n550\t- **Writs:** the Crier's board offers 3 random jobs on existing maps (kill this boss, clear this area, open this coffin). Finish all 3 for a cache. Uses the quest system with no new content.\n551\t- **Sister Pyx:** joins after quest 2 when playing solo; leaves when a second seat joins. She's a bot hero with 3 fixed skills, scales with your level, gets downed and revives after 20 s, and has 40 banter lines triggered by events.\n552\t- **Codex:** lore books, bestiary (unlocks on first kill), and **How to Play** in six big pages (Moving and fighting, Skills and Tones, Loot, Town, Knell Runs, Co-op), so a player understands what they can and can't do.\n553\t\n554\t### Knell Runs\n555\t\n556\tEntered from the **Knell Font** in town, on any difficulty.\n557\t\n558\t- **The map:** 2 floors, 12 to 18 rooms each, mixing all biomes' templates. 1 or 2 modifiers: *Crowded* (+40% density), *Swift* (+20% speed), *Haunted* (extra elites), *Golden* (+100% gold), *Dark* (only hero lights), *Volatile* (monsters explode on death).\n559\t- **The Knell meter** is a big bell-shaped gauge at top centre. Kills fill it: trash 1, big 3, champion 8, rare 12, with a total of about 450 scaled by party size.\n560\t- **At 100%:** \"THE KNELL TOLLS\": a flash, every monster flees or dies, and a Warden crashes down beside you with an arena ring of bone.\n561\t- **Rewards:** guaranteed legendary, Bell Shards, bonus XP, and a 1 in 4 chance of a Grand Key.\n562\t\n563\t**The Grand Knell:** spend a Grand Key. Pick a tier N (monster HP ×1.17^N, damage ×1.08^N). A 10-minute timer; beat it for better loot and Devotion XP. The results screen shows time, tier and your bests per class, saved locally.\n564\t\n565\t### The session round (AI Hub)\n566\t\n567\tA session is one 8-minute Knell Run for the seated players. Full details in section 12.\n568\t\n569\t---\n570\t\n571\t## 8. Art direction"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"443451a4-5c0f-4b9a-ac59-e66b4b17905a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:06.552Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 4. Combat\n\n### Rules\n\n- **Simulation:** 60 Hz in `fixedUpdate`, on a flat world (y = 0). Hero speed 5 to 5.6 m/s, radius 0.4 m. Bodies push softly; a hero stuck for 0.3 s passes through small monsters.\n- **Cast states:** wind-up, hit frame, recovery. Attack speed scales wind-up and recovery. Move input cancels the second half of recovery; dodge cancels anything. Hold a button to repeat.\n- **Moving while casting:** the Lamplighter's Spark Bolt and Sexton's Bone Toss play upper-body clips over `Run` (section 2, item 17). Everything else roots the hero for its wind-up.\n- **Dodge:** a 0.35 s `Roll`, 4.5 m, invulnerable throughout, 3 s cooldown (slider).\n- **Potion:** infinite, heals 60%, 30 s cooldown.\n- **Tallow:** kills drop it at 8% (elites always). Walking over it heals 20%.\n- **Gold** flies to you inside the pick-up radius (3 m). **Items** are picked up by walking over them (inventory has 40 slots; when full, they stay on the ground with a message).\n- **Telegraphs:** any attack worth more than 25% of a same-level hero's life shows a growing red ground ring or line for at least 0.6 s, with a warning sound. Dodging through it always works.\n- **Requiem:** kills within 1 second of each other chain. At 10+ a banner shows the count and pays bonus XP (count × 2% of the kill XP total).\n- **Death:** the candle goes out. Solo: 0.8 s of slow motion. Options: rise here (5 s wait, plus 5 s for each recent death, up to 30), last Lychgate, or town. No penalty beyond the walk. In co-op an ally revives you by holding interact for 2 s.\n\n### Feel recipe (apply to every hit)\n\nUse all of these and tune with the \"feel\" slider.\n\n- Target flashes: swap `mesh.material` to a shared `glowMaterial(PALETTE.white)` for 2 frames. Don't clone materials per monster.\n- Knockback slide; `ctx.particles.burst` tinted by element; a pitched-up hit sound; a damage number that pops and drifts. Crits use scale 2 and `sand`.\n- Big hits: `engine.shake.add(0.1 to 0.5)`, `engine.screen.shockwave(at, { radius })` on novas, `hitstop(0.04 to 0.08)` when solo or on the couch only.\n- **Kills:** humanoids go into `Ragdoll` with velocity away from the hit, scaled by overkill. Keep up to 16 live ragdolls; older ones freeze and dissolve (`dissolve: true` on a per-body clone at death only). Others squash, burst and dissolve. `Decals`: small `plum` splats and `scorch`.\n- **Props:** urns, barrels, crates, coffins, tombstones have HP. On break, hide the library model and do `breaks.break(breaks.add({ at, size, color, cuts }), hitAt, speed)` so chunks fly. They drop gold 40% and Tallow 5%.\n- **Elements:** Sound (`sand`, `white`, expanding rings), Flame (`orange`, `red`, `sand`, a warm point light), Grave (`lime`, `plum`, smoke, a green point light). Lights use `lifetime` and priority 3; heroes 4, loot 2, torches 1.\n\n### Targeting\n\n- **Pad:** skills target softly. The best monster inside a 120° cone of facing and the skill's range gets a reticle ring. Right stick overrides aim and moves the ground reticle for ground-target skills. Melee gets a 0.6 m lunge assist.\n- **Mouse:** hero faces the pointer. Left click on a monster walks into range and attacks; on an NPC or object, walks and uses it; on the ground, moves (hold to keep steering). Shift-click attacks in place. `camera.rayAt` gives the ground point (solve for y = 0); pick monsters by screen distance to their chest (14 art pixels), items by their label rectangle.\n- **Keyboard:** WASD or arrows also move.\n\n### Classes\n\nEveryone has 6 slots. Slots open at levels 1, 1, 3, 6, 9, 12. Any skill can go in any slot. Swap freely out of combat (no cost, 1 s lockout on the changed slot). Each skill has an unlock level; its three Tones unlock at +2, +6 and +11 levels after it (capped at 30).\n\nPercentages are of weapon damage. \"Generator\" means it gives resource and costs nothing. Clips are engine clips unless marked *(new)*.\n\n#### The Bellwarden: melee bruiser\n\nA guardian of the bell-ringers' order who swings a consecrated hand-bell the size of an anvil on a chain. High life, armour +30%, speed 5.0.\n\n**Clangor** (0 to 100) builds on hits and drains after 4 s out of combat.\n**Resonance:** every hit adds a stack to the monster (max 5, 6 s). *Toll* skills consume stacks for +25% damage each. Show stacks as small rings on the monster.\n\n| Skill (level) | Cost / cooldown | Clip | Effect | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Clout** (1) | Generator +10 | `Slash1`, `Slash2`, `Slash3` chain | 150%, 120° arc, 2.8 m | *Ringing:* chains 60% to 2 more. *Heavy:* slower, 230%, stun 0.4 s. *Pious:* heal 2% per target |\n| **Chain Reap** (2) | Generator +6 per target | `Spin` once | 110% circle, 4 m | *Drag:* pulls 1.5 m. *Long Chain:* 5.5 m. *Rust:* bleed 40%/s for 3 s |\n| **Great Toll** (4) | 30 Clangor, Toll | `BellOverhead` *(new)* | 300% ring, 6 m, knockback 3 m | *Twin Peal:* second ring after 0.5 s at 70%. *Cracked:* leaves shock patches 4 s. *Deaf:* 200%, stun 1 s |\n| **Reverberate** (6) | 20 Clangor, Toll | `Shout` | 260% wave, cone, 9 m, passes through | *Echo:* bounces off walls once. *Narrow:* 60% narrower, 420%. *Hymn:* +3 Clangor per target |\n| **Bellfall** (9) | 10 s | `LeapSlam` | Leap up to 12 m; 400%, 2 m, a bell falls with you | *Iron Bell:* leaves a taunting bell 5 s, 100%/s. *Swift:* 6 s, 250%. *Comet:* burning trail |\n| **Clapper Charge** (12) | 8 s | `Charge` | Dash 10 m, 200%, shoves aside | *Battering:* stun at end. *Relentless:* kills refund 50% cooldown. *Wake:* sound trail 80%/s |\n| **Hallowed Ground** (16) | 20 s | `CastBigWeapon` | 8 s ring, 7 m: allies take 30% less, heal 3%/s | *Vigil:* immune to stuns. *Ire:* +25% damage. *Procession:* follows you |\n| **Last Peal** (20) | 45 s | `Spin` loop | 8 s spin: 180% per 0.25 s, 4.5 m, 20% slower, unstoppable | *Cyclone:* pulls. *Thunder:* ends with 800%. *Eternal:* kills add 0.3 s |\n\n**Vows (pick 2):** *Iron* (+20% armour). *Clamour* (+20 Clangor, no drain for 8 s). *Penance* (+15% damage under half life). *Silence* (kills give +15% speed for 3 s).\n\n#### The Lamplighter: ranged kiter\n\nLast of the guild that keeps night at bay. Long coat, wide hat, a lamp pole on the back. Medium life, speed 5.6.\n\n**Wick** (0 to 100) regenerates 14/s.\n**Kindle:** Flame hits Burn (30%/s for 4 s). Burning enemies take +15% from your skills.\n\n| Skill (level) | Cost / cooldown | Clip | Effect | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Spark Bolt** (1) | Generator +4 | `CastWeapon` upper | 120% fast bolt, 18 m, Burns | *Split:* pierce 1, forks on kill. *Swift:* 1.4× speed, 90%. *Star:* arcs to 2 more |\n| **Flare** (2) | 20 Wick | `Cast` | 220% cone, 8 m, monsters miss for 1.5 s | *Phosphor:* 50% wider. *Magnesium:* 340%, no blind. *Signal:* marks, allies +20% for 5 s |\n| **Lantern Hurl** (4) | 30 Wick | `LanternLob` *(new)* | Lob up to 14 m: 240% in 3 m, burning pool 4 s at 60%/s | *Cluster:* 3 small. *Oil:* 8 s pool. *Blue Flame:* 40% slow |\n| **Lamp Post** (6) | 12 s, max 3 | `Dig` *(new)* | Plants a lamp 15 s, fires 70% bolts twice a second | *Arc Lamp:* beams between lamps. *Bright:* heals allies in 4 m. *Bomb:* explodes 500% at the end |\n| **Dusk Step** (9) | 6 s | `Roll` | Blink 8 m, ember decoy 2 s | *Double:* 2 charges. *Scorch:* 180% blast at origin. *Veil:* 2 s unseen, next hit +100% |\n| **Snuff** (12) | 40 Wick | `CastBig` | All Burn within 14 m pays out at once: remaining burn × 3 | *Smother:* stun 1 s. *Relight:* re-Burns after 2 s. *Harvest:* +8 Wick per target |\n| **Beacon** (16) | 25 s | `CastBigWeapon` | 10 s pillar, 7 m: allies +20% damage, +50% Wick regen; enemies inside burn 40%/s | *Walking:* follows you. *Warding:* stops projectiles. *Pyre:* ends with 600% blast |\n| **Long Night's End** (20) | 50 s | `CastBig`, `Triumph` | 7 s: 3 comets a second, 220% in 2.5 m | *Meteor:* one comet, 1800%. *Drizzle:* 5 a second, weaker. *Dawn:* party heals 5%/s |\n\n**Vows:** *Long Wick* (+20 Wick). *Bright Eyes* (+10% crit against burning). *Keeper of Lamps* (+1 Lamp Post). *Last Light* (survive a fatal hit, once per 90 s).\n\n#### The Sexton: summoner and curse\n\nTends the graves and rings the passing bell. Stovepipe hat, black frock, spade. Raises what they bury, at union rates. Medium-high life, speed 5.2.\n\n**Tithe** (0 to 100) comes from generators and +3 for each nearby death.\n**Graveyard Shift:** corpses remain as Graves for 12 s, and some skills consume them.\n\n| Skill (level) | Cost / cooldown | Clip | Effect | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Shovel Swat** (1) | Generator +8 | `ShovelSwat` *(new)* | 140%, arc, 2.6 m | *Spade Edge:* stun 0.3 s. *Flat Side:* slower, 180%, knockback. *Long Handle:* 3.6 m |\n| **Bone Toss** (2) | Generator +5 | `Cast` upper | 110% lob, 14 m, 1.2 m burst | *Ribcage:* 3 shards. *Marrow:* poison 3 s. *Skull:* homing |\n| **Raise Pallbearers** (4) | 30 Tithe, 3 s | `RaiseHands` *(new)* | Up to 4 skeleton minions, 60% each, until killed | *Coffin Crew:* 2 big ones that slam. *Quick Step:* faster. *Volatile:* explode on death |\n| **Exhume** (6) | 20 Tithe | `CastBig` | Explodes up to 5 Graves within 12 m: 300% each, 3 m | *Chain:* blasts make Graves burst. *Feast:* heal 2% each. *Rise:* each leaves a 6 s skeleton |\n| **Coffin Drop** (9) | 9 s | `CastWeapon` | Coffin crashes at target: 380%, 3 m, stun 1 s, stays 4 s as an obstacle | *Family Plot:* 3 coffins. *Occupied:* releases a skeleton. *Lead-Lined:* 700%, 16 s |\n| **Last Rites** (12) | 30 Tithe | `Cast` | 8 s curse, 6 m: enemies take +25%; deaths inside give +6 Tithe | *Slow March:* 30% slow. *Wasting:* 60%/s. *Following:* follows the target |\n| **Gravewalk** (16) | 7 s | `Roll` *(new sink)* | Sink and rise 9 m away: 150% burst, invulnerable 0.4 s | *Deep:* 2 charges. *Hands:* root 1.5 s at exit. *Whole Family:* minions come along |\n| **Danse Macabre** (20) | 60 s | `Triumph` | 10 s: minions +50%, every Grave within 14 m rises, up to 12 extra skeletons | *Tarantella:* +speed. *Requiem:* all explode at the end. *Encore:* 40 s, lasts 6 s |\n\n**Vows:** *Union Rates* (+1 minion). *Plot Holder* (Graves last 20 s, +10% Grave damage). *Perpetual Care* (minions heal you 1% per hit). *Mourner's Due* (+2 Tithe per death).\n\n### Effect ops\n\nSkills are data, not code. `src/sim/effects.js` implements these ops and nothing else; skills and Tones only compose them:\n\n`arc, circle, cone, ring, projectile, lob, chain, dash, leap, blink, zone, obstacle, summon, turret, buff, debuff, pull, knock, stun, apply_status, consume_status, consume_graves, comet_rain, delay, repeat, spawn_decoy`\n\n```js\ngreat_toll: { name: 'Great Toll', cost: 30, tags: ['toll', 'sound'], clip: 'BellOverhead', wind: 0.22, rec: 0.3,\n  fx: [{ op: 'ring', radius: 6, dmg: 3.0, element: 'sound', knock: 3, consume: 'resonance', vfx: 'ring_bronze', sfx: 'bell_big', shake: 0.4 }],\n  tones: { twin_peal: { name: 'Twin Peal', add: [{ op: 'delay', t: 0.5, then: { op: 'ring', radius: 6, dmg: 2.1 } }] } } }\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Loot and progression\n\n### Formulas\n\n```text\nhit         = weaponDps × skill% × (1 + Power/100) × element bonus × (crit? 1.5 + critDmg) × tuning.playerDamage\nreduction   = armour / (armour + 50 × monsterLevel)\nmonster HP  = 20 × 1.15^(L-1) × type × (1 + 0.6 × (players-1)) × difficulty × tuning.monsterHp\nmonster hit = 6 × 1.12^(L-1) × type × difficulty × tuning.monsterDamage\nhero life   = 40 + 10 × level + 8 × Vitality\nweaponDps   = 8 × 1.13^itemLevel × rarity × random(0.9, 1.1)\nxpToNext(L) = round(60 × L^1.75 + 40)\nmonster XP  = (6 + 3 × L) × type\n```\n\nStarting stats: Power 10, Vitality 10, plus 3 Power and 2 Vitality per level. Level cap 30, then Devotion. Monster level is the highest party level, floored by zone: Causeway 1, Ossuary 6, Cloister 11, Belfry 15. Numbers over 9,999 print as `12.4K`.\n\nTarget: level 18 to 22 at the credits. A trash monster dies in 1 to 2 hits at matching gear on Pilgrim.\n\n### Difficulty\n\n| Tier | Monster HP | Monster damage | XP, gold | Legendary chance | Available |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pilgrim | ×1 | ×1 | ×1 | ×1 | Start |\n| Zealot | ×1.6 | ×1.3 | ×1.25 | ×1.2 | Start |\n| Martyr | ×2.6 | ×1.7 | ×1.6 | ×1.5 | Start |\n| Penance I | ×4.2 | ×2.2 | ×2 | ×2 | After the credits |\n| Penance II | ×6.8 | ×2.9 | ×2.6 | ×2.6 | |\n| Penance III | ×11 | ×3.8 | ×3.4 | ×3.4 | |\n| Penance IV | ×18 | ×5 | ×4.5 | ×4.5 | |\n| Penance V | ×29 | ×6.5 | ×6 | ×6 | |\n\nChange tier in town (Knell Font) or from hero select.\n\n### Items\n\n**Slots (10):** Head, Shoulders, Chest, Hands, Legs, Feet, Amulet, Ring, Main hand, Off hand.\n\n**Main hands:** Bellwarden: hand-bell (`mace`), war-bell (`warhammer`), chain flail (`flail`). Lamplighter: lamp staff (`staff`), hand crossbow (`crossbow`), torch wand (`wand`). Sexton: spade (`shovel`), `scythe`, grave sceptre (`sceptre`). **Off hands:** `kite-shield`, `round-shield`, lantern, censer. Weapons you hold are visible on the hero, and helm and shoulder tiers change the silhouette (section 8).\n\n| Rarity | Colour | Affixes | Multiplier | On the ground |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Common | `white` | 0 | ×1 | Nothing |\n| Blessed | `sky` | 1 to 2 | ×1.15 | Short beam (1.2 m) |\n| Reliquary | `sand` | 3 to 4 | ×1.3 | Short beam, small light |\n| Legendary | `orange` | 4 + a power | ×1.5 | 5 m beam, bell strike, floor light |\n| Set | `lime` | 3 + set bonus | ×1.5 | 5 m beam, bell strike, floor light |\n\n**Affixes:** Power, Vitality, Armour %, Crit chance, Crit damage, Attack speed, Cooldown reduction, Cost reduction, Life per hit, Life regen, Move speed (feet only), Area damage, Sound %, Flame %, Grave %, Max resource, Gold find, Magic find, Pick-up radius, Thorns, Socket.\n\n**Names** come from tables, playfully: \"Mournful Cudgel of the Second Burial\", \"Soot-Blessed Hood\". Loot is personal: each player sees only their own drops and gold.\n\n**Drop chances** per kill: trash 12% any item; champion and rare packs always 1 to 3, with at least one Blessed. Legendary base 0.25% per trash, 6% per elite. Guaranteed legendary on first kill of the Bursar; a legendary plus a set piece on first kill of Malison. Target: 3 to 6 legendaries per campaign on Pilgrim.\n\n### Legendary powers\n\n| Item | Slot | Power |\n|---|---|---|\n| The Widow's Clapper | Main | Great Toll rings twice more at half strength |\n| Anvil of Second Thoughts | Off | Clapper Charge drags enemies with you |\n| The Deaf Verger's Cowl | Head | Immune to stuns; Resonance stacks to 8 |\n| Hymnal Greaves | Legs | Chain Reap fires a homing note at each enemy hit |\n| The Last Wick | Main | Spark Bolt splits into 3 when Wick is over 70 |\n| Lantern of the Patient Moth | Off | Lantern Hurl pools drag enemies in |\n| Snuffer's Mitts | Hands | Snuff refunds half its cost per 10 targets and resets Dusk Step |\n| Cinderwalk Boots | Feet | Dusk Step leaves a burning line |\n| Bishop's Second-Best Crook | Main | Pallbearers carry coffins and slam |\n| Ledger of Unpaid Graves | Off | Exhume has no Grave limit, +1 Tithe per Grave |\n| Spade of the First Digger | Hands | Every 5th Shovel Swat digs a Grave |\n| Family Plot Deed | Chest | Coffin Drop drops 3 extra around the target |\n| Plate-Lining | Amulet | Gold pickups heal 1%, and +1% damage per pickup up to 30% for 5 s |\n| Ring of the Thrice-Buried | Ring | Survive a fatal hit at 30% life, once per 90 s |\n| Malison's Knuckle | Ring | +25% against elites; hits on elites chain to their minions |\n| Choirmaster's Baton | Off | Every 6th skill is free and deals +100% |\n| Mourning Band | Ring | +5% damage per live minion or dead ally, up to 30% |\n| Clemency's Shard | Amulet | Every 12 s a note rings around you: 300% in 6 m |\n\nImplement powers as small hook objects (`onCast`, `onHit`, `onKill`, `onPickup`, `modifySkill`). Each must visibly change play.\n\n### Sets (Head, Chest, Hands, Feet)\n\n- **Vestments of the Ringing Order (Bellwarden).** 2: Resonance stacks to 10. 4: Toll skills +300%, and each Toll takes 2 s off Bellfall.\n- **Regalia of the Last Lamplighter (Lamplighter).** 2: Burn +30%. 4: Lamp Posts fire your Spark Bolt Tone at +400%.\n- **Weeds of the Perpetual Mourner (Sexton).** 2: +2 Pallbearers. 4: Exhume +400%, and each Exhume heals minions.\n\n### Town services\n\n- **Pennywhistle:** buy (6 rotating items), sell, and Mystery Caskets (spend Bell Shards, pick a slot, get a random item). Price target: a Reliquary item costs about 2 minutes of the gold you earn at its level.\n- **Dame Brasse:** *Salvage* items into Scrap (Common, Blessed), Dust (Reliquary), Bell Shards (Legendary, Set). *Craft:* pick slot and rarity, pay materials. *Reforge:* reroll one affix of an item, chosen by the player.\n- **Mother Ogive:** *Extract* a legendary power (destroys the item). *The Reliquary* holds three extracted powers (one weapon, one armour, one jewellery), usable as if worn. *Socket* gems. *Merge* three gems into the next tier.\n- **Gems (3 kinds, 3 tiers):** Ember Tear (weapon: damage %; armour: Power), Grave Salt (weapon: crit damage; armour: Vitality), Choir Amber (weapon: attack speed; armour: pick-up radius and gold).\n- **The Collection Box:** a stash shared by all heroes, 3 tabs of 30.\n\n### Devotion\n\nAfter level 30, XP fills Devotion levels, shared across heroes, each costing `15000 + 1500 × n` XP. Each gives 1 point in one of four tracks: Core (Power, Vitality, Speed, Max resource), Offence (Attack speed, Crit, Crit damage, Cooldown), Defence (Life %, Armour, Regen, Reduction), Utility (Area, Cost, Life per hit, Gold). Shown as four big bars, not a table.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Monsters and bosses\n\nAll bodies are authored models (section 8). Elite colouring and affix glows are data.\n\n| Monster | Zones | HP× | Hit× | m/s | Behaviour | Body |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Peatwalker** | Causeway, Ossuary | 1.0 | 1.0 | 1.4 | Crowds; slow swing; bursts into mud | Humanoid, `Shamble` |\n| **Gibbet Drop** | Causeway | 0.7 | 0.9 | 3.4 | Falls from gibbets, lunges | Humanoid |\n| **Rattlebones** | Ossuary, Belfry | 0.8 | 1.0 | 3.2 | Fast sword; flies apart | Humanoid, empty pivots |\n| **Choir Skull** | Ossuary | 0.5 | 1.1 | 2.4 | Floats 9 to 12 m away, slow \"sour note\" shots | Single mesh, hovers |\n| **Pallid Bearer** | Ossuary, Cloister | 4.0 | 1.8 | 1.6 | Coffin slam (0.8 s telegraph), 2 Rattlebones on death | Big humanoid (scale 1.5) |\n| **Tomb Crawler** | Ossuary | 0.4 | 0.6 | 5.0 | Swarms from breakable Nests | `LegStepper`, 6 legs |\n| **Bloat Deacon** | Causeway, Ossuary | 2.0 | 2.5 (burst only) | 2.0 | Swells 1 s, bursts in 4 m, leaves a poison pool | `Squash` blob |\n| **Cinderling** | Cloister, Belfry | 0.4 | 0.7 | 4.6 | Leaps in packs, fire patch on death | Small humanoid (scale 0.6) |\n| **Tithe Collector** | Cloister | 1.6 | 1.2 | 2.8 | Hook pulls you from 10 m; steals gold, returned when killed | Humanoid + ledger |\n| **Penitent** | Cloister, Belfry | 1.2 | 1.4 | 3.0 | Blinks in, 3-hit combo, blinks when struck | Humanoid, robed |\n| **Clapperjaw** | Cloister, Belfry | 5.0 | 2.0 | 2.4 | Roar 0.9 s, charges 10 m at 7 m/s, stuns itself on walls | Big quadruped, `LegStepper` |\n| **Ash Gargoyle** | Cloister, Belfry | 1.4 | 1.2 | 5.0 | Statue until close, then swoops in passes | Winged, low hover |\n| **Shade Acolyte** | Cloister | 1.0 | 0.8 | 2.6 | Raises corpses every 5 s, keeps away; kill first | Humanoid |\n| **The Collection Plate** | Anywhere, rare | 6.0 | 0 | 7.0 | Flees, spills gold, escapes after 12 s; jackpot if killed | Bowl on `LegStepper` |\n| **Crawler Nest, Unrung Font** | Ossuary, Cloister | 8.0 | 0 | 0 | Static spawners, destructible | Prop |\n\n### Elites\n\n**Champion** packs (3 or 4, `sky` names, same Afflictions) and **Rare** packs (one `sand`-named leader with minions). Afflictions per elite: Pilgrim 1, Zealot 2, Martyr and above 3 or 4. Elites have ×4 HP, ×1.5 damage, ×8 XP. All effects are telegraphed and dodgeable.\n\n| Affliction | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| **Tolling** | Expanding shock rings from the pack, every 5 s |\n| **Smouldering** | Burning trail; explodes on death after 1 s |\n| **Shackled** | Chains root you for 1.5 s (telegraphed line) |\n| **Entombing** | Raises walls of bone around you for 3 s |\n| **Vigil Lamps** | Slow rotating beams around the pack |\n| **Penitent Haste** | 40% faster, charges |\n| **Undying** | Rises once at half life |\n| **Plagued** | Poison pools under you |\n\n### Bosses\n\nEvery boss has a top-of-screen bar with phase ticks, a name, taunts with voice, an arena and an entrance. The target fight lengths below are at matching gear on Pilgrim.\n\n**The Bursar** (Ossuary, about 2 minutes). Slow, huge, ledger and abacus.\n- *Audit:* marks a 5 m circle on each player, 2 s later the ledger slams.\n- *Collections:* a sweep steals 10% of your gold as coins scattered on the floor. Picking them up heals you.\n- *Adjustment:* summons Rattlebones \"clerks\".\n- *Foreclosure* (under 30%): walls of coffins close in, shrinking the room until he dies. Melee is safest, ranged gets squeezed.\n\n**Bishop Ambrose Thrice-Buried** (Cloister, about 1 minute). Three short rounds. Each time he \"dies\", a coffin slams down, he's buried, and he bursts out elsewhere stronger: round 1 chains and censer, round 2 adds Penitents, round 3 a fire ring. \"ONE LEARNS TO KEEP A SPADE IN THE COFFIN.\"\n\n**Malison, the Unrung Saint** (Belfry top, 3 to 4 minutes). About 6 m tall, floating, wrapped in ropes, with Old Clemency hanging over a round arena.\n- *Phase 1, Foundation:* rope lashes along telegraphed lines; expanding sound rings with a gap you must roll through; adds.\n- *Phase 2, The Cracked Hour (60%):* floor sections crumble into pits (cells close with a telegraph). Every 15 s the bell tolls: stand behind a pillar or take huge damage (`nav.lineOfSight` from the bell's position). Pillars break after two tolls.\n- *Phase 3, Eventide (25%):* the arena goes dark except the lights around heroes. She chases, slowly, and her touch is terrible. Three bell ropes hang at the rim. Interact with one (hold 2 s, she staggers each time): the bell rings true, she takes 12% and the screen shakes. Three rings end the fight, then the ending plays.\n\n**Knell Wardens** (Knell Runs, 90 s): *the Hollow Sexton* (Bellwarden-sized, raises graves), *the Grand Chorister* (Choir Skull swarm and rings), *Clapperjaw Prime* (charges and walls). Each is 2 phases and reuses existing bodies with new colours and scale.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Places and modes\n\n### Levels are data\n\nThe world is a flat grid with 1 m cells. `src/sim/zonegen.js` stitches ASCII room templates into a map from a seed, and the same code runs on every client:\n\n```text\n###############      # wall       . floor      ~ water or pit (blocked, no wall)\n#......L......#      D door socket   S trash spawn   E elite spawn\n#..B.......B..#      C chest   B breakable   T trap   L light   A shrine\nD......S......D      X entrance or exit   N named prop (from the template's list)\n#...#.....#...#\n#...#..E..#...#\n#......C......#\n#..T.......B..#\n#######D#######\n```\n\nGeneration: start at the entrance, attach templates at door sockets until the room count is met, end with the exit or boss room, seal unused sockets. Every biome has at least 8 templates plus its boss room. A test checks that `nav.path(entrance, exit)` exists for 200 seeds per zone.\n\nDensity: each `S` marker spawns a pack of 4 to 9 and a room has 2 to 4 markers, so 20 to 40 monsters a room. Each `E` marker has a 1 in 3 chance of an elite pack. All of it scales with the density and elite sliders.\n\n### Building a zone (view side)\n\n- **Walls:** merged boxes, not thin wall models. **A wall cell whose floor neighbour lies on its +X or +Z side is a back wall: 3 m tall. A wall on the +X or +Z edge of a room (floor neighbour on its −X or −Z side) is a front wall: a 0.6 m stub.** This is section 2 item 21, and it's what stops walls hiding the player. Tops are dark `ink` caps. Skip cells with no floor neighbour.\n- **Dress the back walls** (`wall-torch`, `banner`, `wall-chains`, `column`) and floors (`bones`, `rubble`, `skull-pile`, `cobweb`). Tall props go near back walls; only low ones near front walls. Any tall prop that can come between camera and hero uses a per-prop `dissolve` material and fades when a hero is behind it.\n- **Textures:** `toonMaterial(PALETTE.mist, { map: textureMap(id) })`, scale UVs to 8 texels a metre, never the map. Merge with `mergeStaticMeshes`.\n- **Physics (cosmetic only):** one big floor box and merged wall boxes so ragdolls and chunks land and stop. Gameplay collision never uses Rapier.\n- **Fog:** `groundFog` per biome.\n\n### Zones\n\n| Zone | Layout | Look | Monsters | Features |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **St. Clement's Yard** | 3 authored rooms | Night, rain, `mud`, `tombstone`, `dead-tree` | Peatwalker | Tutorial, first Unquiet Coffin |\n| **Tollhaven** | Authored, about 60×60 m, safe | Dusk, `cobbles`, `market-stall`, `well`, `lamp-post`, `fountain`, `statue` | None | All services, Knell Font, Writ board, Lychgate |\n| **The Weeping Causeway** | Long outdoor corridor, about 200×60 m, branching | Rain (`Precipitation`), `WaterSurface` in blocked cells, `mud`, `swamp`, `willow`, `dead-tree`, `reeds`, gibbets, broken `cart` | Peatwalker, Gibbet Drop, Bloat Deacon | Wagon escort event, first Champion pack, Drowned Pantry entrance, 2 Lychgates |\n| **Ossuary of Saint Gloam** | 3 floors, 8 to 12 rooms each | Floors `flagstones`, walls `ashlar`, `sarcophagus`, `coffin`, `cage`, `candles`, `altar`, `pit-grate`, `spikes`, `portcullis`, `lever` | Peatwalker, Rattlebones, Choir Skull, Pallid Bearer, Tomb Crawler, Bloat Deacon | Lever doors, floor traps, Nests, the Bursar's Counting House (coin piles, ledgers) |\n| **The Cinder Cloister** | 12 rooms, part open sky | Floors `slate-tiles`, `cinders`, `lava-crust`, `ruined-wall`, `column`, `flame`, `brazier`, ember particles, falling beams | Cinderling, Tithe Collector, Penitent, Clapperjaw, Ash Gargoyle, Shade Acolyte | Defend the novices (timed event), Unrung Fonts, Ambrose in the chapter house |\n| **The Cracked Belfry** | 3 short floors plus the arena | `basalt`, `rune-floor`, `rift-energy` void beyond pits, wind, the great bell | Rattlebones, Cinderling, Penitent, Clapperjaw, Gargoyle | Malison |\n| **The Drowned Pantry** | 1 small floor (optional) | `shallow-water`, `barrel`, `keg`, `crate-stack` | Peatwalker, Bloat Deacon | The Cellarer mini-boss, overdue book |\n\n### World systems\n\n- **Lychgates:** roofed graveyard gates, one per floor or stretch, first touch unlocks. Travel from the Map screen when standing at one or in town.\n- **Passing Bell:** hold to channel 1.5 s (a hit interrupts): a portal to town and back. Not in Knell Runs or sessions.\n- **Votive Shrines:** rack of candles. One use, 30 s buff: *Ardour* (+50% damage), *Haste* (+30% speed), *Ward* (shield 30% life), *Plenty* (+100% gold).\n- **Unquiet Coffin:** interact, then waves for 45 s from the ground; survive for a chest.\n- **The Collection Plate:** 1 chance in 8 per zone load, 1 in 3 in Knell Runs.\n- **Writs:** the Crier's board offers 3 random jobs on existing maps (kill this boss, clear this area, open this coffin). Finish all 3 for a cache. Uses the quest system with no new content.\n- **Sister Pyx:** joins after quest 2 when playing solo; leaves when a second seat joins. She's a bot hero with 3 fixed skills, scales with your level, gets downed and revives after 20 s, and has 40 banter lines triggered by events.\n- **Codex:** lore books, bestiary (unlocks on first kill), and **How to Play** in six big pages (Moving and fighting, Skills and Tones, Loot, Town, Knell Runs, Co-op), so a player understands what they can and can't do.\n\n### Knell Runs\n\nEntered from the **Knell Font** in town, on any difficulty.\n\n- **The map:** 2 floors, 12 to 18 rooms each, mixing all biomes' templates. 1 or 2 modifiers: *Crowded* (+40% density), *Swift* (+20% speed), *Haunted* (extra elites), *Golden* (+100% gold), *Dark* (only hero lights), *Volatile* (monsters explode on death).\n- **The Knell meter** is a big bell-shaped gauge at top centre. Kills fill it: trash 1, big 3, champion 8, rare 12, with a total of about 450 scaled by party size.\n- **At 100%:** \"THE KNELL TOLLS\": a flash, every monster flees or dies, and a Warden crashes down beside you with an arena ring of bone.\n- **Rewards:** guaranteed legendary, Bell Shards, bonus XP, and a 1 in 4 chance of a Grand Key.\n\n**The Grand Knell:** spend a Grand Key. Pick a tier N (monster HP ×1.17^N, damage ×1.08^N). A 10-minute timer; beat it for better loot and Devotion XP. The results screen shows time, tier and your bests per class, saved locally.\n\n### The session round (AI Hub)\n\nA session is one 8-minute Knell Run for the seated players. Full details in section 12.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art direction","numLines":340,"startLine":232,"totalLines":1084}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fz5i7hM5b35gQd7wMkpJ6y","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCJeENhNs91qBbRvHyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vi1WpuRqjAy9qhhhFwyg2J","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","offset":571,"limit":273},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29611,"cache_read_input_tokens":449204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29611},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"c1da0f65-16e8-48df-a298-122aa3d65c1b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:07.710Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCJdxFatevivzzvghTd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Vi1WpuRqjAy9qhhhFwyg2J":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","offset":571,"limit":273}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vi1WpuRqjAy9qhhhFwyg2J","type":"tool_result","content":"571\t## 8. Art direction\n572\t\n573\t**Base:** the engine's native look (`LOOK_PRESETS.none`: 3D low-poly toon rendered as pixel art, Sweetie 16 palette), with a soft vignette (`scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: 0.3 } }]`). Raise the vignette at low life. Everything is palette colours on `toonMaterial`, chunky shapes (0.12 m or more for anything that carries the silhouette), rules from `ASSETS.md` section 4. Tag every actor with `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`.\n574\t\n575\t**Style target:** dark gothic dioramas lit by fire. Deep `ink`, `night`, `navy`, `plum` environments; warm pools of light; saturated accents on anything that matters. The player should always find the hero, the danger and the loot within a second.\n576\t\n577\t**Biome palettes:** Yard and Causeway: `night`, `slate`, `teal`, cold `sky` sun. Town: `plum`, `sand`, warm lamps. Ossuary: `night`, `mist` bone, green and candle lights. Cloister: `ink`, `red`, `orange`, firelight everywhere. Belfry: `navy`, `cyan` crackle, `white` lightning, `rift-energy` beyond the edges.\n578\t\n579\t### The body template (verified)\n580\t\n581\t```js\n582\tconst j = (name, at, kids = []) => ({ group: kids, name, pivot: true, at });\n583\t// Positions are HERO_RIG's rest layout: keep the pivots, change the shapes between them.\n584\tconst humanoid = ({ hips, chest, head, upperArm, foreArm, handR = [], handL = [], thigh, shin, foot }) => [\n585\t  j('Pelvis', [0, 0.62, 0], [...hips,\n586\t    j('Torso', [0, 0.05, 0], [...chest,\n587\t      j('Head', [0, 0.5, 0], head),\n588\t      j('ArmR', [-0.27, 0.42, 0], [...upperArm, j('ForearmR', [0, -0.25, 0], [...foreArm, j('HandR', [0, -0.16, 0], handR)])]),\n589\t      j('ArmL', [0.27, 0.42, 0], [...upperArm, j('ForearmL', [0, -0.25, 0], [...foreArm, j('HandL', [0, -0.16, 0], handL)])]),\n590\t    ]),\n591\t    j('LegR', [-0.14, 0, 0], [...thigh, j('ShinR', [0, -0.3, 0], [...shin, j('FootR', [0, -0.22, 0], foot)])]),\n592\t    j('LegL', [0.14, 0, 0], [...thigh, j('ShinL', [0, -0.3, 0], [...shin, j('FootL', [0, -0.22, 0], foot)])]),\n593\t  ]),\n594\t];\n595\t```\n596\t\n597\tShapes hang below their pivot (`{ box: [0.13, 0.25, 0.13], at: [0, -0.125, 0], c: 'robe' }`). Pass `[]` for any piece a body doesn't need. A weapon inside `HandR` uses `{ use: 'mace', at: [0, -0.35, 0.1], rot: [90, 0, 0] }`, or at runtime `root.getObjectByName('HandR').add(buildModel(id).object)`. Recolour with `buildModel(id, { palette: { robe: 'navy' }, catalog })`. Keep cheap monsters to about 4 palette slots, since each makes meshes per pivot.\n598\t\n599\t### Asset list\n600\t\n601\tPut each in a `src/view/models/*.js` module of plain exports with no engine start, and check with `node check.mjs --sheets src/view/models/x.js`.\n602\t\n603\t- **Heroes (3 bodies, each with 3 armour tiers by level and rarity):**\n604\t  - **Bellwarden:** square shoulders, cowl, bronze trim (`plum`, `orange`), a huge bell on a chain as the weapon, with a `SpringChain` swinging at runtime.\n605\t  - **Lamplighter:** wide-brim hat, long coat (`navy`, `sand`), lamp pole on the back with a `glow` lantern and its own point light.\n606\t  - **Sexton:** stovepipe hat, black frock, grey face (`ink`, `lime` accent), spade.\n607\t  - Helm and shoulder sub-models attach to joints and change with worn gear. A seat-coloured ground ring appears in co-op.\n608\t- **NPCs (6):** the Crier's lantern on a post; Dame Brasse (wide, apron, hammer); Mother Ogive (veil); Pennywhistle (beak mask, big pack); Sister Pyx (plate, wimple, crossbow); Bishop Ambrose (mitre, pale).\n609\t- **Monsters:** table in section 6. Each has a palette variant for elites and glowing eyes (`glow: true`).\n610\t- **Bosses:** the Bursar (scale 2.5 humanoid, huge belly, ledger, abacus); the Bishop; Malison (6 m, non-humanoid: torso, head, four huge rope-wrapped arms as `tube` parts driven by `SpringChain` and `twoBoneIK`, stone cracks with `glow`); Old Clemency (`lathe`, 5 m, cracked, tolls with a swing).\n611\t- **Props the library lacks:** gibbet, lychgate, Knell Font, votive rack, offering dish, ledger, abacus, bell rope, hand-bell, lantern, censer, shovel-as-weapon, pallbearer coffin.\n612\t- **Library:** use it freely for generic props (`LIBRARY.md`: `dungeon`, `architecture`, `containers`, `lighting`, `dressing`, `props`, `town`, `weapons`).\n613\t- **HUD icons:** library ones (`whirlwind-icon`, `leap-icon`, `fireball-icon`, `summon-icon`, `curse-icon`, `aura-icon`, `trap-icon`, `totem-icon`, `shield-bubble-icon`, `dash-icon`, `arrow-volley-icon`, `potion-red`, `skull`, `gold-icon`, `lock`, `check`, `plus`, `minus`, `quest-marker`) plus your own 12×12 sets: one per skill where the library has nothing, one per item slot recoloured by rarity, 3 gems, and all button glyphs (section 10).\n614\t- **Effects:** register particle presets per element (`ember`, `shock`, `grave_smoke`, `coin_spray`, `bone_chips`, `wax`, `peat`). Expanding rings are flat meshes tweened in scale with `glowMaterial`. `Trail` on weapon swings and projectiles.\n615\t- **Loot beams:** as in section 2 item 29. Items lie on the floor with a small label, always visible for Reliquary and up, on Alt or R3 for the rest.\n616\t\n617\t---\n618\t\n619\t## 9. Animation\n620\t\n621\t**Base:** the engine's clip system. Use `HERO_CLIPS` on every humanoid. Hero and NPC locomotion is `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run` driven by speed with `AnimationMixer` crossfades. Set `action.timeScale` from attack speed.\n622\t\n623\t**New clips, as `ClipDef`s in `src/view/clips.js`:** `BellOverhead`, `ChainSweep`, `LanternLob`, `ShovelSwat`, `Dig`, `RaiseHands`, `SinkGround`, `Drink`, `Revive`, `TalkGesture`, `Interact`, `Shamble` (with `gaitClip`), `Lurch`, `Lunge`, `CoffinSlam`, `Swell`, `RopeLash`.\n624\t\n625\t**Monster motion:** humanoid clips with per-type speed; `LegStepper` with `twoBoneIK` for Crawlers, Clapperjaw and the Plate; `Squash` on the Deacon and on landings; hovering is a sine on y plus `SpringChain` for anything that trails (ropes, chains, tails).\n626\t\n627\t**Bosses:** clips for the Bursar and Bishop (they're humanoid); Malison is procedural (arms from `SpringChain` plus scripted strike targets).\n628\t\n629\t**Checks:** `validateClip` on every clip in tests; `analyzeClip` on `Shamble` and any new gait (section 2 item 16).\n630\t\n631\t---\n632\t\n633\t## 10. UI and input\n634\t\n635\t### The rules\n636\t\n637\t- All UI is drawn with `ctx.hud`, in art pixels, the same screens for pad and mouse. DOM is used only for the engine's ⚙ and the fatal no-WebGPU message. **No dense screens:** one job per screen, big icons, short lists, a maximum of 6 lines on an item card.\n638\t- Body text is scale 1 (7 art pixels, about 28 px at 1080p), headings scale 2. Nothing smaller exists. Keep important things inside a safe zone 12 art pixels from each edge.\n639\t- **Layout comes from `hud.width` and `hud.height`** (section 2 item 20). Test at 427×240, 480×270 and 512×288.\n640\t- **`src/ui/ui.js`** is a small immediate-mode layer: each widget registers an id and rectangle per frame. Direction input moves focus to the nearest rectangle that way. **Mouse hover moves focus when the pointer moved**; click activates. Pointer to art pixels: `((x + 1) / 2 × width, (1 − y) / 2 × height)`. Clicks come from `input.buttonEvents`. Each frame it also records `ui.drawnText` and `ui.focus` so tests can read the screen.\n641\t- Pause and full-screen menus use `engine.timeScale = 0` solo and on the couch. In a session nothing pauses: menus sit over the running world and the hero stands still.\n642\t- Call `ctx.input.clearQueued()` when a menu closes so presses don't leak into the game.\n643\t- Your own Settings screen covers what the engine's panel does (through `engine.settings.set`) plus the game's options, so it all works on a pad. The ⚙ shows only on touch-only devices.\n644\t\n645\t### Controls\n646\t\n647\t| Action | Pad (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\n648\t|---|---|---|\n649\t| Move | Left stick | WASD or arrows, or left click on ground |\n650\t| Aim | Right stick (soft lock otherwise) | Pointer |\n651\t| Skill 1 | Cross (0) | Left click on a monster, or Shift-click |\n652\t| Skill 2 | Square (2) | Right click |\n653\t| Skills 3, 4 | Triangle (3), Circle (1) | 1, 2 |\n654\t| Skills 5, 6 | R1 (5), R2 (7) | 3, 4 |\n655\t| Dodge | L2 (6) | Space |\n656\t| Potion | L1 (4) | Q |\n657\t| Interact | Cross tap when a target is within 2.2 m and no hostile within 4 m; hold Cross 0.4 s always | E, or click the thing |\n658\t| Hero screen | Create (8), on release | I or C (gear), K (skills), L (quests) |\n659\t| Pause | Options (9); ignore it while Create is held, since that chord belongs to the hub | Esc |\n660\t| Map | D-pad up | M or Tab |\n661\t| Passing Bell | Hold d-pad down | Hold T |\n662\t| Equip newest upgrade | D-pad left | F |\n663\t| Cycle interact target | D-pad right | Mouse does this |\n664\t| Show all item labels | R3 (11) | Alt |\n665\t| Zoom (Settings range) | Not on a button | Wheel |\n666\t\n667\t**Menus:** left stick or d-pad moves; Cross confirms; Circle backs out; Square and Triangle are contextual; L1 and R1 switch tabs; Options closes. Keyboard: arrows or WASD; Enter or Space confirms; Esc backs out; X and V are contextual; Q and E switch tabs. Mouse: hover, click, right click for the contextual action, wheel scrolls. Add `Tab`, `F` keys and `Alt` to `ctx.input.preventKeys`.\n668\t\n669\t### Prompts follow the last input\n670\t\n671\t`src/ui/glyphs.js`: `lastDevice` flips to `pad` on any pad button or stick past the deadzone, and to `kbm` on any key, click or pointer move over 2 px. `prompt(action)` draws the right sprite everywhere: action bar, toasts, interact prompts, menu footers, tutorial.\n672\t\n673\t- **PlayStation (default):** 11×11 sprites: Cross `sky`, Circle `red`, Square `plum`, Triangle `lime`, L1, R1, L2, R2, Options, Create, d-pad directions, sticks.\n674\t- **Xbox (Settings option):** A `lime`, B `red`, X `sky`, Y `sand`, LB, RB, LT, RT, Menu, View.\n675\t- **Keyboard and mouse:** keycaps drawn from a rectangle plus letter; left and right mouse sprites.\n676\t- Hide the system cursor while the pad is in use. With the mouse, use a pixel gauntlet as a CSS `cursor` from a generated data URL.\n677\t\n678\t### HUD\n679\t\n680\t```text\n681\tLV 12 NAME  ======XP======          ZONE TOAST or BOSS BAR              +--minimap--+\n682\tGOLD 1,204                          QUEST or KNELL METER                |  72 x 54  |\n683\t                                                                        +-----------+\n684\t                                                                         QUEST LINE\n685\t                                 (the world)\n686\t                                                                          STREAK 37\n687\t ||                                                                               _\n688\t || candle                                                                       (_) vessel\n689\t ||          [potion][dodge] [X][SQ][TRI][O][R1][R2]\n690\t```\n691\t\n692\t- **Life is a candle, not an orb.** A tall candle bottom left, 16×70 art pixels, that melts down; the flame gutters and the vignette rises at low life. Draw it each frame with `hud.rect` and `hud.sprite`, with the number on it.\n693\t- **Resource is a class vessel** bottom right: a bronze bell filling (Clangor), a lantern's glass (Wick), a jar of coins (Tithe).\n694\t- **Action bar:** 26×26 slots, icon, cooldown as a falling shutter plus seconds, the current button glyph on each, red flash when you can't pay.\n695\t- **World labels** (projected with the camera): damage numbers, monster name and bar on hover or soft lock, elite names with Afflictions, item labels, NPC names, interact prompts.\n696\t- **Toasts:** level up, new upgrade with the equip prompt, quest updates, legendary name in `orange` (scale 2), Requiem.\n697\t- **Subtitles:** bottom centre, speaker name in their colour, babble voice playing.\n698\t- **Couch co-op:** per-seat corner panels in seat colours: mini candle, vessel and 6 icons at 12 px. No centre bar.\n699\t\n700\t### Screens\n701\t\n702\tEach is one job, reachable by pad alone and mouse alone.\n703\t\n704\t1. **Title.** Slow pan of the Belfry against a stormy sky, embers, big title, \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\". Idle 10 s: attract.\n705\t2. **Main menu.** Continue, New Hero, Knell Runs (locked until the credits or The Last Bell), Settings, About. Idle 10 s: attract.\n706\t3. **Hero select and New Hero.** Three heroes on plinths in the world, camera zoomed in. Selected one plays `Triumph`. Name, one-line fantasy, resource, three signature skills. Names come from a list (shuffle button, no text entry). Then difficulty and start point. Up to 3 hero slots, deletion with a hold to confirm.\n707\t4. **Hero screen,** tabs on L1 and R1:\n708\t   - **Gear:** paperdoll slots left, 8×5 inventory right (24 px cells), item card below: name in rarity colour, two big numbers (DAMAGE +12%, TOUGHNESS −3%), up to 4 affix lines, flavour. Square salvages or drops, Triangle compares.\n709\t   - **Skills:** six slots across the top, the class's 8 skills as big cards, then its 3 Tones. One step at a time. Then the two Vows.\n710\t   - **Stats:** three huge numbers (Damage, Toughness, Recovery), and a short list you can page.\n711\t   - **Devotion:** four big bars.\n712\t   - **Codex:** lore, bestiary, How to Play.\n713\t5. **Vendor and service screens:** Pennywhistle (buy, sell, casket); Dame Brasse (salvage, craft, reforge); Mother Ogive (extract, reliquary, socket, merge); Collection Box. Same card-and-grid layout as Gear.\n714\t6. **Map.** Full-screen explored cells, markers, Lychgate list to travel.\n715\t7. **Dialogue.** Camera zooms on the speaker (`setZoom`, pan the camera target), letterbox bars, subtitle panel, up to 3 choices. Any button advances, hold skips.\n716\t8. **Cutscenes.** `Timeline` for cues, `line()` and `bars()`; the camera stays `iso` and only pans and zooms. Two minimum: the opening and the ending, plus boss entrances. Hold to skip.\n717\t9. **Pause.** Resume, Hero, Map, Party (join and leave seats), How to Play, Settings, **Dev Mode**, About, Save and Quit. In a session: Resume, Settings, How to Play only.\n718\t10. **Settings.** Volumes (Master, Music, Sound, Voices), Glyphs (PlayStation or Xbox), Screen shake, Damage numbers, Zoom, Look (native plus a few presets), Pixel size, Quality, Fullscreen (catch the promise: browsers may refuse it, and an unhandled rejection fails the hub check), Reset to defaults (music back to 10%).\n719\t11. **Knell setup and results.** Tier, modifiers shown as big cards; results as a few big numbers.\n720\t12. **Death overlay.** The system line and the three options.\n721\t13. **About and Credits.** Section 13.\n722\t14. **Touch-only.** Section 13.\n723\t15. **Session card.** Section 12.\n724\t\n725\t### Tutorial\n726\t\n727\tContextual prompts only, in the current glyphs, each gone once done: move, attack, dodge, drink, assign a skill, equip an upgrade, talk, use a Lychgate.\n728\t\n729\t---\n730\t\n731\t## 11. Audio\n732\t\n733\tEverything is synthesised in code: no audio files. Sounds are `SoundDef` data in `src/data/sfx.js`, music is `Song` data in `src/data/songs.js`.\n734\t\n735\t**Music is at 10% by default** (section 2 item 27), and a test asserts it.\n736\t\n737\t**A pad may not unlock sound.** The engine unlocks audio on key, pointer and touch events, not on pad buttons. On the first pad press call `ctx.audio.unlock()`. If `audio.unlocked` stays false, show a small \"PRESS A KEY OR CLICK FOR SOUND\" on the title. There's no real pad here to prove what a browser does, so handle both.\n738\t\n739\t### Music\n740\t\n741\tThe sequencer is chiptune by design. Lean into it: square-wave organ, triangle bass, noise for wind and drums, slow arpeggios. Write your own melodies from this motif, and quote nothing from the source.\n742\t\n743\t**The Clemency motif (D minor):** `D4 A4 F4 E4 | D4 C4 D4 A3`. Every piece states or bends it. Malison's version is the same notes, one semitone off, because the bell is cracked.\n744\t\n745\t| Piece | Where | BPM | Character |\n746\t|---|---|---|---|\n747\t| Vespers | Title, attract | 60 | Solo bell, then organ. Motif plain |\n748\t| Last Lamps | Tollhaven | 72 | Arpeggio like a lute, warm, sad |\n749\t| Weeping Road | Yard, Causeway | 66 | Sparse low pulses, wind noise |\n750\t| Under Gloam | Ossuary | 58 | Long notes, distant high bell, no drums |\n751\t| Cinders | Cloister | 96 | Tense ostinato, low drums |\n752\t| The Ledger | The Bursar | 126 | Mock-pompous march |\n753\t| The Climb | Belfry floors | 104 | Rising, relentless |\n754\t| Eventide | Malison | 138 | Driving, cracked motif, organ stabs; drums cut out in phase 3 |\n755\t| The Knell | Knell Runs | 118 | Driving loop with a meter-rising layer |\n756\t| Clemency | Ending | 66 | Motif resolved to major at last |\n757\t\n758\tEach song has at least 3 patterns (8 or 16 bars), so it doesn't wear out at low volume. Fade or swap music on zone and boss changes with `playMusic`.\n759\t\n760\t### Sound effects\n761\t\n762\tAt least 60 sounds, each with 2+ pitch variants through `pitch` at play time. `layers` make them weighty.\n763\t\n764\t- **The bell** is the game's signature: `layers` of sine partials at 0.5, 1, 1.2, 1.5, 2, 2.67 and 3 times the base frequency, with long decays and slight detune. It marks legendary drops (bright), Great Toll (huge), the Knell meter and Old Clemency (enormous, and a cracked version with a beating partial).\n765\t- **Combat:** swings per weapon, hits per material (flesh, bone, stone, wood), crit layer, shatter, chunk patter, gold spray, Tallow plop, potion, dodge, level up, footsteps per floor.\n766\t- **Monsters:** wake, attack, hurt and death per type; telegraph warnings; boss stingers.\n767\t- **UI:** move, confirm, back, error, tab, equip, salvage.\n768\t- **Ambience:** `audio.loop` voices for rain, fire and wind, with `spatialize` and `muffle`.\n769\t\n770\t### Voices: Animalese gibberish\n771\t\n772\tNo real speech. `src/audio/voice.js` turns each subtitle into babble:\n773\t\n774\t- A **syllable bank** of about 20 short `SoundDef`s per register (consonant noise layer plus two vowel-formant sines with a pitch glide): low, mid, high, demon.\n775\t- Each letter or pair maps to a syllable by hash, so the same line always sounds the same. Punctuation makes pauses; `!` lifts pitch, `?` rises at the end.\n776\t- **Per speaker:** register, base pitch, rate, variance. The Crier is high and fast. Dame Brasse is low, loud and clipped. Ogive is soft and slow. The Bursar is low, with `crush`. **Malison is demon register, doubled an octave down, with an echo layer.**\n777\t- Play through `ctx.audio.play(def, { pitch, volume, pan })`, scaling by your Voices setting (the engine has only master, sfx and music channels). Heroes get short grunts and class barks (\"not enough Clangor\").\n778\t\n779\t---\n780\t\n781\t## 12. Multiplayer\n782\t\n783\t### The couch (the game on its own)\n784\t\n785\tOpened directly, with no hub, the game is a complete solo game with **drop-in couch co-op for up to 4 on one screen**. That's what \"the game on its own\" means here: the TV comes with one screen and up to four pads, and needs no server.\n786\t\n787\t- **Seats:** the keyboard and mouse or the first pad to press is seat 1. In play, any unassigned pad pressing Options, or Party in the pause menu, joins: pick a class, get a guest hero at the party's level, saved per class so it keeps its loot. Holding Options on a pad in the Party menu leaves.\n788\t- **Input:** `src/input/pads.js` polls each pad (section 2 item 25) and forwards state through `ctx.input.send` so engine replays stay valid.\n789\t- **One camera:** target the centre of the seats, and zoom out as far as `setZoom(0.62)` to fit them all. A hero off screen for 2 s teleports to seat 1.\n790\t- **Menus:** any seat can open its Hero screen; the world pauses, the panel is framed in that seat's colour, and only that seat controls it.\n791\t- **Loot** is per seat, with item labels coloured by owner.\n792\t\n793\t### Hub sessions\n794\t\n795\tThe hub loads the game with `AIHub.active` true. Follow its `README.md` exactly. Mode: **`shared-world`**.\n796\t\n797\t```html\n798\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n799\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n800\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n801\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n802\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Fill the Knell, then slay its Warden together\">\n803\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick or WASD. Attack: Cross or click. Skills: face buttons or 1-4.\">\n804\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n805\t```\n806\t\n807\t**Flow:** at load, `if (AIHub.active)` go straight to the session flow: no title, menus, attract or saves. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, run the normal game. Build the round from `info.seed` (the same map on every copy), start the engine (`Engine.headless` if `info.server`), then `AIHub.ready()` with no key press. If the engine can't start, `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n808\t\n809\t**The card (game-owned):** three heroes in a torchlit room, plus the title, the players in their colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in the current glyphs, seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross or a click on Ready calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle, M or a click calls `AIHub.answer('more')`. No choices, no menus. `AIHub.rng('card')` for anything random.\n810\t\n811\t**The round:**\n812\t- A special Knell Run, one floor of 18 rooms, sized so it takes 5 to 6 minutes to fill the meter and 90 seconds for the Warden. HP scales with players.\n813\t- Heroes start at level 10 with all 6 slots filled from a class preset and a plain gear set. Class comes from seat (seat 0 Bellwarden, 1 Lamplighter, 2 Sexton, 3 Bellwarden). In the first room, standing on another class's font for 2 s swaps your class until play has run for 30 s.\n814\t- Level-ups pop a small \"pick 1 of 3\" (a Tone, a Vow or a stat), on d-pad left, up or right, Z, X or C, or a click; it auto-picks after 10 s.\n815\t- Loot works as normal, with one-button equip. The Hero screen opens over the running world.\n816\t- Death: rise after 8 s, or an ally revives you.\n817\t- Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`; show the countdown. Before that the sim doesn't step.\n818\t\n819\t**The end:** Warden dead: host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won: true, stats, awards })`. On `time-up`: host calls it at once with `won: false`. `standings` lists every remaining player, best first, ties grouped, sorted by `score = damage/100 + 50×revives + 20×eliteKills − 30×deaths`. Awards: Bell-Ringer (damage), Undertaker (kills), Good Samaritan (revives), Collector (gold), Regular Customer (deaths). On `end`, for any reason: stop input, sim, sending, music and loops.\n820\t\n821\t**Other rules:** on `leave`, fade that hero out and carry on. Network only through `AIHub`. No chat, emotes or custom names. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, new tabs or navigation. No Quit. Names are drawn on the HUD canvas, never as HTML. `Create + Options` belongs to the hub.\n822\t\n823\t### Netcode\n824\t\n825\t**The host's sim is the only truth.** Clients generate the same map from the seed, run the same view code against a mirror of the world, and send only intent.\n826\t\n827\t| Message | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Contents |\n828\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n829\t| `i` | client to host | no | 10 Hz, always, even idle | Move, aim, held buttons, seq |\n830\t| `c` | client to host | yes | On change | Presses and commands: cast, dodge, interact, equip, salvage. Queue and retry if `send` returns false |\n831\t| `s` | host to all | no | 10 Hz | Flat integer arrays: heroes `[id,x,z,facing,anim,hp,res,flags]`, monsters `[id,x,z,facing,hp]`. Positions × 10 |\n832\t| `e` | host to all | yes | 5 Hz batches | Events: spawn, hit, death, cast, drop, status, banner, subtitle, meter |\n833\t\n834\t**Budgets, from the protocol:** at most 20 messages a second per copy; 16 KB per message; unreliable over about 1,200 bytes is lost whole if any packet is. So keep `s` under 1,100 bytes of JSON: the 24 monsters nearest any hero every time, plus a rotating slice of the rest within 40 m. Cap `e` at 12 KB and carry the rest to the next batch.\n835\t\n836\t**Clients:** interpolate others 120 ms behind. Predict the local hero with the same movement code and the same grid; correct smoothly past 1 m of error. Play cast clips at once; numbers and deaths come from the host. Effects, ragdolls and chunks are local, from events.\n837\t\n838\t**Server copies** (`AIHub.server`): run sim and net only; skip the view. `AIHub.me` isn't in the players; no local seat.\n839\t\n840\t**Hitstop and slow motion:** never on the host. Clients may do purely visual freezes (pausing a mixer for 3 frames).\n841\t\n842\t---\n843\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"e68de197-b151-476b-8604-0f7ff906ba6d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:07.724Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 8. Art direction\n\n**Base:** the engine's native look (`LOOK_PRESETS.none`: 3D low-poly toon rendered as pixel art, Sweetie 16 palette), with a soft vignette (`scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: 0.3 } }]`). Raise the vignette at low life. Everything is palette colours on `toonMaterial`, chunky shapes (0.12 m or more for anything that carries the silhouette), rules from `ASSETS.md` section 4. Tag every actor with `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`.\n\n**Style target:** dark gothic dioramas lit by fire. Deep `ink`, `night`, `navy`, `plum` environments; warm pools of light; saturated accents on anything that matters. The player should always find the hero, the danger and the loot within a second.\n\n**Biome palettes:** Yard and Causeway: `night`, `slate`, `teal`, cold `sky` sun. Town: `plum`, `sand`, warm lamps. Ossuary: `night`, `mist` bone, green and candle lights. Cloister: `ink`, `red`, `orange`, firelight everywhere. Belfry: `navy`, `cyan` crackle, `white` lightning, `rift-energy` beyond the edges.\n\n### The body template (verified)\n\n```js\nconst j = (name, at, kids = []) => ({ group: kids, name, pivot: true, at });\n// Positions are HERO_RIG's rest layout: keep the pivots, change the shapes between them.\nconst humanoid = ({ hips, chest, head, upperArm, foreArm, handR = [], handL = [], thigh, shin, foot }) => [\n  j('Pelvis', [0, 0.62, 0], [...hips,\n    j('Torso', [0, 0.05, 0], [...chest,\n      j('Head', [0, 0.5, 0], head),\n      j('ArmR', [-0.27, 0.42, 0], [...upperArm, j('ForearmR', [0, -0.25, 0], [...foreArm, j('HandR', [0, -0.16, 0], handR)])]),\n      j('ArmL', [0.27, 0.42, 0], [...upperArm, j('ForearmL', [0, -0.25, 0], [...foreArm, j('HandL', [0, -0.16, 0], handL)])]),\n    ]),\n    j('LegR', [-0.14, 0, 0], [...thigh, j('ShinR', [0, -0.3, 0], [...shin, j('FootR', [0, -0.22, 0], foot)])]),\n    j('LegL', [0.14, 0, 0], [...thigh, j('ShinL', [0, -0.3, 0], [...shin, j('FootL', [0, -0.22, 0], foot)])]),\n  ]),\n];\n```\n\nShapes hang below their pivot (`{ box: [0.13, 0.25, 0.13], at: [0, -0.125, 0], c: 'robe' }`). Pass `[]` for any piece a body doesn't need. A weapon inside `HandR` uses `{ use: 'mace', at: [0, -0.35, 0.1], rot: [90, 0, 0] }`, or at runtime `root.getObjectByName('HandR').add(buildModel(id).object)`. Recolour with `buildModel(id, { palette: { robe: 'navy' }, catalog })`. Keep cheap monsters to about 4 palette slots, since each makes meshes per pivot.\n\n### Asset list\n\nPut each in a `src/view/models/*.js` module of plain exports with no engine start, and check with `node check.mjs --sheets src/view/models/x.js`.\n\n- **Heroes (3 bodies, each with 3 armour tiers by level and rarity):**\n  - **Bellwarden:** square shoulders, cowl, bronze trim (`plum`, `orange`), a huge bell on a chain as the weapon, with a `SpringChain` swinging at runtime.\n  - **Lamplighter:** wide-brim hat, long coat (`navy`, `sand`), lamp pole on the back with a `glow` lantern and its own point light.\n  - **Sexton:** stovepipe hat, black frock, grey face (`ink`, `lime` accent), spade.\n  - Helm and shoulder sub-models attach to joints and change with worn gear. A seat-coloured ground ring appears in co-op.\n- **NPCs (6):** the Crier's lantern on a post; Dame Brasse (wide, apron, hammer); Mother Ogive (veil); Pennywhistle (beak mask, big pack); Sister Pyx (plate, wimple, crossbow); Bishop Ambrose (mitre, pale).\n- **Monsters:** table in section 6. Each has a palette variant for elites and glowing eyes (`glow: true`).\n- **Bosses:** the Bursar (scale 2.5 humanoid, huge belly, ledger, abacus); the Bishop; Malison (6 m, non-humanoid: torso, head, four huge rope-wrapped arms as `tube` parts driven by `SpringChain` and `twoBoneIK`, stone cracks with `glow`); Old Clemency (`lathe`, 5 m, cracked, tolls with a swing).\n- **Props the library lacks:** gibbet, lychgate, Knell Font, votive rack, offering dish, ledger, abacus, bell rope, hand-bell, lantern, censer, shovel-as-weapon, pallbearer coffin.\n- **Library:** use it freely for generic props (`LIBRARY.md`: `dungeon`, `architecture`, `containers`, `lighting`, `dressing`, `props`, `town`, `weapons`).\n- **HUD icons:** library ones (`whirlwind-icon`, `leap-icon`, `fireball-icon`, `summon-icon`, `curse-icon`, `aura-icon`, `trap-icon`, `totem-icon`, `shield-bubble-icon`, `dash-icon`, `arrow-volley-icon`, `potion-red`, `skull`, `gold-icon`, `lock`, `check`, `plus`, `minus`, `quest-marker`) plus your own 12×12 sets: one per skill where the library has nothing, one per item slot recoloured by rarity, 3 gems, and all button glyphs (section 10).\n- **Effects:** register particle presets per element (`ember`, `shock`, `grave_smoke`, `coin_spray`, `bone_chips`, `wax`, `peat`). Expanding rings are flat meshes tweened in scale with `glowMaterial`. `Trail` on weapon swings and projectiles.\n- **Loot beams:** as in section 2 item 29. Items lie on the floor with a small label, always visible for Reliquary and up, on Alt or R3 for the rest.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Animation\n\n**Base:** the engine's clip system. Use `HERO_CLIPS` on every humanoid. Hero and NPC locomotion is `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run` driven by speed with `AnimationMixer` crossfades. Set `action.timeScale` from attack speed.\n\n**New clips, as `ClipDef`s in `src/view/clips.js`:** `BellOverhead`, `ChainSweep`, `LanternLob`, `ShovelSwat`, `Dig`, `RaiseHands`, `SinkGround`, `Drink`, `Revive`, `TalkGesture`, `Interact`, `Shamble` (with `gaitClip`), `Lurch`, `Lunge`, `CoffinSlam`, `Swell`, `RopeLash`.\n\n**Monster motion:** humanoid clips with per-type speed; `LegStepper` with `twoBoneIK` for Crawlers, Clapperjaw and the Plate; `Squash` on the Deacon and on landings; hovering is a sine on y plus `SpringChain` for anything that trails (ropes, chains, tails).\n\n**Bosses:** clips for the Bursar and Bishop (they're humanoid); Malison is procedural (arms from `SpringChain` plus scripted strike targets).\n\n**Checks:** `validateClip` on every clip in tests; `analyzeClip` on `Shamble` and any new gait (section 2 item 16).\n\n---\n\n## 10. UI and input\n\n### The rules\n\n- All UI is drawn with `ctx.hud`, in art pixels, the same screens for pad and mouse. DOM is used only for the engine's ⚙ and the fatal no-WebGPU message. **No dense screens:** one job per screen, big icons, short lists, a maximum of 6 lines on an item card.\n- Body text is scale 1 (7 art pixels, about 28 px at 1080p), headings scale 2. Nothing smaller exists. Keep important things inside a safe zone 12 art pixels from each edge.\n- **Layout comes from `hud.width` and `hud.height`** (section 2 item 20). Test at 427×240, 480×270 and 512×288.\n- **`src/ui/ui.js`** is a small immediate-mode layer: each widget registers an id and rectangle per frame. Direction input moves focus to the nearest rectangle that way. **Mouse hover moves focus when the pointer moved**; click activates. Pointer to art pixels: `((x + 1) / 2 × width, (1 − y) / 2 × height)`. Clicks come from `input.buttonEvents`. Each frame it also records `ui.drawnText` and `ui.focus` so tests can read the screen.\n- Pause and full-screen menus use `engine.timeScale = 0` solo and on the couch. In a session nothing pauses: menus sit over the running world and the hero stands still.\n- Call `ctx.input.clearQueued()` when a menu closes so presses don't leak into the game.\n- Your own Settings screen covers what the engine's panel does (through `engine.settings.set`) plus the game's options, so it all works on a pad. The ⚙ shows only on touch-only devices.\n\n### Controls\n\n| Action | Pad (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move | Left stick | WASD or arrows, or left click on ground |\n| Aim | Right stick (soft lock otherwise) | Pointer |\n| Skill 1 | Cross (0) | Left click on a monster, or Shift-click |\n| Skill 2 | Square (2) | Right click |\n| Skills 3, 4 | Triangle (3), Circle (1) | 1, 2 |\n| Skills 5, 6 | R1 (5), R2 (7) | 3, 4 |\n| Dodge | L2 (6) | Space |\n| Potion | L1 (4) | Q |\n| Interact | Cross tap when a target is within 2.2 m and no hostile within 4 m; hold Cross 0.4 s always | E, or click the thing |\n| Hero screen | Create (8), on release | I or C (gear), K (skills), L (quests) |\n| Pause | Options (9); ignore it while Create is held, since that chord belongs to the hub | Esc |\n| Map | D-pad up | M or Tab |\n| Passing Bell | Hold d-pad down | Hold T |\n| Equip newest upgrade | D-pad left | F |\n| Cycle interact target | D-pad right | Mouse does this |\n| Show all item labels | R3 (11) | Alt |\n| Zoom (Settings range) | Not on a button | Wheel |\n\n**Menus:** left stick or d-pad moves; Cross confirms; Circle backs out; Square and Triangle are contextual; L1 and R1 switch tabs; Options closes. Keyboard: arrows or WASD; Enter or Space confirms; Esc backs out; X and V are contextual; Q and E switch tabs. Mouse: hover, click, right click for the contextual action, wheel scrolls. Add `Tab`, `F` keys and `Alt` to `ctx.input.preventKeys`.\n\n### Prompts follow the last input\n\n`src/ui/glyphs.js`: `lastDevice` flips to `pad` on any pad button or stick past the deadzone, and to `kbm` on any key, click or pointer move over 2 px. `prompt(action)` draws the right sprite everywhere: action bar, toasts, interact prompts, menu footers, tutorial.\n\n- **PlayStation (default):** 11×11 sprites: Cross `sky`, Circle `red`, Square `plum`, Triangle `lime`, L1, R1, L2, R2, Options, Create, d-pad directions, sticks.\n- **Xbox (Settings option):** A `lime`, B `red`, X `sky`, Y `sand`, LB, RB, LT, RT, Menu, View.\n- **Keyboard and mouse:** keycaps drawn from a rectangle plus letter; left and right mouse sprites.\n- Hide the system cursor while the pad is in use. With the mouse, use a pixel gauntlet as a CSS `cursor` from a generated data URL.\n\n### HUD\n\n```text\nLV 12 NAME  ======XP======          ZONE TOAST or BOSS BAR              +--minimap--+\nGOLD 1,204                          QUEST or KNELL METER                |  72 x 54  |\n                                                                        +-----------+\n                                                                         QUEST LINE\n                                 (the world)\n                                                                          STREAK 37\n ||                                                                               _\n || candle                                                                       (_) vessel\n ||          [potion][dodge] [X][SQ][TRI][O][R1][R2]\n```\n\n- **Life is a candle, not an orb.** A tall candle bottom left, 16×70 art pixels, that melts down; the flame gutters and the vignette rises at low life. Draw it each frame with `hud.rect` and `hud.sprite`, with the number on it.\n- **Resource is a class vessel** bottom right: a bronze bell filling (Clangor), a lantern's glass (Wick), a jar of coins (Tithe).\n- **Action bar:** 26×26 slots, icon, cooldown as a falling shutter plus seconds, the current button glyph on each, red flash when you can't pay.\n- **World labels** (projected with the camera): damage numbers, monster name and bar on hover or soft lock, elite names with Afflictions, item labels, NPC names, interact prompts.\n- **Toasts:** level up, new upgrade with the equip prompt, quest updates, legendary name in `orange` (scale 2), Requiem.\n- **Subtitles:** bottom centre, speaker name in their colour, babble voice playing.\n- **Couch co-op:** per-seat corner panels in seat colours: mini candle, vessel and 6 icons at 12 px. No centre bar.\n\n### Screens\n\nEach is one job, reachable by pad alone and mouse alone.\n\n1. **Title.** Slow pan of the Belfry against a stormy sky, embers, big title, \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\". Idle 10 s: attract.\n2. **Main menu.** Continue, New Hero, Knell Runs (locked until the credits or The Last Bell), Settings, About. Idle 10 s: attract.\n3. **Hero select and New Hero.** Three heroes on plinths in the world, camera zoomed in. Selected one plays `Triumph`. Name, one-line fantasy, resource, three signature skills. Names come from a list (shuffle button, no text entry). Then difficulty and start point. Up to 3 hero slots, deletion with a hold to confirm.\n4. **Hero screen,** tabs on L1 and R1:\n   - **Gear:** paperdoll slots left, 8×5 inventory right (24 px cells), item card below: name in rarity colour, two big numbers (DAMAGE +12%, TOUGHNESS −3%), up to 4 affix lines, flavour. Square salvages or drops, Triangle compares.\n   - **Skills:** six slots across the top, the class's 8 skills as big cards, then its 3 Tones. One step at a time. Then the two Vows.\n   - **Stats:** three huge numbers (Damage, Toughness, Recovery), and a short list you can page.\n   - **Devotion:** four big bars.\n   - **Codex:** lore, bestiary, How to Play.\n5. **Vendor and service screens:** Pennywhistle (buy, sell, casket); Dame Brasse (salvage, craft, reforge); Mother Ogive (extract, reliquary, socket, merge); Collection Box. Same card-and-grid layout as Gear.\n6. **Map.** Full-screen explored cells, markers, Lychgate list to travel.\n7. **Dialogue.** Camera zooms on the speaker (`setZoom`, pan the camera target), letterbox bars, subtitle panel, up to 3 choices. Any button advances, hold skips.\n8. **Cutscenes.** `Timeline` for cues, `line()` and `bars()`; the camera stays `iso` and only pans and zooms. Two minimum: the opening and the ending, plus boss entrances. Hold to skip.\n9. **Pause.** Resume, Hero, Map, Party (join and leave seats), How to Play, Settings, **Dev Mode**, About, Save and Quit. In a session: Resume, Settings, How to Play only.\n10. **Settings.** Volumes (Master, Music, Sound, Voices), Glyphs (PlayStation or Xbox), Screen shake, Damage numbers, Zoom, Look (native plus a few presets), Pixel size, Quality, Fullscreen (catch the promise: browsers may refuse it, and an unhandled rejection fails the hub check), Reset to defaults (music back to 10%).\n11. **Knell setup and results.** Tier, modifiers shown as big cards; results as a few big numbers.\n12. **Death overlay.** The system line and the three options.\n13. **About and Credits.** Section 13.\n14. **Touch-only.** Section 13.\n15. **Session card.** Section 12.\n\n### Tutorial\n\nContextual prompts only, in the current glyphs, each gone once done: move, attack, dodge, drink, assign a skill, equip an upgrade, talk, use a Lychgate.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Audio\n\nEverything is synthesised in code: no audio files. Sounds are `SoundDef` data in `src/data/sfx.js`, music is `Song` data in `src/data/songs.js`.\n\n**Music is at 10% by default** (section 2 item 27), and a test asserts it.\n\n**A pad may not unlock sound.** The engine unlocks audio on key, pointer and touch events, not on pad buttons. On the first pad press call `ctx.audio.unlock()`. If `audio.unlocked` stays false, show a small \"PRESS A KEY OR CLICK FOR SOUND\" on the title. There's no real pad here to prove what a browser does, so handle both.\n\n### Music\n\nThe sequencer is chiptune by design. Lean into it: square-wave organ, triangle bass, noise for wind and drums, slow arpeggios. Write your own melodies from this motif, and quote nothing from the source.\n\n**The Clemency motif (D minor):** `D4 A4 F4 E4 | D4 C4 D4 A3`. Every piece states or bends it. Malison's version is the same notes, one semitone off, because the bell is cracked.\n\n| Piece | Where | BPM | Character |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Vespers | Title, attract | 60 | Solo bell, then organ. Motif plain |\n| Last Lamps | Tollhaven | 72 | Arpeggio like a lute, warm, sad |\n| Weeping Road | Yard, Causeway | 66 | Sparse low pulses, wind noise |\n| Under Gloam | Ossuary | 58 | Long notes, distant high bell, no drums |\n| Cinders | Cloister | 96 | Tense ostinato, low drums |\n| The Ledger | The Bursar | 126 | Mock-pompous march |\n| The Climb | Belfry floors | 104 | Rising, relentless |\n| Eventide | Malison | 138 | Driving, cracked motif, organ stabs; drums cut out in phase 3 |\n| The Knell | Knell Runs | 118 | Driving loop with a meter-rising layer |\n| Clemency | Ending | 66 | Motif resolved to major at last |\n\nEach song has at least 3 patterns (8 or 16 bars), so it doesn't wear out at low volume. Fade or swap music on zone and boss changes with `playMusic`.\n\n### Sound effects\n\nAt least 60 sounds, each with 2+ pitch variants through `pitch` at play time. `layers` make them weighty.\n\n- **The bell** is the game's signature: `layers` of sine partials at 0.5, 1, 1.2, 1.5, 2, 2.67 and 3 times the base frequency, with long decays and slight detune. It marks legendary drops (bright), Great Toll (huge), the Knell meter and Old Clemency (enormous, and a cracked version with a beating partial).\n- **Combat:** swings per weapon, hits per material (flesh, bone, stone, wood), crit layer, shatter, chunk patter, gold spray, Tallow plop, potion, dodge, level up, footsteps per floor.\n- **Monsters:** wake, attack, hurt and death per type; telegraph warnings; boss stingers.\n- **UI:** move, confirm, back, error, tab, equip, salvage.\n- **Ambience:** `audio.loop` voices for rain, fire and wind, with `spatialize` and `muffle`.\n\n### Voices: Animalese gibberish\n\nNo real speech. `src/audio/voice.js` turns each subtitle into babble:\n\n- A **syllable bank** of about 20 short `SoundDef`s per register (consonant noise layer plus two vowel-formant sines with a pitch glide): low, mid, high, demon.\n- Each letter or pair maps to a syllable by hash, so the same line always sounds the same. Punctuation makes pauses; `!` lifts pitch, `?` rises at the end.\n- **Per speaker:** register, base pitch, rate, variance. The Crier is high and fast. Dame Brasse is low, loud and clipped. Ogive is soft and slow. The Bursar is low, with `crush`. **Malison is demon register, doubled an octave down, with an echo layer.**\n- Play through `ctx.audio.play(def, { pitch, volume, pan })`, scaling by your Voices setting (the engine has only master, sfx and music channels). Heroes get short grunts and class barks (\"not enough Clangor\").\n\n---\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n### The couch (the game on its own)\n\nOpened directly, with no hub, the game is a complete solo game with **drop-in couch co-op for up to 4 on one screen**. That's what \"the game on its own\" means here: the TV comes with one screen and up to four pads, and needs no server.\n\n- **Seats:** the keyboard and mouse or the first pad to press is seat 1. In play, any unassigned pad pressing Options, or Party in the pause menu, joins: pick a class, get a guest hero at the party's level, saved per class so it keeps its loot. Holding Options on a pad in the Party menu leaves.\n- **Input:** `src/input/pads.js` polls each pad (section 2 item 25) and forwards state through `ctx.input.send` so engine replays stay valid.\n- **One camera:** target the centre of the seats, and zoom out as far as `setZoom(0.62)` to fit them all. A hero off screen for 2 s teleports to seat 1.\n- **Menus:** any seat can open its Hero screen; the world pauses, the panel is framed in that seat's colour, and only that seat controls it.\n- **Loot** is per seat, with item labels coloured by owner.\n\n### Hub sessions\n\nThe hub loads the game with `AIHub.active` true. Follow its `README.md` exactly. Mode: **`shared-world`**.\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Fill the Knell, then slay its Warden together\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick or WASD. Attack: Cross or click. Skills: face buttons or 1-4.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\n**Flow:** at load, `if (AIHub.active)` go straight to the session flow: no title, menus, attract or saves. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, run the normal game. Build the round from `info.seed` (the same map on every copy), start the engine (`Engine.headless` if `info.server`), then `AIHub.ready()` with no key press. If the engine can't start, `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n\n**The card (game-owned):** three heroes in a torchlit room, plus the title, the players in their colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in the current glyphs, seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross or a click on Ready calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle, M or a click calls `AIHub.answer('more')`. No choices, no menus. `AIHub.rng('card')` for anything random.\n\n**The round:**\n- A special Knell Run, one floor of 18 rooms, sized so it takes 5 to 6 minutes to fill the meter and 90 seconds for the Warden. HP scales with players.\n- Heroes start at level 10 with all 6 slots filled from a class preset and a plain gear set. Class comes from seat (seat 0 Bellwarden, 1 Lamplighter, 2 Sexton, 3 Bellwarden). In the first room, standing on another class's font for 2 s swaps your class until play has run for 30 s.\n- Level-ups pop a small \"pick 1 of 3\" (a Tone, a Vow or a stat), on d-pad left, up or right, Z, X or C, or a click; it auto-picks after 10 s.\n- Loot works as normal, with one-button equip. The Hero screen opens over the running world.\n- Death: rise after 8 s, or an ally revives you.\n- Play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`; show the countdown. Before that the sim doesn't step.\n\n**The end:** Warden dead: host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won: true, stats, awards })`. On `time-up`: host calls it at once with `won: false`. `standings` lists every remaining player, best first, ties grouped, sorted by `score = damage/100 + 50×revives + 20×eliteKills − 30×deaths`. Awards: Bell-Ringer (damage), Undertaker (kills), Good Samaritan (revives), Collector (gold), Regular Customer (deaths). On `end`, for any reason: stop input, sim, sending, music and loops.\n\n**Other rules:** on `leave`, fade that hero out and carry on. Network only through `AIHub`. No chat, emotes or custom names. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, new tabs or navigation. No Quit. Names are drawn on the HUD canvas, never as HTML. `Create + Options` belongs to the hub.\n\n### Netcode\n\n**The host's sim is the only truth.** Clients generate the same map from the seed, run the same view code against a mirror of the world, and send only intent.\n\n| Message | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Contents |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `i` | client to host | no | 10 Hz, always, even idle | Move, aim, held buttons, seq |\n| `c` | client to host | yes | On change | Presses and commands: cast, dodge, interact, equip, salvage. Queue and retry if `send` returns false |\n| `s` | host to all | no | 10 Hz | Flat integer arrays: heroes `[id,x,z,facing,anim,hp,res,flags]`, monsters `[id,x,z,facing,hp]`. Positions × 10 |\n| `e` | host to all | yes | 5 Hz batches | Events: spawn, hit, death, cast, drop, status, banner, subtitle, meter |\n\n**Budgets, from the protocol:** at most 20 messages a second per copy; 16 KB per message; unreliable over about 1,200 bytes is lost whole if any packet is. So keep `s` under 1,100 bytes of JSON: the 24 monsters nearest any hero every time, plus a rotating slice of the rest within 40 m. Cap `e` at 12 KB and carry the rest to the next batch.\n\n**Clients:** interpolate others 120 ms behind. Predict the local hero with the same movement code and the same grid; correct smoothly past 1 m of error. Play cast clips at once; numbers and deaths come from the host. Effects, ragdolls and chunks are local, from events.\n\n**Server copies** (`AIHub.server`): run sim and net only; skip the view. `AIHub.me` isn't in the players; no local seat.\n\n**Hitstop and slow motion:** never on the host. Clients may do purely visual freezes (pausing a mixer for 3 frames).\n\n---\n","numLines":273,"startLine":571,"totalLines":1084}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Vi1WpuRqjAy9qhhhFwyg2J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
