{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCb8EJhjfQJjGnUSfRC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` now covers everything in `TASK.md`, and this time I checked it instead of just saying so. The hook was right that my earlier claim was unchecked, and the check found real gaps, which are now fixed.\n\n## How I checked\n- **Line-by-line audit:** a script mapped all 110 non-blank `TASK.md` lines to specific text in `PLAN.md`, and none are unmapped. It looks for key phrases, so it can't judge quality; I also re-read the whole plan myself.\n- **Audit results:** 55 of 56 rows passed first time. The one failure and one failed side check were errors in my search patterns, and both pass now they're corrected.\n- **`STAGE.md` rules:** the plan contains no `TASK.md` file or folder names. `planner-exit-interview.json` has `STAGE.md`'s four questions, exactly and in order.\n- **Internal references:** every section and item number the plan cites exists.\n\n## What I fixed\n- **Spelled out instead of only pointed at:** all 14 Source Information fields with what to write for each, all 14 feedback questions, the full exit interview shape, and the contents of the About screen.\n- **Missing rules added:** the title method, the \"polished vertical slice\" bar, the `pkill` and `playwright install` rules, and where to fetch the hub files.\n- **Features a player might never see:**\n  - Devotion needs level 30, but the story ends around level 20, so The Last Bell start now gives a level 30 hero with Devotion points, a Grand Key and a set bonus.\n  - The first Collection Plate and first shrine are now scripted rather than left to chance.\n  - A new 15-row table says where each feature first appears, and the playthrough tests must confirm it.\n- **Bugs:**\n  - Session heroes started at level 10 with six slots, but the sixth opens at level 12, so they now start at 12.\n  - \"Requiem\" and \"Penance\" each named two different things, so I renamed the Tone and the Vow.\n- **New tests in the plan:**\n  - The engine and hub client files must match the downloads byte for byte.\n  - The exit interview's shape is checked.\n  - All About screen text must actually appear on screen.\n- **Coverage table:** it now follows `TASK.md`'s order and says how each item gets proved.\n\n## Where I disagree with the hook\n- **`planner-exit-interview.json` stays as it is:** `STAGE.md` asks for that exact file and shape. The builder's exit interview describes a finished game, so writing one now would mean making it up. The plan gives builders its shape instead, without naming the file, as `STAGE.md` requires.\n- **The plan still mentions `TASK.md` items like the exit interview and About screen:** the goal is coverage of everything `TASK.md` asks for, and `STAGE.md` only rules out file and folder names.\n\nAs before, nobody has built the game from this plan, so its balance numbers and content are untested starting points. The folder now holds only `PLAN.md`, `planner-exit-interview.json` and the original `STAGE.md` and `TASK.md`, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2186,"cache_read_input_tokens":529466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2186},"output_tokens":702,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"ec7882ad-9a43-454b-985e-d87cb60094f0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:06:58.027Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCb7syUh6PRWLXxAWm8"}
