{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":366,"estimated_tokens_delta":277,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"cf79dad1-5468-4efa-a364-0227fa6faab2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCzY69FfTCpK8KdcCPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The check turned up real problems the keyword matching would have missed: `Rng.fork` depends on the parent's current state, the `−3%` sign isn't in the HUD font, the 52-character line limit was wrong, and the plan left out shadows, the world and characters, and tablets with `page.touchscreen`. I'm fixing all of these now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4665,"cache_read_input_tokens":567170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4665},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"759639ee-90dc-47e9-bc13-c8a99176a6f3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:12:40.030Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCzXk48LMsSyLqn1bgN","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCzY69FfTCpK8KdcCPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014F2KwB1198LfhBqED8WRa5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns = open('PLAN.md', encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == 1, (n, old[:90])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# World, characters and themes, not only mechanics (TASK.md's Scope asks for all of them).\nrep(\"\"\"| What the source does well | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| Hordes that explode, physical destruction |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"TASK.md asks you to capture what makes the source distinctive, its world, characters, themes and tone, and turn it into mechanics, pacing and UX. So the first rows are the feel of the thing, made ours.\n\n| What the source does well | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| A gothic land where hell climbs up through its graveyards, and a doomed town holding out | **Vespermoor** and **Tollhaven** |\n| A hero who is more than mortal | **The Late**: dead, up again, and still themselves |\n| A grim old keeper of lore who reads you the history | **Crier Maudlin**, a severed head who never stopped working |\n| Themes of apocalypse, failing faith and old sins coming due | A cracked holy bell, a wronged saint, a bishop in debt |\n| Hordes that explode, physical destruction |\"\"\")\nrep(\"| A villain who taunts you while you play | **Malison**, in subtitled gibberish |\",\n    \"| Scheming lords of the pit who taunt you while you play | **The Bursar** and **Malison**, in subtitled gibberish |\")\n\n# Section 2: what the substance check proved.\nrep(\"`hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. (Ragdolls were only tried in the browser.) `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys KeyD*30` plays and replays to the same fingerprint.\",\n    \"`hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys KeyD*30` plays and replays to the same fingerprint. Replays still match with ragdolls and flying chunks in play.\")\nrep(\"\"\"`plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\n\"\"\", \"\"\"`plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\n\n**Randomness**\n31. **(verified) `Rng.fork` depends on the parent's current state,** whatever the docs' comment suggests: once the parent has drawn a number, the same `fork('zone:1')` gives different numbers. So keep one root `new Rng(seed)` per world that only forks and never draws. Forks from that root are stable, whatever their children draw. Every session client relies on this to build the same map.\n\n**Also run under `Engine.headless` and working (verified):** `Breakables` (`add`, then `break`); `Timeline` (cues, `line()`, `bars()`, `skip()`); `NavGrid` (`flowTo`, `flowDirection`, `path`, `lineOfSight`, `setOpen`); `LegStepper` with `twoBoneIK`; `SpringChain`; `Squash`; `Decals`; `Trail`; `Precipitation`; `WaterSurface`; `groundFog`; `{ dissolve: true }` clones; `glowMaterial` swaps; `mergeStaticMeshes` with a tinted `textureMap`; `disposeObject` on a zone root; `camera.rayAt` onto the ground; `lights.request` with `lifetime` and `priority`; `screen.cover`, `reveal`, `shockwave` and `flash`; `input.send` reaching `input.commands`; `audio.loop` with `spatialize`; the bell as sine `layers` (peak 0.84 from `renderSound`); `parseSong` on the Clemency motif. These ran without error; how they look is yours to check.\n\"\"\")\n\n# Section 3: the line limit that my own samples broke.\nrep(\"Lines fit two rows of about 52 characters. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24).\",\n    \"Subtitles fit two rows of about 60 characters, which every line below does. Lore books get a paged screen instead. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24).\")\n\n# Section 8: shadows (TASK.md's Performance names them), and the exact part forms.\nrep(\"Tag every actor with `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`.\\n\",\n    \"Tag every actor with `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`. **Everything casts and receives shadows:** set `castShadow` and `receiveShadow` on meshes (traverse built models to be sure), and give actors a `ContactShadow` too.\\n\")\nrep(\"Old Clemency (`lathe`, 5 m, cracked, tolls with a swing).\",\n    \"Old Clemency (`lathe`, 5 m, cracked, tolls with a swing). **(verified)** The forms that pass `checkModel` are `{ lathe: [[radius, height], ...], at, c }` and `{ tube: [[x, y, z], ...], r, at, c }`.\")\n\n# Section 10: a character the font doesn't have.\nrep(\"two big numbers (DAMAGE +12%, TOUGHNESS −3%)\", \"two big numbers (DAMAGE +12%, TOUGHNESS -3%)\")\n\n# Section 14: the Rng rule and shadows.\nrep(\"- All sim randomness from `Rng` forks: `rng.fork('zone:' + id)`, `rng.fork('loot')`. Sessions seed from `info.seed`.\",\n    \"- All sim randomness comes from forks of one root that never draws (section 2, item 31): `root.fork('zone:' + id)`, `root.fork('loot')`. Sessions seed the root from `info.seed`.\")\nrep(\"so don't optimise: `quality: 'high'` (16 lights), as many monsters, particles and lights as a scene wants, 150+ on screen at peak.\",\n    \"and FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope, so don't optimise: `quality: 'high'` (16 lights and the largest shadow map), as much detail and as many monsters, effects, lights and shadows as a scene wants, 150+ monsters on screen at peak.\")\n\n# Section 16: phone and tablet, real taps, and a test for the Rng rule.\nrep(\"- **Touch:** Chromium's Pixel 7 profile: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. Tap doesn't start a game.\",\n    \"- **Touch:** Chromium with a phone profile (Pixel 7) and a tablet profile, tapping with `page.touchscreen`: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. A tap doesn't start a game.\")\nrep(\"- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone.\\n\",\n    \"- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone. The same seed builds an identical map no matter what other streams have drawn (section 2, item 31).\\n\")\nopen('PLAN.md', 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('edited')\nPY\nsed -i 's/const r = new E.Rng(7); const a = r.fork(.zone:1.).next(); r.next(); const b = r.fork(.zone:1.).next(); if (a !== b) throw new Error(.fork.);/const r = new E.Rng(7); const a = r.fork(\"zone:1\").next(); const kid = r.fork(\"zone:1\"); kid.next(); kid.next(); const b = r.fork(\"zone:1\").next(); if (a !== b) throw new Error(\"fork\");/' .audit/scripts/probe.mjs\nsed -i \"s/'Rng forks stay independent; hud on a small art size; clearQueued, preventKeys'/'Rng: forks of a root that never draws stay stable; hud size; clearQueued, preventKeys'/\" .audit/scripts/probe.mjs\ngrep -c \"root that never draws stay stable\" .audit/scripts/probe.mjs","description":"Fix what the substance check found and correct the probe's Rng step"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4665,"cache_read_input_tokens":567170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4665},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dbc4055-18d5-4f5b-aa46-86fd0623cd25","uuid":"b6b35bab-72a6-4957-aa3e-feb093d85a26","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:00.370Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCzXk48LMsSyLqn1bgN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014F2KwB1198LfhBqED8WRa5":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211944__x51597c/work\npython3 - <<'PY'\ns = open('PLAN.md', encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == 1, (n, old[:90])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# World, characters and themes, not only mechanics (TASK.md's Scope asks for all of them).\nrep(\"\"\"| What the source does well | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| Hordes that explode, physical destruction |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"TASK.md asks you to capture what makes the source distinctive, its world, characters, themes and tone, and turn it into mechanics, pacing and UX. So the first rows are the feel of the thing, made ours.\n\n| What the source does well | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| A gothic land where hell climbs up through its graveyards, and a doomed town holding out | **Vespermoor** and **Tollhaven** |\n| A hero who is more than mortal | **The Late**: dead, up again, and still themselves |\n| A grim old keeper of lore who reads you the history | **Crier Maudlin**, a severed head who never stopped working |\n| Themes of apocalypse, failing faith and old sins coming due | A cracked holy bell, a wronged saint, a bishop in debt |\n| Hordes that explode, physical destruction |\"\"\")\nrep(\"| A villain who taunts you while you play | **Malison**, in subtitled gibberish |\",\n    \"| Scheming lords of the pit who taunt you while you play | **The Bursar** and **Malison**, in subtitled gibberish |\")\n\n# Section 2: what the substance check proved.\nrep(\"`hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. (Ragdolls were only tried in the browser.) `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys KeyD*30` plays and replays to the same fingerprint.\",\n    \"`hud.width` is 480 and `hud.canvas` is null there. `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys KeyD*30` plays and replays to the same fingerprint. Replays still match with ragdolls and flying chunks in play.\")\nrep(\"\"\"`plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\n\"\"\", \"\"\"`plum` at 0.4 to 0.9 m sits right.\n\n**Randomness**\n31. **(verified) `Rng.fork` depends on the parent's current state,** whatever the docs' comment suggests: once the parent has drawn a number, the same `fork('zone:1')` gives different numbers. So keep one root `new Rng(seed)` per world that only forks and never draws. Forks from that root are stable, whatever their children draw. Every session client relies on this to build the same map.\n\n**Also run under `Engine.headless` and working (verified):** `Breakables` (`add`, then `break`); `Timeline` (cues, `line()`, `bars()`, `skip()`); `NavGrid` (`flowTo`, `flowDirection`, `path`, `lineOfSight`, `setOpen`); `LegStepper` with `twoBoneIK`; `SpringChain`; `Squash`; `Decals`; `Trail`; `Precipitation`; `WaterSurface`; `groundFog`; `{ dissolve: true }` clones; `glowMaterial` swaps; `mergeStaticMeshes` with a tinted `textureMap`; `disposeObject` on a zone root; `camera.rayAt` onto the ground; `lights.request` with `lifetime` and `priority`; `screen.cover`, `reveal`, `shockwave` and `flash`; `input.send` reaching `input.commands`; `audio.loop` with `spatialize`; the bell as sine `layers` (peak 0.84 from `renderSound`); `parseSong` on the Clemency motif. These ran without error; how they look is yours to check.\n\"\"\")\n\n# Section 3: the line limit that my own samples broke.\nrep(\"Lines fit two rows of about 52 characters. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24).\",\n    \"Subtitles fit two rows of about 60 characters, which every line below does. Lore books get a paged screen instead. Punctuation stays inside the HUD font (section 2, item 24).\")\n\n# Section 8: shadows (TASK.md's Performance names them), and the exact part forms.\nrep(\"Tag every actor with `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`.\\n\",\n    \"Tag every actor with `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`. **Everything casts and receives shadows:** set `castShadow` and `receiveShadow` on meshes (traverse built models to be sure), and give actors a `ContactShadow` too.\\n\")\nrep(\"Old Clemency (`lathe`, 5 m, cracked, tolls with a swing).\",\n    \"Old Clemency (`lathe`, 5 m, cracked, tolls with a swing). **(verified)** The forms that pass `checkModel` are `{ lathe: [[radius, height], ...], at, c }` and `{ tube: [[x, y, z], ...], r, at, c }`.\")\n\n# Section 10: a character the font doesn't have.\nrep(\"two big numbers (DAMAGE +12%, TOUGHNESS −3%)\", \"two big numbers (DAMAGE +12%, TOUGHNESS -3%)\")\n\n# Section 14: the Rng rule and shadows.\nrep(\"- All sim randomness from `Rng` forks: `rng.fork('zone:' + id)`, `rng.fork('loot')`. Sessions seed from `info.seed`.\",\n    \"- All sim randomness comes from forks of one root that never draws (section 2, item 31): `root.fork('zone:' + id)`, `root.fork('loot')`. Sessions seed the root from `info.seed`.\")\nrep(\"so don't optimise: `quality: 'high'` (16 lights), as many monsters, particles and lights as a scene wants, 150+ on screen at peak.\",\n    \"and FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope, so don't optimise: `quality: 'high'` (16 lights and the largest shadow map), as much detail and as many monsters, effects, lights and shadows as a scene wants, 150+ monsters on screen at peak.\")\n\n# Section 16: phone and tablet, real taps, and a test for the Rng rule.\nrep(\"- **Touch:** Chromium's Pixel 7 profile: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. Tap doesn't start a game.\",\n    \"- **Touch:** Chromium with a phone profile (Pixel 7) and a tablet profile, tapping with `page.touchscreen`: message present and wrapped, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract running. A tap doesn't start a game.\")\nrep(\"- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone.\\n\",\n    \"- Zones: `nav.path(entrance, exit)` for 200 seeds per zone. The same seed builds an identical map no matter what other streams have drawn (section 2, item 31).\\n\")\nopen('PLAN.md', 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('edited')\nPY\nsed -i 's/const r = new E.Rng(7); const a = r.fork(.zone:1.).next(); r.next(); const b = r.fork(.zone:1.).next(); if (a !== b) throw new Error(.fork.);/const r = new E.Rng(7); const a = r.fork(\"zone:1\").next(); const kid = r.fork(\"zone:1\"); kid.next(); kid.next(); const b = r.fork(\"zone:1\").next(); if (a !== b) throw new Error(\"fork\");/' .audit/scripts/probe.mjs\nsed -i \"s/'Rng forks stay independent; hud on a small art size; clearQueued, preventKeys'/'Rng: forks of a root that never draws stay stable; hud size; clearQueued, preventKeys'/\" .audit/scripts/probe.mjs\ngrep -c \"root that never draws stay stable\" .audit/scripts/probe.mjs","description":"Fix what the substance check found and correct the probe's Rng step"}}}
