n   -> Phone and tablet profiles.\nL54      Stand-in: listener\n   plan 1077: Sound, by what Web Audio produces:** the engine doesn't expose its output node, so wrap `AudioNode.prototype.connect` in `addInitScript` to also feed anything connec...\n   -> Analyser tap on real output, plus renderSound.\nL55      Stand-in: second player\n   plan 1091: Then a **game-level** check: two frames, drive P2 by synthetic keys inside its frame, and read `frame.contentWindow.__GAME__` to see P2's hero move in P1's world and...\n   -> Beyond the protocol: asserts P2 moves in P1's world.\nL56      Stand-in: iPhone\n   plan 133: WebKit here has no WebGPU, so test touch in Chromium.\n   -> Honest limit noted.\nL57      Stand-in: TV\n   plan 1079: Screenshots** for your own eyes (`tools/shots.mjs`, at 1920×1080): title, attract, combat with 40+ monsters, each zone, each class casting, Gear, Skills, each vendor...\n   -> 10-foot view judged at that size.\nL61-64   Sharing rules\n   plan 17: Stay out of the folders beside yours.\n   -> Restated with the one correction to TASK.md's flags.\nL72      Show ALL features\n   plan 251: TASK.md wants every feature shown, so none of them is left to luck.\n   -> Table of 15 rows; tests assert each. Devotion hole fixed via The Last Bell.\nL72      Player understands what they can and can't do\n   plan 593: Codex:** lore books, bestiary (unlocks on first kill), and **How to Play** in six big pages (Moving and fighting, Skills and Tones, Loot, Town, Knell Runs, Co-op), s...\n   -> Plus contextual tutorial prompts.\nL72      Polished vertical slice\n   plan 26: The bar:** a feature-complete demo, treated as a complete, polished vertical slice, long enough to show every feature and mechanic so a player understands how the ga...\n   -> The stated bar, with a feel recipe.\nL72      Infrastructure for designer tools\n   plan 1011: So the rest of the game can be built later: all content is plain tables in `src/data`, rooms are ASCII, models are `ModelDef`s (`node check.mjs --sheets`), songs are...\n   -> All content is data, with a recipe page.\nL74      Dev mode from the pause menu\n   plan 905: Pause menu → Dev Mode.** Not in sessions.\n   -> Pause screen lists it; pad-navigable.\nL74      Standard testing tools\n   plan 910: Spawn:* any monster, any elite with chosen Afflictions, any boss, Collection Plate, Unquiet Coffin, kill all.\n   -> Seven groups of tools.\nL74      Live sliders\n   plan 918: Monster HP, Monster damage, Monster density, Elite frequency, Player damage, Player life, Player speed, Cooldown scale, Resource regen, XP rate, Gold rate, Legendary...\n   -> 18 named; the sim reads them live.\nL74      Reset to defaults\n   plan 916: Live sliders** (from `src/data/tuning.js`; each with its default shown and a **Reset to defaults** button):\n   -> Test confirms it restores.\nL76      Attract after 10 s idle on title or menu\n   plan 889: After **10 seconds with no input on the title or main menu**, start a looping AI-played tour.\n   -> Both screens; tested by stepping 600 frames.\nL76      Loops, may cheat\n   plan 891: It runs a real world with real bots using `src/sim/bot.js`, cheating freely (invulnerable, level 25, full bars, good gear, no cooldown limits, reduced monster HP).\n   -> Scripted tour of 7 stops covering every zone and class.\nL76      Any input exits\n   plan 889: Any input** (key, click, pointer move over 2 px, pad button or stick past deadzone) exits straight back to where it was.\n   -> Defines input for each device.\nL80      Writing style like the source's\n   plan 187: High gothic proclamation:** narration, lore books, Malison.\n   -> Three registers and 32 sample lines to write from.\nL83      Designed for a DualSense or standard pad\n   plan 694: Skills 3, 4 | Triangle (3), Circle (1) | 1, 2\n   -> Full button map with standard-mapping indices.\nL83      TV at 10 feet\n   plan 679: Body text is scale 1 (7 art pixels, about 28 px at 1080p), headings scale 2.\n   -> Sizes, safe zone, checked by 1080p shots.\nL83      Same game, same screens\n   plan 678: All UI is drawn with `ctx.hud`, in art pixels, the same screens for pad and mouse.\n   -> Single UI layer.\nL83      Keyboard and mouse feel native\n   plan 302: Left click on a monster walks into range and attacks; on an NPC or object, walks and uses it; on the ground, moves (hold to keep steering).\n   -> Click-to-move, hold to steer, shift-click: real genre behaviour, not stand-ins.\nL83      Keys PC players expect\n   plan 699: Hero screen | Create (8), on release | I or C (gear), K (skills), L (quests)\n   -> Full key table.\nL83      Hover moves focus\n   plan 681: Mouse hover moves focus when the pointer moved**; click activates.\n   -> Tested with page.mouse.move.\nL83      Prompts follow last input\n   plan 712: `src/ui/glyphs.js`: `lastDevice` flips to `pad` on any pad button or stick past the deadzone, and to `kbm` on any key, click or pointer move over 2 px.\n   -> Defined and used everywhere; tested.\nL83      PlayStation glyphs by default\n   plan 714: PlayStation (default):** 11×11 sprites: Cross `sky`, Circle `red`, Square `plum`, Triangle `lime`, L1, R1, L2, R2, Options, Create, d-pad directions, sticks.\n   -> Sprite list given.\nL83      Xbox glyphs in Settings\n   plan 715: Xbox (Settings option):** A `lime`, B `red`, X `sky`, Y `sand`, LB, RB, LT, RT, Menu, View.\n   -> Also on the Settings screen list.\nL83      Keys and mouse buttons\n   plan 716: Keyboard and mouse:** keycaps drawn from a rectangle plus letter; left and right mouse sprites.\n   -> Drawn from data.\nL85      No dense, web-style screens\n   plan 678: No dense screens:** one job per screen, big icons, short lists, a maximum of 6 lines on an item card.\n   -> Limits stated: item card at 6 lines.\nL87      Touch: no touch controls\n   plan 936: No on-screen controls.\n   -> `touch: false`, verified.\nL87      Touch: the message\n   plan 936: Show the attract mode with \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" wrapped to `hud.width` (a portrait phone fits about 22 characters a line) and the engine's ⚙.\n   -> Wraps on a narrow phone, a real case found here.\nL87      Touch: settings button\n   plan 152: Add `settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }` to that **(verified: `false` removes the button)**. Your own Settings screen replaces the ⚙ everywhere ex...\n   -> Verified both ways.\nL87      Touch: attract runs\n   plan 901: On a touch-only device it runs too.\n   -> Tested on phone and tablet profiles.\nL90      No TODOs or stubs\n   plan 18: No stubs.** If you run out of budget, cut whole features in the order given in section 15, never halfway.\n   -> Plus lint and a cut-whole-features rule.\nL93      On About/Credits\n   plan 924: TASK.md marks this as critical, and these are its contents:\n   -> Pages listed; test reads them back.\nL93      In the chat reply\n   plan 24: Your final chat reply,** carrying Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n   -> In the hand-back list and done list.\nL93      unknown when unsure\n   plan 926: Write `unknown` for anything you can't confirm.\n   -> Stated twice.\nL94-106  All Source Information fields\n   plan 926: Source Information,** one labelled line each, in this order: Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Resea...\n   -> 14 labels in TASK.md's order, each with what to write.\nL107     Usage\n   plan 926: Usage reads exactly `added on import`, as a plain string in the bundle, because the agent that imports the game replaces it with the real cost, tokens and time.\n   -> Keeps it findable, says never to estimate.\nL109-128 Exit interview shape\n   plan 1138: This block is copied word for word from TASK.md; the strings in it say what goes in each value:\n   -> Byte-identical, checked by audit.\nL130-151 All feedback questions\n   plan 1180: Answer each of these, in this order.** They're word for word from TASK.md.\n   -> 14 questions, checked by audit.\nL132     Honest issue counts\n   plan 1205: Keep the numbers honest.** From M0 on, add one line to `tests/ISSUES.md` for each issue a test catches, marked critical or not, and note anything the engine made you...\n   -> Otherwise the count would be a guess.\n\nrequirements reviewed: 78, without plan text: 0\n\nPLAN.md after:  ac9bac417d6ad1dd  unchanged: yes","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ATpZevUbxZGJXMPr9EEeje","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
